    <node id="&quot;BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bees are the central animals in the text, described as part of a superorganism (the colony) that humans can develop a personal, emotional, and respectful relationship with."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees are the insects that form colonies and undergo the swarming process to perpetuate their species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees are the primary biological entities discussed, comprising colonies with workers, drones, and a queen, which the beekeeper must manage and house."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees are the primary biological entities in the text, forming a colony and cluster to survive winter by consuming honey and pollen stores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cold-blooded insects that form clusters to generate and conserve heat through shivering their flight muscles to survive winter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects that are the focus of the beekeeping activities described, requiring specific feeding and care during winter and spring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insects that live in hives, produce wax and honey, and exhibit clustering behavior for warmth during winter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social insects that live in colonies, store honey, and use stinging as a defensive mechanism to protect their home and wealth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insects within the hive whose activities, growth, and health are being monitored by the beekeeper."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d689db19e9533ba99ddacc008292886b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1583}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2068}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A person experienced in the practice of apiculture who manages honeybee colonies and can provide guidance on handling bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A person who manages and cares for bees, utilizing tools like smokers and veils to handle them safely."&lt;SEP&gt;"A person who manages and monitors bee colonies to ensure their health and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A person who manages and studies bees, whose success depends on understanding bee behavior and stimuli."&lt;SEP&gt;"A person who manages bee colonies and benefits from the efficiency of the bees' dance language and pollination process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A person who manages bees and typically develops a physical and psychological tolerance to bee stings through regular exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who manages bee colonies, controls their diet, and may collect or provide pollen supplements."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who manages honey bee colonies and implements strategies to protect hives from pests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper is an individual responsible for monitoring weather patterns, checking hive conditions, and providing supplemental feeding to ensure the colony's survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper is the individual responsible for managing, monitoring, and assisting the bee colony to ensure its survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"The human individual who manages bee hives, whose behavior and chemistry significantly influence the reactions of the bees."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f4bb80b935e118383082352a101ac3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1585}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2070}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEE STING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A defensive action by a bee that involves piercing a subject with a stinger, potentially causing reactions ranging from minor pain to anaphylactic shock."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1584}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAPHYLACTIC SHOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A severe, life-threatening systemic allergic reaction characterized by nausea, body rash, difficulty breathing, and dizziness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1584}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STING KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical kit prescribed by a physician to be carried by individuals allergic to bee stings for emergency treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1584}]</data>
