    <node id="&quot;DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A government agency that provides threshold requirements and guidance for agricultural products."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state or federal government department responsible for policies and support related to farming and food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state-level government agency providing legal information, offices, and grants to aid farms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state-level government body recommended for consultation regarding the selection of trees for windbreaks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Department of Agriculture is a US federal agency created in 1862 to support agricultural interests and research."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Department of Agriculture is the government body responsible for overseeing agricultural services and providing advisors for farming surveys."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state Department of Agriculture is a government entity that provides advertising opportunities and agricultural oversight."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state's department of agriculture is an official agency that serves as a source of information on beekeeping laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state-level agency responsible for agricultural rules, regulations, and providing information on value-added programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state-level government agency that maintains lists of farmers' markets and regulates agricultural activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ca358634d91f845f6dd19689edaf7b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63283b5b0d7af44d93e355da3bac994e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a748f8974ea30d2229e5c6357765d4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df7ec17c31731168941c83b97fd64a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f78f364d74eca8b91a5a10f5f9de4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c07830327394a77dc9e8ac1a53acd63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778a8623cc35798aa1ed41ffa090e9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25521141823b7becef820b71d7dbda0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5deb38ed9dc0a60bcac768fbb7955c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a603ecfe84d863d026d6d7309cc4add3</data>
