    <node id="&quot;LORENZO L. LANGSTROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Reverend Lorenzo L. Langstroth is the discoverer of 'bee space' and is known as the father of modern beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1574}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A conventional vertical beehive design that mimics the shape of a standing hollow tree, utilizing frames and specific 'bee space' dimensions for standardized honey production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A rectangular hive with suspended movable frames that allows beekeepers to examine combs and harvest honey without destroying the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"A revolutionary beehive design patented in 1852 that utilized movable frames, sparking the commercialization of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific design of beehive that uses movable frames to hold honey and brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of beehive design characterized by movable frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of beehive design that changed how beekeepers extracted honey and selected for bee productivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A standard type of beehive characterized by specific dimensions and the use of frames and foundation, often requiring more precise construction than a TBH."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of beehive utilizing removable frames, developed by Lorenzo L. Langstroth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A vertical hive design using standardized movable frames, widely used in commercial beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"An invention that revolutionized beekeeping, making it possible to earn a living from the practice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Langstroth hive is a beekeeping system based on the discovery of bee space, utilizing specific dimensions and movable frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Langstroth hive is a specific type of beehive design that has become the industry standard for beekeepers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Langstroth hive is a standardized beehive design using frames that allow for easier movement of combs and is widely used by commercial beekeepers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84b0074137dce67380e1f3b23f86de2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9b2fa060b49dfcd9523440966c974ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e06b0074dff6e9083043d922831e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6278bcba2e2dfe6f1202b147f87019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0984220078ce71973ba3b0fa10b37a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-141bd4f59be1ccee796abafaf0658f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13bef129d93b5a27e008dbee0931310</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1572}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bee space is a conceptual discovery regarding the specific width of space that bees leave open for passage, which revolutionized hive design."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific gap distance (approximately 6-9mm) that bees naturally leave between combs, which beekeepers utilize to design hive components."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific gap of three-eighths of an inch that bees leave for maneuvering, which Langstroth used to design his movable frame hive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1574}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMOVABLE FRAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Removable frames are a piece of beekeeping equipment that allows for the extraction of honey and hive manipulation without destroying the colony."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1574}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEESWAX FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beeswax foundation is a material used in hives to allow wax to be renewed periodically on frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax foundation is a pre-formed sheet of wax provided in hive frames to guide bees in building straight honeycomb."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sheets or strips of wax used in hives to guide bees in building cells of a specific size and shape."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1572}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A device used to rotate honey combs at varying speeds to fling honey out of the frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"A device using centrifugal force to extract honey from combs without destroying them."&lt;SEP&gt;"A device, often a centrifuge, used by beekeepers to extract honey from combs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The honey extractor is a device used to remove honey from movable, renewable frames."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bfa52bca196a2a92c24daffb2347956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1574}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN EXCLUDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A device that prevents the queen from moving between hive sections to stop her from laying eggs in honey supers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A device used in a beehive to restrict the movement of the queen and drones."&lt;SEP&gt;"A device used in beehives to prevent the queen from entering the honey supers while allowing worker bees to pass."&lt;SEP&gt;"A device used in hive management to prevent the queen bee from entering honey supers; also referred to as a honey excluder."&lt;SEP&gt;"A grid-like device that allows worker bees to pass but prevents the queen bee from entering specific parts of the hive, such as honey supers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A queen excluder is a device used in beekeeping to prevent the queen bee from passing through to certain areas of the hive, aiding in her location or the separation of brood and honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen excluder is a device that prevents the queen bee from laying eggs in the honey supers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9654edf0284987ba4f0c8bde4acffe9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edb74059818291619d1eccac02bb8df4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6550c1217ac242a6cb1c3d9a5de5ee35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91fddbed5da654e2156cc50a2222b4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85263881590bbad34c8bcb9551c9a883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 415}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1590}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2079}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LANGSTROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historical beekeeper and writer who observed the behavior of bees attracted to the sweets of a candy shop."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical figure and apiarist who developed formulas for bee-yard success and wrote about the factors affecting honey secretion."&lt;SEP&gt;"An author or expert on beekeeping who provided guidance on the gentle handling of bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who wrote about the difficulty of reasoning with practical beekeepers who dismiss 'book knowledge'."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual, likely a beekeeper or apiologist, who wrote about the preferences of bees and the quality of red raspberry honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inventor and beekeeper who patented the Langstroth hive in 1852, though he struggled financially and mentally to enforce his patents."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inventor who developed the movable frame hive based on the concept of 'bee space' to improve beekeeping productivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is a beekeeping expert whose writings describe the behavior of bee colonies, the necessity of the queen, and the dangers of close breeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is a figure who wrote about the domestication of honey bees and documented various remedies for bee stings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is a historical figure in beekeeping who documented deserted hives and honey stores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is a historical figure in beekeeping whose writings on the importance of feeding bees are cited from over 150 years ago."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is a writer or researcher quoted regarding the behavior of bees and their poison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is an individual associated with beekeeping who advocated for using cold water as the best remedy for bee stings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is an individual quoted regarding the behavior of bees and their tendency to swarm when in desperation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is mentioned as an authority on beekeeping who observed the relationship between hive construction and queen loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth is the individual whose discovery of movable, renewable frames revolutionized beekeeping and enabled the rise of commercial operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth was a beekeeper and author who developed a new hive design and wrote a treatise on bee diseases and pests in 1853."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lorenzo L. Langstroth, the inventor of the removable frame hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lorenzo Langstroth, an author and expert on bees who discussed the classification of honey and its quality over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The inventor of the modern beehive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3c9fa8be9c480f16c9786fe42c4a409a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911d39a734ce63729ca31ddecfbbdb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a1dc7299568504eb57c9d8e4201b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b198fa71b44d8dd33dcfc2eb267be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b0512dda0784c4b872422e6d8bd9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d84e8388b1b3835cf15d2729a7bded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9961d83fcb353d87b0c300b9b3408c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1f94cc5f14959e322093167c5b5ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b5f53667458d570c2b31bf11f9a153b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69a6f293580aa424d04ad67558a1427b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d8286e6a8f25ded00034a7a287f09cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6deba29b237640ada67472e874a1f037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0702b35ab5da980ccafcd8b491aa1562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6a3d7885d5c7d0196e5f8b1d626686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464158e8ae6f11d3eade0bd5a72fca55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b499dcfe1898219f12671e71bc768e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1bab4a72f46eead5c78b6d5b292d2ef</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1573}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2058}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apiculture is the industry and practice of beekeeping and managing honey bees for honey production and other benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture is the industry and practice of beekeeping, focusing on the management and breeding of honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture is the practice and study of beekeeping, encompassing the raising of bees, the production of honey and related products, and the management of bee colonies for agricultural and commercial purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture is the practice of beekeeping and the management of honey bee colonies, discussed here in terms of stewardship and interventionist vs. natural approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture is the practice of beekeeping, involving the management and study of honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture is the scientific study and practice of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apiculture, or beekeeping, is the industry of maintaining bee colonies for honey and pollination services."&lt;SEP&gt;"The agricultural practice of keeping, caring for, and managing honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry and practice of beekeeping and managing honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The practice and industry of beekeeping and managing honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The practice of beekeeping, described as a natural biological activity that affects the health of the land and its inhabitants."&lt;SEP&gt;"The practice or study of beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f592015c17fe4fa51a988e96c438765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f30f69a81886f658de51b870faedd598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b4571fdea2316371681c34c7f3af2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465116abb167ac763044821a4bc0e58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b5f53667458d570c2b31bf11f9a153b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c53fadbf74ed2ba310e067e40c2b8ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9beaf57f9c81cafddb4809192172310f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-872e529e8b629698186a747278056799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe7c71f0a95e2aad6e89fc32c4e429f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fcbe54cf1d72b0c107b42a5d283af2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbfbbce7bbb2b1195a5322a8057953dc</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1567}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historical period marked by the shift to manufactured goods and the internal combustion engine, which changed the landscape of farming and grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical period of transition to new manufacturing processes that helped construct the modern food system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical period of transition to new manufacturing processes, after which the term 'teenager' emerged and the societal contributions of that age group declined."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical period of transition to new manufacturing processes, used as a benchmark for the scale of disruption caused by Peak Oil."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical period of transition to new manufacturing processes, which the text notes coincided with the emergence of the term 'teenager' and a decline in meaningful societal contributions by that age group."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of historical economic and technological change that increased the demand for wine and growth of urban areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of major industrialization characterized by the exploitation of coal, iron, and minerals, and the use of labor-saving devices like the steam engine."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of significant technological and social change that led to the breakdown of traditional European agricultural systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution is a historical period marking the beginning of significant carbon additions to the atmosphere."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution is a historical period of development that led to a huge human population and the transfer of food from producing regions to manufacturing centres."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution is a historical period of technological transformation and the rise of early capitalism that shifted human experience away from agrarian work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution is a historical period of transition to new manufacturing processes that changed attitudes and lifestyles, hastening the evolution of beekeeping classifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution was a period of major industrialization fueled in part by the shift of peasants from rural land to cities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Industrial Revolution was a period of major industrialization in England that altered work rules, rural practices, and the concept of embeddedness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a8642109c3696b9ba422659c44934bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-591de784bfb5c3376bd8c1f7c511d0e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b806e4889dafc2c60b53b1b25c1ad3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a35a75b0bc3a557b68f4dc4d5219ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a052fbc2d60ddc1ffd04862131ebb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac6f2d596c9d9fe2bc3b9afda4f10df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b5f53667458d570c2b31bf11f9a153b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a7f4aa7178f919427c0954ff8040e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec816632b945dc5236be5a3d82d9ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e284959bc106cad9570b943c5c94ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ea25deaf7ccaf87a5c9a61060e9100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8f4ced19f39489760889dcf78f83b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be6b9145cdce9275f8166f477a4339b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4be7aab5835b5557dffc1a1c85fd336d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 836}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALIAN BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A race of honey bees known for being all-around good for beekeeping and are the most common race in the described country."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific breed of honey bees typically sold in 3-pound packages with a queen for beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific race or subspecies of honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Italian bees are a specific race or strain of honeybees considered the standard in the country due to being gentle and readily available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Italian bees are a specific type of honey bee mentioned as responding well to a powdered sugar and garlic powder mix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-218f65ec9b659cddff295e2ed6826cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b5f53667458d570c2b31bf11f9a153b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91fddbed5da654e2156cc50a2222b4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c677fc2f4fb5468d4e8323dee76a0c5a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1561}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2049}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOVABLE, RENEWABLE FRAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Movable, renewable frames are the technological innovation discovered by Langstroth that allowed for hive manipulation and the harvesting of honey without destroying colonies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b5f53667458d570c2b31bf11f9a153b</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1573}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2058}]</data>
