    <node id="&quot;APIS MELLIFERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apis mellifera is the Latin name for the honey bee, described as an industrious creature that contributes to Earth's abundance through pollination and honey production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the Western honey bee, which became a host for the Varroa mite around 1960."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the scientific name for the European honey bee, which may suffer direct detrimental effects from genetically modified plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the scientific name for the western honey bee species, characterized by its natural survival instinct to swarm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the species name for the European honey bee."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the species of honey bee that serves as a host for Varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apis mellifera is the species of honey bee whose drone brood is preferred by varroa mites for reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Western honey bee species, which beekeepers aim to help develop coexistence behaviors with mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the European honey bee, whose basic biology is essential for rearing new colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the European honey bee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the Western honey bee, characterized by its swarming behavior and colony structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the Western or European honey bee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the honey bee species to which both African and European bees belong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the honey bee, which may suffer detrimental effects from consuming GM pollen."&lt;SEP&gt;"The species of Western honey bee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The species of honey bee commonly kept by beekeepers in North and South America."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2f592015c17fe4fa51a988e96c438765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a11bfe1dc62c3ee867b5e29138914b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2691225b766f240d4e630fa426b6e435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09a1f67060248bded3f20fbcda85abc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c516e184f72cae24cee188c702d41f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e31a42be32b10fec891321276eff3bb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff2a1270133813dbf92927fcbf14a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35f6eef0d2ff08b3a3b7b2c2e942edde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8f2ee1522e3b4a6c4f7618a9db21e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad48e636e32974fc2872c98d15a0914&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4642364014d20a8527d9fb4ec06bdb04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1514064bbd0a8e145cda20ebb9ecab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bac18720725e6cd5a486707a79f3f616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
