      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A continent mentioned in the context of agricultural prevalence and topsoil loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"A continent where African bees spread and interbred with European bee races."&lt;SEP&gt;"A continent where Apis mellifera is the primary honey bee species found."&lt;SEP&gt;"A continent where the Japanese variant of the varroa mite spread in the 1970s."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region mentioned in the context of the exploitation of natural soil wealth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region where bees were found to be relatively resistant to varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region where the plantation system took on a new magnitude and aspect."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region where travelers observed Christian churches housing wood conks in glass spheres."&lt;SEP&gt;"A subtropical/tropical region where coffee and banana plants are abundant."&lt;SEP&gt;"South America is a continent mentioned as the region where a relative traveled and experienced sacred mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"South America is a continent where no-till farming practices are discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"South America is a region where approximately 42 percent of conservation agriculture farmland is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"South America is a region where conservation agriculture and no-till farming gained significant popularity, particularly in Brazil and Argentina."&lt;SEP&gt;"The continent through which Africanized bees spread northward."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mountain home and origin of the potato crop."</data>
