    <node id="&quot;ROYAL JELLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutrient-rich substance, also called bee milk, fed to larvae to develop them into queens."&lt;SEP&gt;"A secretion from glands in the heads of nurse bees used as exclusive food for young workers for the first 3 days and as the primary diet for queen larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A secretion from nurse bees, listed as one of the five frequently discussed products of the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"A secretion from worker bee glands used as brood food and sold to humans as a health supplement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Royal jelly is a specialized secretion from the glands of nurse bees used to feed larvae, particularly those destined to become queens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Royal jelly is a thick, creamy, highly nutritious substance secreted by nurse bees used to develop larvae into queens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Royal jelly, also known as bee milk, is a secretion from the glands of worker bees used to feed honey bee brood during the larval stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64bd868f29e83effc96703b72e21cc18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911d39a734ce63729ca31ddecfbbdb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218f65ec9b659cddff295e2ed6826cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c389aa55b6d5b4c773f2c917b36e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bf03b457112a6e1094db904efcfe2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b652e467f32b1db6fbb1cf5b9315586e</data>
