    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTELLIGENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Defined in the text as the ability to apply knowledge, reason, and think abstractly, which is contrasted with the ability to learn through experience."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1561}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2052}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEARNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process by which a bee's behavior can be modified by experience, such as associating food with odor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1561}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2052}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The drone is a male bee whose role in the colony's total scheme is critical, primarily involved in mating."&lt;SEP&gt;"The male honey bee, characterized by a wider body and larger eyes, lacking a stinger and not participating in hive work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The male honey bee, larger than workers but smaller than the queen, whose primary role is mating with the queen to ensure fertilization and species propagation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a44dc74bf3cf27c95be223e2ae38c2f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e80ed5175459c22df05858f37cc067</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1580}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2063}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A developed female honey bee capable of laying fertilized and unfertilized eggs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary female bee in a colony responsible for egg laying."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary female bee in a colony responsible for laying eggs; her acceptance by the colony is crucial for success."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary female bee in a colony responsible for reproduction and laying eggs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary female bee in a colony who emits a specific odor to signal her presence and governs the colony's social structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary female bee in the colony responsible for laying eggs in a pattern to expand the brood nest."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary reproductive female bee in a colony responsible for laying eggs to maintain and grow the population."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary reproductive female bee in a colony, central to the hive's survival and organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary reproductive female bee in a colony, essential for the growth and survival of the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary reproductive female in a bee colony, whose health and age significantly impact the colony's population and success."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen is the central figure of the colony responsible for egg laying and overall colony stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen is the primary reproductive female in a bee colony, responsible for laying eggs to maintain the population."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen is the reproductive female of the bee colony who leads the swarm and is responsible for egg-laying."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reproductive female bee in a colony, typically kept in a small cage during transport in a package."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reproductive female bee responsible for laying eggs in the colony."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f51ec44f0c17ad5253b21395cf12591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651bdc43ce4f434b1e5c689b3528db55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9654edf0284987ba4f0c8bde4acffe9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b481828497c05f9df552dd81b644f543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85263881590bbad34c8bcb9551c9a883</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 415}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1590}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2079}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROOD NEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The area within the hive where the queen lays eggs and the larvae develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The heart of the hive where young bees emerge and where brood rearing takes place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1579}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE COLONY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The colony is the social organizational unit of honey bees, characterized by a division of labor and a collective response to internal and external needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colony refers to the group of bees being managed, which functions as a collective biological organization with specific growth patterns and social behaviors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colony refers to the organized social group of bees living together in a hive, functioning as a single unit for survival and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The organized social group of bees living and working together in a hive for mutual survival and success."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2b5f69931d3a60795392f1cd07c4c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1582}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECTICIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical substances used to kill insects, which can cause massive disruptions or death within a bee colony."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1582}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHEROMONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical signals given off by adult bees and brood that communicate the status and needs of the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical signals used as a control mechanism to attract and manage pest beetle species, including small hive beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical substances emitted by an organism that act as stimuli to others of the same species, triggering specific behavioral responses, perceived as odors or tastes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical substances emitted by organisms to stimulate specific behavioral responses in others of the same species, serving as a primary communication method for bees."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f51ec44f0c17ad5253b21395cf12591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fce1495ba322c9e7eb5acd1c4069cdf</data>
