    <node id="&quot;SWARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A natural process of colony reproduction where a portion of the bees leave the parent colony to establish a new one."&lt;SEP&gt;"Swarming is a natural process of colony propagation where a portion of the bee population, including the queen, leaves the parent colony to establish a new colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Swarming is a natural process where a queen bee and a large group of worker bees leave their original colony to establish a new home."&lt;SEP&gt;"Swarming is a natural reproductive process where a bee colony breaks into two groups to create a replica of itself."&lt;SEP&gt;"Swarming is the natural process of reproduction for a honey bee colony, where a queen and a group of worker bees leave the hive to establish a new colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process where a portion of a colony, including the queen, leaves to establish a new home."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651bdc43ce4f434b1e5c689b3528db55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c516e184f72cae24cee188c702d41f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6550c1217ac242a6cb1c3d9a5de5ee35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1205bbac28347dacca693957c5262ae4</data>
