    <node id="&quot;POLLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A necessary part of the bees' diet, specifically required by newly emerged young bees for brood rearing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A protein source collected by bees, stored in cells, and characterized by various colors."&lt;SEP&gt;"A substance collected by bees, often used as a health food supplement for humans or fed back to bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dust-sized particles from plant anthers used for procreation and essential for rearing bee brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dustlike grains produced in flower anthers, serving as the male reproductive element and a protein source for bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pollen is a nutritional store collected by bees, necessary for the health and development of the brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pollen is the male reproductive part of a flower, serving as the primary protein source for bee muscle, gland, and tissue development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The male reproductive part of a flower, collected by bees and consolidated into pellets for nutritional value and colony development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64bd868f29e83effc96703b72e21cc18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9654edf0284987ba4f0c8bde4acffe9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6550c1217ac242a6cb1c3d9a5de5ee35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b652e467f32b1db6fbb1cf5b9315586e</data>
