    <node id="&quot;FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A base, often made of wax or plastic, used in supers to encourage bees to build comb."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sheet of wax or plastic used in beehives to provide a starting point and guide for bees to build straight combs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A textured sheet, usually made of wax or plastic, that provides a template for bees to build straight honeycombs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A wax or plastic sheet used as a base for bees to build comb upon."&lt;SEP&gt;"A wax or plastic sheet, often wire-reinforced, that provides a starting pattern for bees to build honeycomb."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foundation is a thin sheet of wax or plastic used as a starting point for bees to build their honeycomb cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foundation is a wax or plastic sheet used in frames to provide a starting point for bees to build comb."&lt;SEP&gt;"The base material provided in frames that bees use to build wax combs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wax or plastic sheet that provides a starting point and pattern for bees to build honeycombs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91fddbed5da654e2156cc50a2222b4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59256e1e091228ca7c65d0b5d8fb2348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 407}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1556}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT PINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hardware used to hold the frames securely in place within the hive body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 407}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1556}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNER COVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beekeeping component placed on top of the hive to maintain bee space and provide ventilation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A component of a beehive that can be reversed to facilitate ventilation and insulation when used with an insulation board."&lt;SEP&gt;"A cover placed between the hive bodies and the outer cover to provide ventilation and insulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hive cover situated beneath the outer cover that allows for ventilation and feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"A piece of hive equipment placed between the super/hive body and the outer cover to maintain bee space and provide ventilation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The inner cover is a component of the hive that can be fitted with insulation or notches to provide ventilation and moisture control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67600081c317292f8ef362e2f5621f34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1de5be48f8b86dabc08e5087f75750aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9b2fa060b49dfcd9523440966c974ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59256e1e091228ca7c65d0b5d8fb2348</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 406}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1545}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTER COVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The final protective top of the hive, often telescoping to fit snugly over the structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outer cover is the top-most part of the hive, which often needs to be weighed down or strapped to prevent it from being displaced by wind or animals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outermost cover of a modern beehive designed to protect the hive from precipitation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The top cover of a beehive, which can be propped up to allow airflow and evaporate moisture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9654edf0284987ba4f0c8bde4acffe9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1de5be48f8b86dabc08e5087f75750aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
