    <node id="&quot;GEORGIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A U.S. state that has fought with Tennessee and Alabama over water rights and river access."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where another beekeeper reported losing six hundred hives in a similar manner."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where samples of healthy and afflicted hives were collected."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state on the East Coast known to be inhabited by the phorid fly."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state with a climate suitable for outdoor cultivation of Paddy Straw mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state with a climate suitable for using open-air, netted growing rooms for yield recapture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A southern US state known for producing package bees due to its climate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state in the US mentioned as a source of uniform matrons for requeening bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A warm southern state in the US where the small hive beetle is considered a significant pest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Georgia is a U.S. state mentioned as a location where a pedal-powered bean sheller is popular at a market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Georgia is one of the states forming the southern Appalachian mountain region associated with ASAP's local food criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Georgia is the location where Dave Hackenberg currently places his bees in the woods to avoid pesticides."</data>
