    <node id="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A liquid feed consisting of sugar and water used by beekeepers to feed bees to ensure comb is drawn out."&lt;SEP&gt;"A liquid mixture of sugar and water used to feed bees, often applied to comb cells to stimulate activity or provide energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mixture of sugar and water used as a food source for bees, prepared in various stages such as the hard ball candy stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mixture of sugar and water used by beekeepers to feed bees when natural nectar stores are insufficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mixture of table-grade sugar and water used as a food source for bees, especially during installation and early colony growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar syrup is a feed used by Miller in the spring to sustain bees as they wait for almond blooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar syrup is a man-made food source used by beekeepers to feed hives that are low on honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar syrup is a mixture of sugar and water used as a supplemental food source for bees during cold weather."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar syrup is a mixture of sugar and water used by beekeepers to feed bees to encourage comb building or prevent starvation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb545522a163c5982461b497e852ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464158e8ae6f11d3eade0bd5a72fca55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-693ffb57dfcac7260fd0345d7e791e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb5ed2e7521db41a82dfc5b79b8b701</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1587}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2074}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nuc (nucleus colony) is a small hive body used for starting new colonies or transporting a small group of bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nuc, or nucleus colony, is a small colony of bees used to start a new hive, consisting of a few frames of bees and brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nucleus colony, or nuc, is a small honey bee colony used by beekeepers to divide a hive, reduce mite populations, and rear new queens."&lt;SEP&gt;"A small nucleus colony of bees used as an alternative to a package for starting a new hive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-35f6eef0d2ff08b3a3b7b2c2e942edde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
