    <node id="&quot;HIVE BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hive body is a structural component of a beehive that houses frames and provides space for the colony to live and store honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"The main box structure of a beehive that contains frames where bees build comb and raise brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"The main boxes of the hive that house the brood nest and the primary population of bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The main part of a hive, usually a box 9⅝ inches deep containing brood frames."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2b5f69931d3a60795392f1cd07c4c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67600081c317292f8ef362e2f5621f34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
