    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTRANCE REDUCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An entrance reducer is a tool used to limit the size of the hive entrance to help the colony defend against robbing bees."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2b5f69931d3a60795392f1cd07c4c3a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1582}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A box filled with frames placed above the brood chamber to store excess honey for harvest."&lt;SEP&gt;"A component of a beehive used specifically for the storage of honey by bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A honey super is an additional box placed on top of the hive bodies to allow bees to store surplus honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"A super is a specific hive body placed on top of the colony intended for the storage of surplus honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"A super is an additional hive body placed on top of the colony to provide extra space for honey and brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"A superstructure placed on a beehive to provide specific space for bees to store surplus honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supers are shallow or mid-sized boxes used in beekeeping to replace hive bodies or to collect surplus honey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2b5f69931d3a60795392f1cd07c4c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39baafb5b073ac43e9932248ea8ca932</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1598}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH CURVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The growth curve is a diagrammed mathematical representation of the expected population increase of a bee colony over a season."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2b5f69931d3a60795392f1cd07c4c3a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1582}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECTAR FLOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A period during the season when flowering plants produce nectar, stimulating wax production and colony expansion in bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The period when flowering plants produce nectar, triggering increased activity and honey production in the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"The period when flowers produce nectar in abundance, signaling the transition to spring and the end of supplemental feeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1583}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2068}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The act of adding supers to a hive to provide additional honey storage space."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process and method of placing supers on a hive to manage honey storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39baafb5b073ac43e9932248ea8ca932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1598}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FALL MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of preparing a bee colony for winter, involving specific tasks that often begin in spring and continue through autumn."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1583}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 2069}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WINTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The coldest season of the year, during which bee colonies are confined to the hive and form clusters for survival."</data>
