    <node id="&quot;NOSEMA DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A disease affecting bees that may require medication to manage before winter."&lt;SEP&gt;"A disease causing brown spotting or staining on frames and combs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fungal/protozoan parasitic disease affecting honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A serious disease caused by protozoa that infects the gut of adult bees, including workers, drones, and the queen."&lt;SEP&gt;"A widespread and serious infection of the gut of adult bees caused by a protozoa, leading to reduced productivity and colony decline."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad055bc816d7df3212732523b38332d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c4227735c6f952b192f6d769deb712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1564}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A parasite that affected bee colonies across North America, causing panic in the beekeeping industry in the mid-1980s."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pest affecting European honey bees that was imported or migrated into the US between 1984 and 1997."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as Acarapis woodi, these are microscopic pests that infest the breathing tubes (tracheae) of honey bees, causing respiratory distress and colony losses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microscopic parasites that infest the tracheae of honey bees, potentially shortening their lives and affecting colony vitality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parasites (Acarapis woodi) that cause bees to die with wings rotated into a K-shape."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parasitic mites that affect the health of bees within a colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parasitic mites that inhabit the breathing tubes of honey bees, causing debilitating effects on colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parasitic mites that inhabit the tracheal system of bees, treatable with Miticur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracheal Mites are parasites that infect the respiratory system of honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracheal mites are parasites of bees that beekeepers must manage individually as they are widespread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracheal mites are parasites that inhabit the breathing tubes of honey bees, potentially harming the colony."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940d85de3b7092a6c76b3ef360a50ea0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c4227735c6f952b192f6d769deb712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbe3628e117427ed1c35a791b026e9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4642364014d20a8527d9fb4ec06bdb04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c85b379d83c9f869435c42e6568dee9</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 324}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1328}]</data>
    </node>
