    <node id="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A capping scratcher, also known as an uncapping fork, is a tool used by beekeepers to remove drone pupae from cells for mite inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used by beekeepers to remove and uncap drone brood to inspect for the presence of mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used to break up low spots and missed cappings on a honey frame."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as an uncapping fork, this tool is used to remove wax cappings from areas of the comb that a knife or machine cannot reach."</data>
