      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Foulbrood (AFB) is a bacterial disease affecting honey bee colonies, characterized by spores that harbor in hive products like beeswax, pollen, and honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Foulbrood is a serious bacterial disease affecting honey bee larvae, characterized by the formation of brown, putrefying brood and a distinct sour odor."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Foulbrood, a bacterial disease affecting honey bee larvae caused by Paenibacillus larvae."</data>
