    <node id="&quot;APISTAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 'hard' chemical mite treatment containing fluvalinate, which the varroa mite developed resistance to over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical treatment used to control mites in honey bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"A contact miticide containing fluvalinate, provided as impregnated plastic strips used to treat mite infestations in beehives."&lt;SEP&gt;"A miticide strip used by beekeepers to kill varroa mites, which eventually became ineffective due to mite resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A previously effective miticide delivered via plastic strips in hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"A toxic chemical strip used to treat varroa mite infestations in hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apistan is a chemical control product used in beekeeping to combat varroa mite infestations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apistan is a chemical used to kill varroa mites in bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apistan is a commercial product containing the active ingredient fluvalinate used for mite control in beehives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apistan is a miticide product consisting of flexible plastic sticks coated with low doses of medicine used to treat varroa mite infestations in bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apistan is a pesticide strip used in hives that relies on the active chemical component fluvalinate."</data>
