      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound used in Apistan to short-circuit the biological system of varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical miticide approved by the EPA for use in beehives."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical treatment for mites that can leave residues in honeycombs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluvalinate is a chemical component related to the pyrethrin family of pesticides, used as the active ingredient in Apistan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluvalinate is a miticide and the active ingredient in Apistan used to control varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"The active chemical ingredient in Apistan used for controlling mites in honey bee colonies."</data>
