    <node id="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A device used as a recommended defense to deter bears from entering beeyards by delivering an electric shock."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fencing system used to control the movement of livestock and manage the areas of pasture being grazed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fencing system using electric current to deter livestock, valued for its cheapness and flexibility in creating and adjusting paddock divisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fencing system using electricity to control the movement of livestock, used here to facilitate rationed grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fencing system using electricity to restrict the movement of livestock, enabling the division of pastures into smaller, manageable sections for rationed grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fencing technology sometimes associated with rationed grazing to control animal movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A simple instrument used in rational grazing to manage the timing of grass rest and regrowth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used by farmers to create movable boundaries for cattle, reducing the labor involved in shifting grazing areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used in grazing systems to manage the movement of livestock and shift grazing areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used in rationed grazing systems to manage the movement of livestock."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used to divide grazing land into paddocks and control the movement of livestock."&lt;SEP&gt;"An electric fence is a device used by the narrator to keep livestock out of a creek and protect the land."&lt;SEP&gt;"An electric fence is mentioned as a tool for dividing pastures, though the text emphasizes that it is a means to an end rather than the goal of rational grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The electric fence is a security system used to deter bears and other pests from apiaries using an electric shock."&lt;SEP&gt;"The electric fence is a tool used in grazing systems to divide pastures and manage the movement of animals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The electric fence is a tool used to manage and move livestock in a rationed grazing system, moved twice daily to control grass access."</data>
