    <node id="&quot;U.S. DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A United States government agency that implemented food safety initiatives to limit risks from E. coli."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government agency that created the certified-organic label for agricultural products."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government department established by Abraham Lincoln, referred to as 'the people's department,' to support agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also referred to as the Usda, this is the federal agency responsible for agriculture in the United States, which provides definitions for farm sizes and farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Agriculture is the government agency where Bennett conducted his professional work in soil science."&lt;SEP&gt;"The USDA is the federal agency that encourages and oversees agricultural production and food safety protocols in the United States, housing various offices and libraries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The USDA is the federal agency that encourages and oversees agricultural production and food safety protocols in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"The federal agency responsible for agriculture and food, which published 'A Citizen's Guide to Food Recovery'."&lt;SEP&gt;"The federal agency responsible for agriculture in the United States, where Howard W. 'Bud' Kerr, Jr. served."&lt;SEP&gt;"The federal agency responsible for agriculture in the United States, where King worked."&lt;SEP&gt;"The federal agency responsible for government services and programs related to farming and agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The government agency responsible for setting standards for 'safe and wholesome' meat, which influences dietary practices in the US."</data>
