    <node id="&quot;FARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An industry that expanded without local energy restraints, leading to environmental issues and the development of the NIMBY mindset."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the industry involving the cultivation of crops and raising of livestock, requiring equipment maintenance and cost analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the industry involving the cultivation of plants and raising of animals for commercial purposes, characterized by specific tax laws and record-keeping requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the industry of cultivating land and raising livestock, discussed in terms of its economic viability and lifestyle appeals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the industry of cultivating land, raising livestock, and managing crops to produce food and income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the primary industry discussed, encompassing production types, history, lifestyle, and agripreneurship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the primary industry discussed, encompassing various types of agricultural operations including crop and livestock production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farming is the primary industry discussed, focusing on sustainable operations, livestock management, and resource optimization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry and practice of cultivating crops and raising livestock, governed by principles of sustainability, profitability, and environmental soundness."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry focused on cultivating crops and raising livestock, characterized here by the use of interns and specific physical labor requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry of cultivating land, raising livestock, and producing agricultural products for profit."</data>
