    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTOSYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biological process used by plants to obtain carbon and mass from the air."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photosynthesis is the biological process by which plants capture carbon to grow and create exudates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which green cells in plants use sunlight to synthesize nutrients from carbon dioxide and water, providing the building material for plant growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which plants extract energy from the sun, requiring water to function."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which plants obtain carbon from the atmosphere, which challenged the traditional humus theory of soil fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which plants use solar energy to create food, mentioned as a fundamental source of biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process used by plants to create elements necessary for the formation of new cells and the initial re-growth of the plant."&lt;SEP&gt;"The natural process by which plants use sunlight to produce crops and forages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f83b407929c9c73f6150edfd6dc214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c27be2a10bcdcaefcaa83280a8660a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2473f4dcebdbdd42ecfa05be804a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3bdad2c51924f6ea3d4926cb64ba97c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa752fa09edea3d82b95c339728d49cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2a728c62a50818090fcc2e56fcaf5fc</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 50}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN FIXATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biological process where atmospheric nitrogen is converted into a form usable by plants, requiring organic matter, oxygen, moisture, and bases like calcium carbonate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A biological process where leguminous plants or bacteria like Azotobacters convert atmospheric nitrogen into a form usable by plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen fixation is the biological process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into a usable form for plants, specifically mentioned in the context of soil organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The biological process by which nitrogen from the air is converted into a form that plants can use, involving rhizobia and specific soil minerals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ffae2696b4f9024085ef90af5320a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f80535289583d0b174a792dec934f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f685240aeecfc4a0556f03c0af930046</data>
