    <node id="&quot;COVER CROPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cover crops are a soil-conserving agricultural technique used to build soil fertility and prevent erosion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cover crops are plants grown primarily to benefit the soil, such as hairy vetch and clover, used by Brandt to recycle nutrients and support microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cover crops are plants like radishes, sunflowers, and vetch planted primarily to manage soil erosion, soil quality, and nutrient availability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plants grown primarily to manage soil erosion, soil fertility, and weed suppression rather than for harvest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plants grown primarily to prevent soil erosion, suppress weeds, protect soil from freezing/thawing, and improve microbiological activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The practice of sowing specific plants, such as winter rye or hairy vetch, to prevent erosion, retain moisture, and stop nutrient leaking in the soil."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eea73e36d5dc1a7d6617766c0a980521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eddf2c11ae7d5f7c383adfd979b680d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28351085b82af5a0f49bb9d74856507b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d3e2ae9649f6dc7e9301ed98bc01d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c12c90d0c9b0f56b008795013b9e85a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b6332789cdbd68f546cf7328c6217fd</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 563}]</data>
    </node>
