      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A geographic region in the United States where the Rainbow Farmer's Cooperative operates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States mentioned as a source of meat."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States mentioned in the context of optimal birthing temperatures and timing for livestock."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States that experienced a poor honey crop due to a cool, wet summer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States where grains are grown and where bison once grazed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States where urban water supplies are affected by nitrogen pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the United States where wheat harvests are associated with hot, dry days in July and August."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region of North America featured in William Cronon's ecological history."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region of the United States where sweet clover nitrogen levels were studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a geographic region mentioned in the context of cultural communication styles regarding farming and agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a geographic region where high winds and drought can affect the stability of greenhouse posts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a region in North America where oak forests and Chanterelles can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a region in the United States mentioned as a context where mildness in communication is culturally important, particularly regarding farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a region in the United States mentioned in the context of losing soil organic matter from agricultural lands."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a region in the United States where grain production and processing have historically consolidated."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwest is a region where local Amish farmers cultivate fields using traditional methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The region of North America opened up for homesteading by the use of Deere's plow."</data>
