    <node id="&quot;MANAGEMENT-INTENSIVE GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific livestock production method focused on the strategic movement of animals to improve pasture health and yield."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as MIG, a farming approach that emphasizes the thinking process and management to ensure farm sustainability and success."&lt;SEP&gt;"Management-intensive grazing (or MIG) is a specific agricultural technique used to manage livestock and land sustainably and profitably."&lt;SEP&gt;"Management-intensive grazing is a specific agricultural method involving a minimum of sixteen grazing paddocks to maximize forage use and cattle productivity."</data>
