    <node id="&quot;CSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) is a food system where consumers buy shares of a farm's harvest, shifting management risks and focusing on production and community connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) is a model of food distribution and support mentioned as a way for teens to impact the food system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) is a socio-economic model of agriculture where consumers buy shares in a farm's harvest, sharing the risks and rewards of the food production process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) is a socio-economic model where consumers support a farm in exchange for a share of the produce."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) is a socio-economic model/system where consumers prepay for a share of a farm's produce, sharing the risks and rewards of production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture, a cooperative model used for selling farm produce directly to consumers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture, a model for selling produce directly from farmers to consumers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture, a model where consumers support a farm through shares in exchange for a portion of the harvest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture, a model where members support a farm and may visit the site, potentially leading to liability risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture, a system where consumers buy into a local farm's harvest for the season."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture; a model where growers sell produce directly to consumers, often requiring a variety of crops."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Supported Agriculture; a subscription-based farming model mentioned as a point of comparison for food circles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community-supported agriculture (CSA) is a production and marketing model where consumers buy shares of a farm's harvest in advance, sharing the risks and rewards of food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community-supported agriculture, a system where shareholders share the production risks and provide some labor on the farm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bbbece9d51f6abc4742c05514bea625e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd26cfc74dc054c475a18b57c09b309a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc62cfc471a50456f18bf536e809f4aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26f04bc8df6a747ead835cc8d210eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efe185a1df447e99af70cc3756a14187&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6df96ec37541056c75a89771b307b9cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c449279cf31a0e070abdb1ec56f6fbc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e929a727edf557065879c8f5b9dc9020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa81fea1066bfc4f1fbbd063489245c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0237853ab2dfc7f5ad3804ab83cf15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d16c2413dd929af8532f1ba9572924a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
