    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY-SUPPORTED AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A model of agriculture where consumers support local farmers through a subscription or membership, known as CSAs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and economic model of agriculture where consumers support farmers directly."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social-economic model where consumers buy 'shares' of a farm's harvest in advance to support the farmer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system where consumers support local farmers by paying for a share of the harvest in advance, fostering a community-based food system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system/model of agriculture where consumers connect directly with a farm and purchase a season's worth of produce in advance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as CSA, a financial and social model where consumers support farmers by paying for a share of the harvest in advance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An alternative food system model aimed at revitalizing the connection between producers and consumers to cultivate virtue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community-supported agriculture (CSA) is a social and economic model that connects producers and consumers, expanding as part of the sustainable movement."</data>
