    <node id="&quot;LOCAL FOOD MOVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A burgeoning movement focused on sourcing food from nearby producers to ensure transparency and sustainability, currently in its infancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A grassroots social and economic movement focused on reclaiming food systems to grow community spirit, sustainability, and resilience across all levels of society."&lt;SEP&gt;"A movement focused on increasing the proportion of food grown and processed in a local community to improve health and sustainability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and economic movement focusing on the consumption of food grown or produced locally."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local food movement is a social and economic effort to increase the production and consumption of food grown locally to improve health and education."&lt;SEP&gt;"The local food movement is a social and economic trend focusing on sourcing food from local producers to improve sustainability and community connection."</data>
