    <node id="&quot;DRIP IRRIGATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method of irrigation that delivers water directly to the bed, used in conjunction with low tunnels."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method of irrigation that delivers water slowly to the roots of plants, involving components like drip tape, headers, and regulators."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method of irrigation that delivers water slowly to the roots of plants, often using drip tape and emitters to conserve water."&lt;SEP&gt;"A preferred method of irrigation for most vegetable and fruit crops that requires a water pressure of 15 to 30 psi."&lt;SEP&gt;"An efficient irrigation method that delivers water directly to the plants' root zone, reducing water waste and preventing foliar diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drip irrigation is a watering technology installed by the Seattle Urban Farm Company to efficiently water urban gardens."</data>
