    <node id="&quot;GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A country associated with multiple publication and congress locations including Braunschweig and Kelheim."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country in Europe from which many poor people emigrated to America to become wealthy farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country in Europe, the location of Koeltz Scientific Books."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country in Europe."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country where archaeological excavations revealed Nordic black earth similar to terra preta."&lt;SEP&gt;"A country where rooftop gardening and apiculture have been common for years."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germany is a country where a similar trend of returning to permanent pastures occurred as seen in Britain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germany is a country where pasture yields are examined and compared."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germany is the country where the Grassland Research Station is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germany is the homeland of the Anglo-Saxon immigrants and the origin of their village and farming customs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germany is the origin of N. E. Miller's immigrant farmer parents."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where Geith conducted his research on the composition of grass."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where Geith's hand-books on rotational grazing were used and published."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where Rengen is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Grassland Research Station at Cleves is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Grassland Research Station is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Hohenheim Institute is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Rengen Grassland Research Station is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Rengen and Dikopshof experiments on rationed grazing took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Rengen estate and the associated grazing experiments took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Rengen estates and the Eifel region are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The country where the Research Institute at Brunswick-Völkenrode is located and where soil data was collected."</data>
