    <node id="&quot;NUESTRAS RAÍCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A community organization focused on urban farming, youth programs, and celebrating Puerto Rican heritage."&lt;SEP&gt;"A community-based nonprofit organization that provides farming training, business incubation, and food access to low-income people in Holyoke."&lt;SEP&gt;"A grassroots nonprofit organization that serves as an example of a community-based food organization providing localized economic benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large nonprofit formed from the expansion of La Finquita and other programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nationally recognized project that incubates new businesses and farmers, empowers women and youths, and celebrates Puerto Rican food heritage."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization based in Holyoke, Massachusetts, that focuses on community support and gardening for immigrant farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization based in Holyoke, Massachusetts, that works on growing new farmers through incubators."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization in Holyoke, Massachusetts, that transforms vacant or abandoned lots into community gardens."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization in Holyoke, Massachusetts, that transitioned from a small community garden to a hub for youth and women's empowerment and a small-enterprise incubator."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization likely focused on community gardening or cultural heritage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuestras Raíces is a grassroots nonprofit organization in Holyoke, Massachusetts, founded by Puerto Rican immigrants to promote economic, human, and community development through food, agriculture, and the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nuestras Raíces is an organization that uses community gardens to foster youth and women's empowerment and operates a farmer incubator."</data>
