      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A U.S. government agency created in the 1970s to protect human health and the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A federal agency tasked with protecting human health and the environment, mentioned here in the context of regulating pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government agency that declared the site a Superfund site, performed cleanup, and later provided a Sustainable Development Challenge Grant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also referred to as the EPA, a government agency responsible for environmental protection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EPA is a federal agency that funds voluntary brownfields remediation programs to help clean contaminated sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EPA is a government agency that provides approval for genetically modified corn."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-86ff000ef6783ed151c47581219450eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb807e6a60ab003ee9b4b47c9c83c846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6fd2b31420a632f31dfe7120da040d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6389477351f5ce08f5964ec7d9d64e85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78d99903600ffa6f92d29953bed6a52</data>
