    <node id="&quot;COMPOSTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Composting is a biological process and technology used by Lynchburg Grows to create healthy soil from leaves, wood chips, and dining hall waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Composting is a farming technique for re-fertilization involving the decomposition of organic matter, which can be done by hand or mechanically."&lt;SEP&gt;"Composting is the biological process of breaking down organic matter, such as night soil and crop stubble, to reclaim nutritional value for soil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Composting is the process of increasing the volume of fertilizing material by mixing animal and vegetable wastes, an alternative to the traditional manure heap."&lt;SEP&gt;"Composting is the technology/process of recycling organic matter, such as cane trash and filter press cake, into a valuable organic manure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of recycling organic matter, such as vegetable wastes and manure, into a nutrient-rich soil amendment through controlled decomposition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-afc70624d5d4eaaf334c2f206580b15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cee86d7056c73fbe7bdaa432b2abe64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ac72dfa70392b35da5b9538cf9d2202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f80535289583d0b174a792dec934f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d39c198d76fe810125daf8052a573b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04c7decd932543d02d71519d2eca78a1</data>
