    <node id="&quot;JOEL SALATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small-scale farmer in northern Virginia known for creating low-capital production prototypes and the North American pastured chicken industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"An author, speaker, and farmer who serves as a model for integrating livestock and produce on a farm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is a college-educated entrepreneur and farmer who advocates for a Jeffersonian approach to agriculture and runs Polyface Farm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is a farmer and innovator associated with Polyface Farm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is a farmer, author, and contrarian thinker described as a 'Christian libertarian environmentalist capitalist lunatic' who advocates for sustainable, non-industrial food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is an author and figure associated with Polyface Farm who wrote about the mob-stocking technique."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is the innovator and owner of Polyface Farm, known for his challenge to the status quo and his sustainable farming systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is the owner and operator of Polyface Farm who advocates for bioregional food clusters and local food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is the owner and operator of Polyface farm, focusing on sustainable agriculture, healing the land, and innovative farming systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is the owner of Polyface Farm who inspired Jamie Ager to pursue profitable farming through a different operational model."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joel Salatin is the visionary behind Polyface and the concept of bioregional, scalable, sensitive food clusters to support small family farms."</data>
