    <node id="&quot;DUST BOWL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A period of severe drought and famine in North America that tested the resilience of agricultural systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of severe dust storms and ecological collapse in the American and Canadian prairies during the 1930s."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of severe environmental devastation and drought that forced many people, including the Joad family, to migrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A severe environmental disaster in the 1930s characterized by soil erosion and farm failures."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ecological disaster characterized by severe drought and wind storms that ruined land in the Great Plains during the 1930s."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl refers to the era of severe dust storms and soil erosion in the 1930s, primarily affecting the American prairies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl refers to the period of severe dust storms and ecological disaster that affected farm families in the American prairies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl was a historical environmental disaster caused by soil erosion and drought, cited as a reason for the necessity of crop residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl was a major ecological disaster and period of severe dust storms that affected the Great Plains."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl was a national disaster characterized by severe dust storms that affected the U.S. Midwest, including Texas, the Dakotas, and Ohio."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl was a period of severe dust storms and ecological damage caused by drought and tillage practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dust Bowl was a period of severe dust storms that highlighted the need to abandon plowing."</data>
