    <node id="&quot;DANIEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A son of the author who engaged in imaginative play and learned persistence through working on projects."&lt;SEP&gt;"A thirteen-year-old apprentice on the author's farm who possessed superior situational awareness and an understanding of danger."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is Williams' husband who works the land despite harsh weather conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is a person involved in the farming operation who explains the process of rotational grazing to the mower operator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is a son of the narrator who started a successful rabbit breeding and selling business from a young age."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is an individual associated with Polyface Farm who suggested using plastic bags instead of trays for packaging chicken."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is an individual mentioned in the context of his character development and business acumen through a rabbit enterprise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is an individual who, along with Sheri, makes nutrient-dense jerky from deer loins on their farm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is the husband of Rose Marie Williams who works on the family farm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daniel is the son of the author, who started a rabbit enterprise at age eight to develop his farming skills and business acumen."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author's son who built a crude hot smoker for food preservation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author's son who learned to drive a tractor and was homeschooled."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author's son."&lt;SEP&gt;"The narrator's son who handles day-to-day farm operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The son of the author who built his own house on the farm using local lumber."&lt;SEP&gt;"The son of the narrator and Teresa, who was capable of moving a hundred cows at eight years old."</data>
