    <node id="&quot;GREEN REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mid-20th century movement to increase crop yields and eliminate hunger through technology and policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period beginning in the 1940s characterized by research, development, and technology transfer to increase crop production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of agricultural development characterized by fertilizer-intensive practices and top-down implementation via government and corporate research."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of agricultural intensification that increased crop yields through the use of chemical fertilizers and pesticides, often at the expense of soil life."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of agricultural transformation characterized by high-yield wheat and rice varieties and intensive fertilizer use."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of significant agricultural transformation characterized by the use of high-yield crop varieties and chemical inputs, which the text suggests is based on failed philosophical concepts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of technological advancement in agriculture during the second half of the 20th century involving high-yield seeds, pesticides, and fertilizers to increase food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of technology transfer and agricultural intensification that increased food production but increased dependence on nonrenewable energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period of transformation in agriculture characterized by the shift to chemical-based fertilizers and high-yield crops to feed the world."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution is referenced as a period of agricultural transformation characterized by a primary focus on technological limits rather than the economic ability of farmers to bear costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution refers to a period of agricultural intensification characterized by the use of high-yielding varieties, chemical fertilizers, and extensive land clearing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution refers to a period of agricultural transformation characterized by a fertilizer-intensive approach to boosting crop yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution refers to a period of intense agricultural technology transfer that increased crop yields globally, used here as a benchmark for yield increase."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution refers to a period of transformation in agriculture characterized by the widespread use of chemical-based fertilizers, herbicides, and pesticides to increase food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of agricultural transformation that focused on high-yielding crops and chemicals, though it often excluded traditional subsistence farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of technological advances in agriculture that boosted yields but increased corporate control of the food system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f57077126bc61f1a2588c34ca9614e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05c72d9498345815172a428a41b0f62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2f3cf7878919c86769d45741d13fa4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59a4b4194753d7082d9b1d100574c96f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac6f2d596c9d9fe2bc3b9afda4f10df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5244a72295d4f84fc85246a4eb4df315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ab141b6aa8655dd452f4b60acea75bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8f4ced19f39489760889dcf78f83b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2473f4dcebdbdd42ecfa05be804a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d827b4b169dc20f345800758c486eb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ebf23631547617747b7c2b24e2249cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c384530d2705c862df0ec1ef11c2d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b265b8d53df8f70babd69fc84ec3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3b1063c1d500ceacda94be5c1a920e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28ab0744bd2c8644bdc99e6c30ae80a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
    </node>
