    <node id="&quot;PERMACULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A concept and philosophy pioneered by Bill Mollison that fuses permanent agriculture and permanent culture to promote sustainable environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A design system based on ecological principles that aims to create sustainable and productive human habitats by mimicking natural ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of agricultural and social design principles centered on simulating or directly utilizing the patterns and resilient features of natural ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of agricultural and social design principles, mentioned in the context of a mycological twist."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of ecological design focused on creating sustainable and regenerative homes, neighborhoods, and communities through nature's patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"An approach to land management and sustainable agricultural design that incorporates the use of mushrooms for environmental benefit."&lt;SEP&gt;"An approach to land management and sustainable design focused on keeping water in the landscape and mimicking natural ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ecological design system and strategy used to integrate mushroom cultivation for environmental health and soil generation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permaculture is a sustainable land-management and design system based on mimicking natural ecosystems to increase biodiversity and regenerate the land."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permaculture is a system of agricultural and social design principles centered on simulating or directly utilizing the patterns and resilient features observed in natural ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permaculture is an integrated farm model and design system mentioned as a framework for incorporating mycological practices."</data>
