    <node id="&quot;NO-TILL FARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A farming method that avoids plowing to preserve soil structure and organic matter, promoted by Guy Swanson."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming method that avoids plowing, reducing soil erosion, diesel costs, and fertilizer needs while improving water absorption."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming method that leaves crop residue at the ground surface to allow soil microbes to break down nutrients and reduce the need for tillage."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agricultural method that avoids plowing and tilling the soil to reduce erosion and input costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agricultural technique that avoids plowing to reduce soil erosion and improve soil health, though its adoption is often hindered by the cost of herbicides."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agricultural technique that avoids tilling the soil, instead seeding crops through crop residues to preserve soil structure and health."&lt;SEP&gt;"No-till farming is a practice that eliminates plowing to reduce carbon emissions and improve soil health."</data>
