      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An author or thinker whose views on agricultural policy, food, and health are being analyzed and critiqued by the narrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual cited for noting unaccounted for costs in the context of agricultural specialization."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who believes that mainstream agriculture is on a collision course with food consumers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pollan (Michael Pollan) is an author and critic who advocated for redefining agricultural policy as a 'food bill' to include consumer interests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pollan is an individual to whom Kahn described the environmental gains of industrial organic food."</data>
