    <node id="&quot;TYSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A company associated with large-scale chicken houses and industrial farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large corporate entity known for industrial chicken houses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large food company mentioned as an entity that cannot afford for people to embrace the truth about the food system."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large-scale industrial chicken producer used as a baseline for comparison against pastured chicken fat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a company associated with chicken houses and industrial food production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a large commercial poultry company mentioned in the context of food security and industrial farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a large company that contracts with farmers to grow chickens, characterized by the author as a system of voluntary feudalism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a large conglomerate in the food industry that utilizes contract growers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a large food processing company that maintains facilities in various towns and is often used by institutions as a 'local' source despite its corporate structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is a large industrial food corporation viewed by the author as a dubious source of food security."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tyson is mentioned as a benchmark for industrial-scale poultry production, representing the corporate model Polyface seeks to avoid."</data>
