    <node id="&quot;BRITAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Britain is a country where ley farming was practiced and where farmers are observed returning to permanent pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is a country where open-cast mining has impacted agricultural land, necessitating reclamation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is a country where pasture yields and the sale of sugar beet roots to refineries are discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is mentioned as a place where descriptions of pasture rotation were supplied in the eighteenth century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is mentioned in the context of agricultural land reclamation following the damage caused by open-cast mining."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is the country mentioned in the context of its specific ley farming practices and permanent grass challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is the country where the author has surveyed and valued land across nearly every county."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is the island where Roman and later Saxon agricultural systems were established and practiced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain is the location where Newman Turner's ley farming system was implemented."&lt;SEP&gt;"Britain, mentioned as one of the countries where scientists have expressed opinions on grass proteins."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small island nation mentioned as being dependent on exports according to a false doctrine."</data>
