    <node id="&quot;GRASS TETANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolic disorder in cattle caused by factors such as rationed grazing on temporary pasture and the application of nitrogenous fertilizers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metabolic disorder in cattle discussed in Chapter 6."&lt;SEP&gt;"A paralysis affecting animals, particularly those at grass, characterized by hypomagnesemia and ionic imbalance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A physiological condition or phenomenon mentioned as being more accentuated in certain farming systems (ley farming)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grass tetany is a metabolic condition in ruminants characterized by hypomagnesemia and respiratory failure, often triggered by excessive ammonia production in the rumen due to high nitrogen intake."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed80c461fcd7ae24e2d82990c8272a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71693cd9138b6f0587b3bd7e7c04e4e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7397fa08c6c2db670404830568aebfea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d719ed515957569d5a5c0e944e89a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2c3c06185787a0960e3e64c56f15b</data>
