    <node id="&quot;RENGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A location associated with the improvement of grazing practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location in Germany used for common grazings and agricultural observation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location in Germany where Heine carried out experiments on rationed grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location in Germany where common grazings and estates are situated."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where observations regarding the effects of fertilisers on grazing were made by B. Mott."&lt;SEP&gt;"A place associated with the production or use of Swedish wire racks for drying forage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rengen is a location where Professor Klapp utilized an isolating cage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rengen is a location where a specific layout of rationed grazing (Plan III) was implemented on a 17.5-acre pasture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rengen is the location where the agricultural trials on grassland improvement were conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The location where Professor Klapp conducted research with isolating cages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The location where the nitrogen distribution trials and studies on grass production were conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific geographic area and experimental site used for studying the restoration of grazings and the effects of mowing and fertilizers."</data>
