      <data key="d1">"A region in France mentioned in the context of average rest periods for grass grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in France mentioned in the context of average rest periods for pasture grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in France where André Voisin conducted his field observations of grazing cows."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in France where André Voisin's farm was located and where he conducted field observations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in France where the Chapel of Harcourt Castle is situated."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in France where the author observed that rationally managed pastures produce more starch equivalent and protein than arable crops."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region where the author observed significant grass growth and documented specific rest periods for farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normandy is a region in France where Harcourt Castle is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normandy is a region in France where the author's farm and the Pays de Caux are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normandy is a region mentioned in the text where specific figures for utilisable fresh grass in permanent pastures were observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normandy is a region mentioned to illustrate the difference between rationally grazed and continuously grazed pastures during dry years."</data>
