    <node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A traditional grazing method where livestock remain in a pasture from spring until the end of the season."&lt;SEP&gt;"A traditional livestock management method where animals have constant access to a pasture, used in the text as a baseline for comparison against rational grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous Grazing is a livestock management method where cows remain permanently on the same pasture throughout the grazing season."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous grazing is a livestock management method where animals have constant access to a pasture, often leading to inefficient grass utilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous grazing is a method of livestock management where animals have constant access to a pasture, often resulting in lower productivity due to 'hidden' short rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous grazing is a traditional livestock grazing method where animals have constant access to pasture, resulting in lower yields compared to rational grazing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-efe222393fecd71e1d91aa776f41fdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7266683ce075bd299f9731e6b76917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09b74f41d21f409ec5a0b3f597231b30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c11548aaf18b892f15ea3985a824bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9ed5666e76c6deff78175910984bd83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b61ec4c92f8837c4ca00c85162881f8</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1886}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROTATIONAL GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grazing method where cows have free access to a paddock for a set period before being moved to another, allowing the first paddock to rest."&lt;SEP&gt;"An older term for rationed grazing, involving the rotation of grassland to allow for plant recovery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotational grazing is a general livestock management system involving shifting herds between different paddocks or blocks to allow for grass recovery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotational grazing is a livestock management practice involving the movement of livestock between different paddocks to allow grass recovery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotational grazing is a livestock management practice where cattle are moved between different paddocks to allow vegetation to recover."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotational grazing is a practice of moving livestock between paddocks to improve soil health, forage quality, and sequester carbon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rotational grazing is a specific type of rational grazing where animals are moved between different plots of land to allow for adequate regrowth of grass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c583da6fce90c421f7955d582682c8c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f69fd7bda60518d54e55e7ff039d4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7266683ce075bd299f9731e6b76917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a47444af0a2806843b6ade04b1af8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42a3e63b49bd29b4af01b8a4548a8d8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583d1c446eecee65cf5a758322efee03</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 954}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATIONED GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A livestock management practice and industry term involving the controlled distribution of grass and grazing time to animals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rationed grazing is a grazing management method where the allocated area varies based on grass availability, which can lead to a reduction in the number of pasture blocks at rest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rationed grazing is a livestock management system where animals are given specific portions of pasture to graze over a set period to optimize grass regrowth and soil health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rationed grazing is a system of grazing management where the amount of forage available to animals is controlled."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3b7266683ce075bd299f9731e6b76917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583d1c446eecee65cf5a758322efee03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-527055291c96f565ab1e262a61faefd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42a3e63b49bd29b4af01b8a4548a8d8c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 954}]</data>
    </node>
