      <data key="d1">"A chemical element analyzed within the materials, often used to calculate protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element measured as a component of the materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element mentioned in the context of handling dangers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used as a fertilizer to increase yield and growth vigour in grass, acting immediately but lacking persistence."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used as an indicator of protein content in feed materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used as an indicator of protein content in nutritional analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used here as an indicator of protein content in feed materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used in fertilizers to increase pasture production and yield."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical element used to determine protein levels in the provided materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical nutrient applied to pastures as a dressing to increase grass growth and consequently increase the livestock stocking rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen is a chemical element analyzed as a percentage of the clover hay materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen is a valuable chemical element and plant food found in manure that can be lost to the air through denitrification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen is used as a fertilizer to sustain the vigour of grass and prolong the grazing season."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen, specifically in the form of nitrogenous fertilisers, is used as a chemical input to increase the yield and growth rate of grass swards."</data>
