    <node id="&quot;NITRATE OF LIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical dressing used to stimulate the regrowth of grass in pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nitrogenous fertiliser used to accelerate the initial growth of grass in paddocks to extend the grazing season."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nitrogenous fertiliser used to sustain grass growth and increase yield."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nitrogenous fertilizer mentioned as having a more rapid action than ammonium nitrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nitrogenous fertilizer used as a dressing to increase grass productivity and reduce rest periods for grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific form of mineral nitrogen applied to the Voisin pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of nitrogenous fertiliser used in experiments to determine its effect on grass palatability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of rapidly acting nitrogenous fertiliser used to accelerate plant growth after cutting."&lt;SEP&gt;"An alkaline nitrogenous fertilizer characterized by its ultra-rapid effect on grass growth, even during periods of low rainfall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrate of lime is a specific type of nitrogenous fertiliser used at 15% nitrogen to enhance grass growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrate of lime is a specific type of nitrogenous fertiliser used to stimulate increased grass growth in pastures."</data>
