      <data key="d1">"A legume often found in swards and selectively grazed by cows."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legume plant that fixes nitrogen in the soil and acts as an organic fertilizer for associated grasses in pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legume species that acts as a free source of nitrogen and contributes to the quality of permanent pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legume that acts as a factory for free nitrogen production through nodule bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"A plant species that disappears in places where there is an accumulation of cow droppings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A plant that acts as a natural factory for the free production of nitrogen in the soil."&lt;SEP&gt;"A plant widely considered a premier honey plant, producing some of the finest honey in the world."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of forage legume that contributes to the richness of pastures when nitrogen is used and rotations are well managed."</data>
