      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A professor whose work studied how cows harvest grass and their reluctance to work extra hours despite extended grazing areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher at Cornell who studied the effects of cutting intervals on the evolution of pasture flora."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher at the Royal Agricultural College who studied the quantities of grass harvested by cattle using isolating cages."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who conducted pioneer investigations in 1942-43 regarding the quantities of grass harvested by cattle."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who perfected a device for recording cow jaw movements and conducted studies on grazing and harvesting times."&lt;SEP&gt;"An academic at the Royal Agricultural College involved in examining livestock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professor Johnstone-Wallace is a researcher who studied cow grazing patterns, observed their efficiency, and developed a device to record jaw movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professor Johnstone-Wallace is a researcher whose experimental work on cows and scraping operations is cited as a point of comparison for grazing conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professor Johnstone-Wallace is an individual who described the daily timetable of the cow named Beauty."</data>
