    <node id="&quot;HOHENHEIM SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method of grassland management involving the circulation of livestock over paddocks and the use of fertilizers, though often misunderstood regarding rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific agricultural or grazing system developed by the Hohenheim Institute."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific method of grazing management that experienced failures related to untoward acceleration, leading to attempts to re-divide paddocks through rationing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific method of rational grazing that manages the period of stay and area allocation for livestock to optimize pasture regrowth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific method or system of intensive grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific system of grazing characterized by rotational methods, which the author argues often neglected the laws of rational grazing and the importance of rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific system of grazing management that the author suggests has failures due to the neglect of rational grazing laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific system of pasture management used for dividing paddocks and rationed grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of grassland management that focused on stocking density and seasonal fluctuation but neglected the time factor of rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of grazing management pioneered in Hohenheim that recommends dividing herds into groups to optimize grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of grazing that focuses on stocking density and seasonal fluctuations in grass growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of livestock management and grazing developed by German pioneers, focusing on concepts like stocking density."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of rational grazing that advocates for grazing very young grass."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of rotational grazing developed and tested at the Hohenheim Institute."&lt;SEP&gt;"An old rotational grazing system characterized by the use of 6-9 paddocks and 3 groups, which the author classifies as poor due to long occupation periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hohenheim system is a method of pasture rotation developed by pioneers, which initially failed to recognize the 'time' factor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hohenheim system is a specific method of rotational grazing mentioned as being prone to untoward acceleration due to the reduction of the period of stay."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7501c88b4753d0e36195cd4c777c004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bee7d5fac9dd017be636b45597ba373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35c3962af55711c0635829973feaae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c665e654c8f8cb10f4fdb30c92234e59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27f7fce25d74a4f961f260af1c936fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6a42b8fcc5c0e0603222e6a77532e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4635ce50d45ae30de5b4112d1277975&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15abe44b0e95afa45dd19faa53ac41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3ac60d1b06ce49b0e74445bd5c35d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efe222393fecd71e1d91aa776f41fdc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35c3c9ebeb198810313353b85457c6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b5c4dee5fdcb706e6698994dfba9ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-316166cea4a329a4db2bdc24f524fa03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42a3e63b49bd29b4af01b8a4548a8d8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-583d1c446eecee65cf5a758322efee03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6a574882030ef63f3252a0c0ac0f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 952}]</data>
