      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1886}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KÖNEKAMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A German pioneer of rotation whose work served as a basis for the author's definitions of rational grazing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27f7fce25d74a4f961f260af1c936fff</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1886}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANIMAL UNIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A standardized measure of livestock used to quantify grazing requirements and pasture production, though noted as being inexact."&lt;SEP&gt;"A unit of measurement defined as a bullock or dry cow of 10 cwt (500 kg) live weight, used to simplify calculations in herd grazing productivity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27f7fce25d74a4f961f260af1c936fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 951}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COW-DAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A simplified measurement of pasture productivity based on the number of days a cow can graze on a specific area."&lt;SEP&gt;"A unit of measurement representing the grazing days of animal units, calculated by multiplying the number of animal units by the number of days spent grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A unit of measurement used in the feeding and management of livestock."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27f7fce25d74a4f961f260af1c936fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cd47d3de7f87ca5f9d415c2e16ce46f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 951}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVESTOCK CARRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the number of animals a given area of land can support over a specific period, influenced by rotation periods and soil nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"The number of animal units or total living weight supported on average by a specific unit of land area (e.g., per acre or hectare)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-418420d01189e0b2be4207485e8eabea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 951}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOCKING DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stocking density is a calculated measure used by the founders of rotation to determine the number of livestock units relative to the area of land grazed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stocking density is a static figure representing the amount of livestock per unit of land area."&lt;SEP&gt;"The number of animal units or weight of meat supported by a specific area of a paddock being grazed simultaneously; it is inversely proportional to the number of groups and the area of the paddocks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-42a3e63b49bd29b4af01b8a4548a8d8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 951}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BESATZDICHTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A German term fundamental to the Hohenheim System, translated as 'stocking density' or 'instantaneous livestock carry'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 951}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIOD OF STAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Period of stay is the duration an individual group of livestock spends on a single paddock."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific duration in days or hours that a single group spends grazing a paddock during one rotation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIOD OF OCCUPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Period of occupation is the total duration a paddock is grazed in each rotation, calculated by the period of stay multiplied by the number of groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The total time a paddock is grazed by all groups in a single rotation, equal to the sum of the periods of stay of individual groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659e8a1d0c3ea0d7149e2c946a891e09</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTENSITY OF GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intensity of grazing is a calculated measure defined as the product of stocking density and the period of occupation, measured in cwt./days/acre or kg./days/ha."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intensity of grazing is a unit of measurement that varies proportionally with the period of occupation for a constant stocking density."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0169a1c039e632cea63d0b0e23a7089d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REST PERIOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rest period is the duration between two grazing passages during which grass is allowed to recover without being grazed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c6be08cda7aded7207a29a510cfd328</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BESATZLEISTUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Besatzleistung is a technical unit used in grazing management that accounts for stocking density and time, representing animal units per acre/hectare per day."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0169a1c039e632cea63d0b0e23a7089d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1907}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JUSTUS LIEBIG PRIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Justus Liebig Prize is the highest German scientific distinction awarded to scientists, such as Professor Klapp."</data>
