      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RATIONAL GRAZING PLAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rational grazing plan is a systematic approach to managing pasture resources, focusing on the determination of the number of paddocks to optimize rest periods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0169a1c039e632cea63d0b0e23a7089d</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 987}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAWS OF RATIONAL GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A set of principles and guidelines (including Universal Laws) that govern the timing of stay, occupation, and rest periods to maintain grass health and animal nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"A set of principles or guidelines governing the systematic and efficient management of livestock grazing to optimize grass production and animal health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f09c1defaf6c7013ba4ecd1cac40b5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bee7d5fac9dd017be636b45597ba373</data>
