    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCHUPPLI SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grazing system where cows exclusively eat very young grass (6-7 cm high), which can prevent rumination and lead to health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"A rotational grazing system that was universally recommended but associated with accidents that impeded the development of rational grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific grazing system characterized by short stay periods (e.g., 1 day) for animal groups, categorized as 'perfect' regarding occupation periods but potentially flawed regarding rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific system of grazing mentioned in the context of stock health and the ability of animals to ruminate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific system of rotational grazing referenced as a method for managing grass rest periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Schuppli system is a rotational grazing method involving specific periods of stay, occupation, and rest for paddocks to manage grass growth and animal feeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92e328d3b527b1888b7f5192459a3b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bee7d5fac9dd017be636b45597ba373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7397fa08c6c2db670404830568aebfea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de51cda9d4527990e36f2dadce1bd2c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a162c341c26a72367f6faf337a944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8df78d16e962e8d1ecc294f9d88aaa9</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 963}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSAL LAWS OF RATIONAL GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A set of principles and rules governing the management of grazing to optimize grass rest periods and livestock productivity."</data>
