    <node id="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method of containment using electrified wires, noted for increasing labour requirements when managing multiple herd groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of electrified fences used to manage livestock movement and divide pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system used to control the movement of dairy cattle to ensure even distribution of waste on the field."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system using electric wires to delimit grazing areas for livestock, allowing for movable boundaries to manage grass consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technology used to divide pastures and restrict livestock, enabling the practice of rationed grazing in imitation of tethering."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tool used to delimit grazing areas, which requires precise placement to avoid varying the size of grass blocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electric fencing is a method of dividing pastures into paddocks used in rational grazing to manage stock movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electric fencing is a tool used to arrange the movement of herds and define paddocks in a rational grazing system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electric fencing is a type of fencing used to create divisions within a pasture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c665e654c8f8cb10f4fdb30c92234e59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be12d9958cb9a319997a5bf0e64b56d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d4663e2e3eeb5466a2592bc8824b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3ac60d1b06ce49b0e74445bd5c35d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7397fa08c6c2db670404830568aebfea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76d65cb7a255c82a11696f947cda5684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35c3c9ebeb198810313353b85457c6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418420d01189e0b2be4207485e8eabea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb662dfdbe902c6b759c1dcd149c71a</data>
