    <node id="&quot;AGRARIANISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comprehensive worldview and philosophy that emphasizes the intimate and practical connections between humans and the earth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A set of ideals and views emphasizing that human practice achieves its potential when adaptively responsive to the broader environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and philosophical belief system centered on the value of agrarian lifestyles and the embeddedness of farm households in nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and philosophical belief system that emphasizes the importance of rural life, farming, and the moral value of place-bound community."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and political philosophy centered on the value of agrarian life, often idealized in literature and poetry as a model for virtuous living."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and political philosophy that emphasizes the importance of land ownership and farming as the basis for a virtuous society."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social and political philosophy that presumes farming and ranching have special moral and political significance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social or political movement and philosophical tradition focused on land reform, the cultivation of soil, and the belief that farming shapes moral character."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agrarianism is a social and political philosophy that views farming as an intrinsically valuable way of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a53fa8bfd883994c6d2b9b2bb273da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff197400ac8e94cfb08419bd8a6c660a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c1e39a2b39311bfd6f1c3c05dab313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2658166fe89ce4edb6d09b3e73ec9d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0140bfa459686f6fbd2f146390859bcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cbdcc7923d3d20d9cd83a4cae784b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-947a257970445f551cab2afa22b20c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f55b24ad3e4ece28934dea2092a4f72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1c1d4f15102d0ce3bf4f9a157c71f3</data>
