      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A contemporary environmental philosopher who argues against the dogma of methodological individualism."&lt;SEP&gt;"A critic of the author's work."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scholar who describes the movement of methodological individualism within the social sciences."&lt;SEP&gt;"An academic or author listed in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"An author and researcher who conducted a monumental study of sustainability, recommending that key value decisions be expressed in plain English."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryan Norton is a scholar who describes the movement of methodological individualism and its application to environmental philosophy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryan Norton is a scholar who summarized the distinction between weak sustainability as a commitment to economic growth and strong sustainability as a commitment to maintaining natural resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryan Norton is an author and thinker who argues for focusing on indicators rather than broad definitions or philosophies of sustainability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryan Norton is an author whose book on sustainability introduces the concept of 'wicked problems'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryan Norton is an environmental philosopher who explored 'weak anthropocentrism' in the context of preserving biodiversity."</data>
