    <node id="&quot;THE GRAPES OF WRATH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 1939 novel by John Steinbeck that depicts the struggles of people during the Dust Bowl era."&lt;SEP&gt;"A classic novel written by Steinbeck that depicts the struggles of the Joad family and the American working class during the 1930s."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel by John Steinbeck that depicts the struggles of the Joad family during the Dust Bowl era."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel by John Steinbeck that serves as a case study in social injustice and the economic plight of the Joad family."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel by John Steinbeck that serves as a moral critique of the socioeconomic and ecological conditions during the Dust Bowl."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel by John Steinbeck used as a source for deriving libertarian, egalitarian, and utilitarian lessons."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel by Steinbeck that portrays the migration of the Joad family and the authentic nature of agrarian frameworks."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel written by John Steinbeck depicting the struggles of the Joad family during the Great Depression."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel written by John Steinbeck used to explore the moral significance of land and political philosophies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A novel written by Steinbeck focusing on the experiences of harvest gypsies and the working class."&lt;SEP&gt;"An epic novel of American agriculture published in 1939."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Grapes of Wrath is a novel and subsequent film that probes the internal contradictions of rural life in an industrialized society."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Grapes of Wrath is a novel by John Steinbeck that depicts the struggles of rural Americans during the Great Depression."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Grapes of Wrath is a novel by John Steinbeck that explores the struggles of the Joad family and the conflict between different social classes during the Depression."</data>
