    <node id="&quot;ALBERT BORGMANN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A philosopher whose thought is utilized by Aiden Davison and the author to describe the development of conversations on sustainability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A philosopher whose writings on focal practices are used to articulate agrarian ideals in present-day environmental philosophy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Albert Borgmann is a philosopher known for his view of the 'device paradigm' and the impact of technology on social relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Albert Borgmann is a philosopher who developed the concepts of focal things and focal practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Albert Borgmann is a thinker who writes about the culture of the table and the way technology impacts meaningful human encounters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The philosopher who proposed the 'culture of the table' as a way for Americans to recover moral meaning."</data>
