    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ETHICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A branch of philosophy and social science that studies the moral relationship between humans and the environment, emphasizing nonanthropocentric values."&lt;SEP&gt;"A branch of philosophy that studies the moral relationship of human beings to the environment and its non-human contents."&lt;SEP&gt;"A field of study focused on the moral relationship between humans and the environment, encompassing both ecocentric and anthropocentric perspectives."&lt;SEP&gt;"An academic journal focusing on ethics within the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An area of philosophy that examines the ethical relationship between humans and the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental Ethics is a field of study exploring the moral relationship between humans and the environment, including nonanthropocentric intrinsic value approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental Ethics is the philosophical study of the moral relationship of human beings to the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental ethics is the field of study concerning the moral relationship of human beings to the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental ethics is the field of study exploring the implications of resource sufficiency, functional integrity, and moral obligations to nature."</data>
