    <node id="&quot;ALDO LEOPOLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A founder of present-day environmental philosophy who developed the concept of adaptive management and emphasized the connection between humans and farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldo Leopold is a celebrated figure who advocated for the moral status of land beyond its legal standing as property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldo Leopold is a researcher who recognized the importance of predators, specifically wolves, in maintaining the integrity of wildlife ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldo Leopold is an early environmentalist who helped shape an environmental ethic and the study of ecology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldo Leopold is an environmental philosopher and critic of productivity and efficiency who advocated for the extension of ethics to the land."&lt;SEP&gt;"An environmentalist and philosopher known for his 'land ethic' and warnings about the spiritual dangers of disconnecting from farming."</data>
