    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A farming industry focused on non-GMO crops and natural pest control, currently threatened by GMO contamination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming system that avoids synthetic chemical inputs, though the text notes it can be unsustainable if tillage is regularly practiced."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming system that avoids synthetic fertilizers and pesticides, focusing on organic inputs to boost soil health and food quality."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming system that avoids synthetic pesticides and fertilizers, where ingredients of Api Life are approved for use."&lt;SEP&gt;"A farming system that avoids the use of synthetic fertilizers and toxic chemicals, gaining increased media exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"A low-input alternative to industrialized agriculture focusing on sustainable and natural farming methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method of farming that avoids synthetic fertilizers and pesticides, which the author suggests can be transformed into more sustainable enterprises through soil health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method of farming that emphasizes building humus in the soil, abstaining from toxic chemicals, and mimicking natural biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A system of farming based on biological philosophies, emphasizing soil health, sustainability, and the minimization of nonrenewable inputs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic Agriculture is a holistic approach to farming that emphasizes organic standards and working with the entire system rather than mechanized components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic agriculture is a farming system that avoids the use of synthetic pesticides and chemical fertilizers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic agriculture is a method of farming that Boa distinguishes from his own philosophy of 'working with nature'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic agriculture is the industry and practice of producing food without prohibited synthetic substances, governed by specific labeling and production standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic agriculture refers to low-input alternatives to industrialized farming."</data>
