    <node id="&quot;THOMAS JEFFERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A former president of the United States, politician, and diplomat who expressed a deep passion for market gardening."&lt;SEP&gt;"A founding father of the United States whose agrarianism significantly influenced agricultural policy and philosophy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical figure mentioned as the owner of Monticello."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical figure who designed Monticello to maximize water collection through the use of cisterns and guttered walkways."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical figure whose understanding of the relationship between agriculture and democracy is used as a point of comparison for social goals."&lt;SEP&gt;"An emblematic figure and former U.S. President whose writings and philosophy champion the importance of those who labor in the earth."&lt;SEP&gt;"The designer of the moldboard plow in 1784 and a former U.S. President."&lt;SEP&gt;"The historical figure whose farm book and writings are commented upon by E. M. Betts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The third U.S. President, whose vision of agriculture centers on a rural landscape populated by small-scale farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The third US President whose public land surveys established the rectangular grid pattern of American land ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a Founding Father of the United States, mentioned to emphasize the absurdity of current food laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a founding father of the United States who is quoted regarding the dangers of government and the necessity of the Constitution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure quoted as stating that civilization rests upon the soil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure whose farm journal inspired Brown to explore different agricultural methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is mentioned in the context of home architecture as an example of design that can resist moral commodification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a founding father of the United States and the 'Sage of Monticello,' who viewed farming as a source of moral virtue and a foundation for citizenship and democratic liberty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a historical figure who practiced cover crops and crop rotation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a plantation owner who obsessively researched European farming practices and implemented cover crops at Monticello."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was the president of the United States who promoted agrarianism to ensure the political sustainability of the American republic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df17faa8ab3183c29a4b66fae2714601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fa32270872b031b3439ffee7b8e80ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cb406e891356d1587251b9654548965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5de108a27458ac00232a67eeb238da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1aeb9ecf61216ee718f86040aa4be47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0140bfa459686f6fbd2f146390859bcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d79546c95c1a5631655818b803bd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d23622a472c2e4d3c363267d1723d003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3e7055c35d73ed38d71048f4698efe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e976627ea5fcff24256824faede03467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbee5906ccf87e51970dafe6fdbbc7a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-270e8e189a4efba65e50b1ea16695100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b8e1c006d239029795854fde00ebba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa6c175f37ce7089fa657f33595c666c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81158f16b3cf87e12a53465738040b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a1e22431c1d8795ecb01bd608567b97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-253af24cc5cc2d7d952a8f5e4a183029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89e0c8ba0c6c6bf2f348e4c571b8b7d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2cf80818ad7c91412e85ae6acc7ed17</data>
