    <node id="&quot;THE JOADS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family of rural farmers and displaced migrants during the Great Depression who migrate from the Great Plains to California."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Joad family, characters who transition from land-owning farmers in Oklahoma to itinerant proletarian wage laborers in California."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Joads are a family in Steinbeck's novel who experience the displacement and struggle of the Dust Bowl era."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Joads are the central family in The Grapes of Wrath whose harsh treatment serves as a moral message about the working class."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Joads are the central family in The Grapes of Wrath, representing the rural poor and the agrarian experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central family in The Grapes of Wrath who experience class-consciousness and loss of their land."</data>
