    <node id="&quot;GREAT PLAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broad region in North America characterized by flat land, which was the site of the Dust Bowl."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region of North America that underwent significant agricultural transition and environmental disaster."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region where farmers plowed dry soils, leading to loss of fertility and contributing to the Dust Bowl."&lt;SEP&gt;"A vast prairie region in North America, previously known as the 'Great American Desert', where settlers attempted to cultivate land."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Great Plains is a broad geographic region where Jackson studied undisturbed prairies to develop natural systems agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Great Plains is the broad geographic region of which the 100th meridian marks the edge."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Great Plains is the geographic region where industrial-style farming occurred and where the Dust Bowl ecological disaster took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The region of the United States where the Joads lived and where ecological disasters occurred."</data>
