    <node id="&quot;STEINBECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Author of The Grapes of Wrath who researched harvest gypsies and documented working-class mentality."&lt;SEP&gt;"John Steinbeck, the author of 'The Grapes of Wrath' and 'In Dubious Battle', whose works explore themes of class, agrarianism, and morality."&lt;SEP&gt;"John Steinbeck, the author of 'The Grapes of Wrath' and 'In Dubious Battle'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steinbeck is the author of The Grapes of Wrath, known for his respect for the Okies and his Left-leaning yet anticommunist political views."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steinbeck is the author of The Grapes of Wrath, who used his writing to critique Depression-era capitalism and explore rural life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steinbeck is the author of The Grapes of Wrath, whose work explores social injustice and class conflict."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steinbeck is the author of the novel The Grapes of Wrath and is noted for his portrayal of human drama."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author of 'The Grapes of Wrath' and 'In Dubious Battle' who researched the experiences of Okie refugees and the Dust Bowl."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author of The Grapes of Wrath who perceived the shift toward large-scale monoculture in agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author of The Grapes of Wrath who seems to favor an egalitarian interpretation of social plight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff197400ac8e94cfb08419bd8a6c660a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a488dc13c8287677db8f5b116ebb1a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aefcb893844980b6670c3646efbfb38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4464b8294896264256a3f3b6134be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a35b2a215a1a617e29c8a09335fbef4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98e88e7751e5f203238d792144d7be41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbda84dab68b9c3b861089573a0fbdc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a496eb9c6c8d4c66c22b3ac65fe5b31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98c0d05f4a0ed6c440d52fd2f060cf55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa77f0fb0b764c03a67455a510f03dae</data>
