    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OKIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A term referring to the displaced people from Oklahoma, specifically those migrating to California for work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Migrant workers from Oklahoma who moved to California, characterized by their agrarian ethics and struggles with class conflict."&lt;SEP&gt;"Migrants from the Dust Bowl regions who traveled to California in search of work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Okies are migrants from Oklahoma, often tenant farmers, who moved west during the Depression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Okies are the itinerant migrant workers from Oklahoma depicted in The Grapes of Wrath."&lt;SEP&gt;"Okies refers to the displaced farmers and migrants from Oklahoma and surrounding areas during the Dust Bowl."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Okies are displaced farmers and migrants who interpret the moral significance of place through geographically based reciprocities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ff197400ac8e94cfb08419bd8a6c660a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aefcb893844980b6670c3646efbfb38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4464b8294896264256a3f3b6134be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98e88e7751e5f203238d792144d7be41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbda84dab68b9c3b861089573a0fbdc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a35b2a215a1a617e29c8a09335fbef4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98c0d05f4a0ed6c440d52fd2f060cf55</data>
