    <node id="&quot;DEVICE PARADIGM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A conceptual framework where the world is seen as a collection of devices designed for efficiency and optimization."&lt;SEP&gt;"A philosophical concept by Borgmann describing how technology transforms focal practices into the effortless consumption of goods, removing the need for skill and effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"The device paradigm is a concept proposed by Albert Borgmann regarding how specialized and reliable devices replace the need for integrated human skills."&lt;SEP&gt;"The device paradigm is a technological framework where success is measured by the ability to make goods available without entanglements or nuisances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a05a27b0a2c8f9742e7ba9f368d106d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10cc72332e9d3a585995c00ff0c00c57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6cef65b73cbf090d0f46d890908a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81158f16b3cf87e12a53465738040b4b</data>
