    <node id="&quot;BERRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scholar or thinker who, along with Borgmann and Strong, urges attention to the disappearance of place and the dissolution of community in the context of industrial society."&lt;SEP&gt;"An interpreter of American culture who argues that urban experiences fail to instill virtues like solidarity and self-reliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Berry is an author or thinker whose versions of the rural idyll are discussed in the context of agrarian ideals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Berry, likely Wendell Berry, is an author and proponent of agrarian ideals who emphasizes the value of farming and stewardship of the land."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wendell Berry is an author and thinker whose version of agrarianism focuses on deep moral and philosophical ideals rather than purely political or economic ones."</data>
