    <node id="&quot;AIKEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aiken is a philosopher and author of the essay 'Ethical Issues in Agriculture' who explores the moral obligations of farmers toward nature and the ecosystem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aiken is a scholar or author whose views on profit, subsidies, incentives, and the hierarchy approach to agricultural goals are discussed and contrasted by the narrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aiken is a scholar or philosopher who proposes a rights-based approach to agricultural goals, prioritizing human food needs and environmental safety over private profit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aiken is an individual whose approach to prioritizing agricultural goals is described as powerful and insightful, though limited by a reliance on individual rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aiken is an individual whose comments regarding liberal values and human rights in response to hunger are referenced."</data>
