    <node id="&quot;MODERN AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Modern agriculture is the industrial approach to farming characterized by specialization, which Berry critiques for eroding community and diverse skills."&lt;SEP&gt;"The conventional system of farming characterized by specific myths and practices that the author argues are often unsustainable and lead to land degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry of farming and livestock management, within which the Langstroth hive became a transformative implement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry of farming in the modern era, characterized by the use of plant breeding stations and the challenge of soil impoverishment."</data>
