    <node id="&quot;HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A researcher who conducted pioneering work on scientific aerobic compost, primarily in India during the 1920s and 1930s."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual referenced for his work on scientific composting and biological soil health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is a proponent of soil health and organic farming who believed in the unique association between rhizomes and soil microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is a scientist and farmer who advocated for an integral approach to agriculture, emphasizing the balance between growth and decay and the importance of context over reductionism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is a scientist and researcher who advocated for an integral approach to agriculture, emphasizing the context of the plant, soil, and local community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is an advocate for organic farming who developed techniques for improving soil fertility and viewed soil as a living entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is an individual whose ideas on agriculture were eclipsed by the fertilizer-intensive approach of the Green Revolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard is one of the overseas researchers whose results on waste conversion were studied by Van Vuren."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f41a230435631a03248889184c93b965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79a1a0cb0810e8c4db52132d6d4c6596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b265b8d53df8f70babd69fc84ec3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3b1063c1d500ceacda94be5c1a920e</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 568}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A figure associated with the vision of large-scale nutrient recycling in agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A historical figure whose vision for a farming system involves the recycling of organic wastes and soil health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pioneer of agricultural chemistry whose work 'Chemistry in Its Application to Agriculture' served as a foundation for the science."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scientist and author who advocated for the return of organic matter to soil to maintain fertility and proposed the Law of Compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scientist mentioned as a foundational figure in agricultural chemistry."&lt;SEP&gt;"An author whose 1843 essay highlighted the importance of fertilizers in farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liebig is a scientist whose work on the mineral chemical constituents in the soil focused attention on soil chemistry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liebig refers to Justus von Liebig, a chemist whose views on nutrient transfers and soil fertility are referenced by the author."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liebig was a biologist whose biological theories and quotations were historically used to legitimate scientific agricultural endeavors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liebig was a nineteenth-century figure whose primary targets included the concept of élan vital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liebig was a pioneer in both scientific theory and practice regarding the chemical properties of soil and the development of artificial manures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49fe442094e7ea7c8e57a86dad17be24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75cc73a73aa1db4b46b480931b5836ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-456bc896ed30713380e8b9384c79721c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b994c4aaecb06bda273f0e09161deddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9781b535da0b0987f5145a6a7ffd9b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acedae6125ad11e630130aae1932e3ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b117c84af6b43cb698d268784eb7234e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54ae758c012dc186d43caf6a059360a</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 443}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1613}]</data>
    </node>
