    <node id="&quot;GOVERNMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Administrative bodies that compute the statistical toll of animal disease and seek remedies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Governments are described as conceptual structures and ideas that exist on paper, often preserved at the cost of real-world health and environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Governments are described as organizational structures and concepts that people mistakenly identify as the foundation of their survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Governments are organized forms of collective behavior and social institutions that regulate human behavior and are often subject to reform and modification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organized social entities and human institutions that exercise authority and regulate collective behavior."</data>
