    <node id="&quot;CORPORATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Corporations are described as ideas or concepts around which people and resources are organized, though the author argues they are not 'real things' and can be harmful to the natural world."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corporations are described as organizational structures and concepts that people mistakenly identify as the foundation of their survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corporations are organized social entities and collective behaviors involved in economic activity and the maintenance of social subsystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organized social entities and human institutions focused on economic activity and corporate governance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce80ba3882cb722be4a56897ecdb4355&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737fb05b56336a1f569d769f73394b31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe8805778c266769eb0b693963728ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98ffdda5b456b304e6585d043b124d6</data>
