      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ancient Roman poet who described the mistaken belief that bees were born from rotting meat."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ancient author who described the wax moth as a plague of apiaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"An author mentioned as the writer of the text, contrasting with John Miller."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ancient Roman poet and author of The Georgics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Virgil is a Roman poet who, in his work the Georgics, attributed flood destruction to upland plowing and suggested contour plowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Virgil is a classical poet mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Virgil is an ancient author whose writings about sick bees are quoted in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Virgil is the ancient Roman poet and author of 'The Georgics'."</data>
