    <node id="&quot;LARRY KRAUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beekeeper and associate of John Miller who maintains traditional habits and avoids modern technology like email."&lt;SEP&gt;"A beekeeper described as a very nice person who owns three thousand hives and shares yards with his assistant."&lt;SEP&gt;"A friend of Miller located in Wyoming."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual mentioned as being very nice, as described by John Miller."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larry Krause is a beekeeper from Riverton, WY, who believes honey is the best feed for bees and maintains heavy hives for winter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larry Krause is a migratory beekeeper and a long-time friend of John Miller."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larry Krause is an acquaintance of John Miller whom he meets for dinner in Wyoming."</data>
