    <node id="&quot;IDAHO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A U.S. state known for irrigated valleys where creamy clover honey is harvested."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where beekeepers use potato cellars to store bees for two months."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state known to be inhabited by the phorid fly."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state in the US known for its efficient production of potatoes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state in the USA where Morels were found in the ruins of a house destroyed by fire."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state used as a wintering ground for bees, specifically utilizing climate-controlled potato cellars for dormancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is a U.S. state mentioned as a place where farmers live and seek advice on selling local produce."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is a state bordering Utah where Miller placed some of his hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is the location where Jay managed the beekeeping operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is the location where Miller's bees are kept in potato cellars during their winter quarters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is the state where Miller keeps his bees in cellars during their winter rest before transporting them to California."&lt;SEP&gt;"Idaho is the state where Ryan Elison originally came from before working for Miller."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. state where Miller Honey Farms is based."&lt;SEP&gt;"The US state Miller drove to in 1974 and where he attended several educational institutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The location of Miller's company home base where tracheal mites had not yet been detected."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state where Earl Miller established his beekeeping operation and where the family initially operated."</data>
