    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL VALLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A four-hundred-mile stretch in California between Bakersfield and Red Bluff, uniquely suited for bulk commercial almond cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A geographic region in California where John Miller's property is situated."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California characterized by agricultural activity and subject to various commodity thefts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California known for high-yield almond production and sophisticated agricultural strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California that serves as a massive hub for almond orchards and bee pollination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California where agricultural pesticides are used and almond orchards are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California where farmers have shifted from other crops to planting almonds to maximize profit."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California where thousands of beehives migrate every winter for almond pollination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in California where vast stretches of almond orchards are located and where bees are transferred for pollination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Valley is a region where Miller's wintering grounds are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Valley is a highly productive agricultural region in California known for its almond acreage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Valley is a region in California containing vast almond orchards that rely on commercial pollination."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Valley is a region in California where extensive citrus orchards, including clementines and Murcotts, are planted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Valley is a region in California where vast almond acreage exists and thousands of beehives are transported."</data>
