    <node id="&quot;CCD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CCD (Colony Collapse Disorder) is a phenomenon characterized by the sudden disappearance of worker bees from a colony, causing hive failure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon characterized by the mass disappearance of worker bees and the collapse of honey bee colonies worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon involving the mass disappearance of honey bee populations, which has drawn significant media and scientific attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon where honey bee colonies disappear, the cause of which has been the subject of various scientific theories and studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon where honey bee colonies experience massive die-offs, characterized as a disorder rather than a single disease due to a combination of stress factors, pathogens, and environmental toxins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon where honey bee colonies experience sudden mass disappearances of worker bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is a phenomenon where honey bee populations decline drastically, which has paradoxically improved the public image of bees and provided financial opportunities for the bee industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) refers to the phenomenon of mass honey bee colony deaths, with a significant onslaught noted in 2007."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon affecting bee populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon causing bees to disappear and increasing the demand for replacement queens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon characterized by the disappearance of worker bees from a colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon characterized by the mass disappearance of worker bees in honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon of mass honey bee disappearance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon where bee colonies disappear, making standardized bees more vulnerable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon where honey bee colonies experience sudden population loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon where honey bee populations decline rapidly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, a phenomenon where the majority of worker bees in a colony disappear, causing the colony to collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder, an event appearing around 2006 characterized by intolerable hive losses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colony Collapse Disorder; investigations into this phenomenon have revealed the displacement of N. apis by N. ceranae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de87ea9ee6a2918a9d0691e22c69a3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a697f407a502a7dd40f46f29b9540dbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3b8b4459ac7b875e2ed855774601f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-280e4eba2d5b92ebc5f548d23b3591b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dbdef00cf07d39bd84f0bbdd0936be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53dab54c5e432f26775d35bbbc12efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba112c4310be31fc99e92db5c7bc7f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52fd5c92980e8846f221b5900200a76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d84e8388b1b3835cf15d2729a7bded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24285ce060eba50dee0f1aeb98d3fb26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936929886afd4a64ba379fe6ac052a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad59b3ec786d96ceb0cf84e4d5b8446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c384530d2705c862df0ec1ef11c2d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6deba29b237640ada67472e874a1f037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b56d1daf41a7135af792e5f17f10061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ecb691c2f9f13d9852979644924e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412bb4d9e4870a3cb542b0d1793d0568</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1015}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1911}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICHARD ADEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beekeeper from South Dakota who owns eighty thousand hives, the most in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"A commercial beekeeper who operates on a massive scale with approximately 80,000 hives across multiple states."&lt;SEP&gt;"Richard Adee is the nation's largest beekeeper who initially supported the PPB theory before experiencing significant colony losses himself."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6a3d7885d5c7d0196e5f8b1d626686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936929886afd4a64ba379fe6ac052a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24285ce060eba50dee0f1aeb98d3fb26</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 606}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTH DAKOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A U.S. state mentioned as a comparison point for large-scale farming and the success of conservation agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state mentioned as a place where farmers share commonalities with Costa Rican farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where guiding principles of soil-building farming were applied by Dwayne Beck."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where the Dakota Lakes Research Farm and the town of Platte are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where the farm is located and where the introduction of no-till farming has had a positive community impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where the principles of no-till farming were successfully implemented and transformed agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state used by migratory beekeepers for hive placement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state where the parasitic phorid fly was observed parasitizing honey bees in 2009 and 2010."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the locations where Richard Adee conducts beekeeping operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is a U.S. state mentioned by the author to compare the flatness of the landscape."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is a U.S. state where lessons in pest management are applied and research experiments were conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is a US state mentioned as a region where specific pest management lessons are applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is a US state where conservation agriculture has proven effective on large modern farms."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is one of the locations where Randy Anderson conducted studies on weed pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is the U.S. state where the described farming shifts and the research farm are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"South Dakota is the location where Dwayne Beck's farming operations are situated."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. state where Richard Adee is based."</data>
