    <node id="&quot;GACKLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small town in North Dakota that has seen significant population decline and school consolidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A small, homogenous town in North Dakota characterized as a fading prairie outpost."&lt;SEP&gt;"A town in North Dakota and the site of Miller's summer home for the honey season."&lt;SEP&gt;"A town in North Dakota that served as a prairie depot for railroad customers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A town in North Dakota used as a reference point for Miller's summer bee locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gackle is a rural community in North Dakota suffering from the decline of the agricultural economy and loss of its youth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gackle is a small town in North Dakota, known as a duck hunting capital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gackle is a town that serves as a setting for the narrative, described as a testament to persistence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gackle is the town or area where Miller's honey house is located and where the narrative events take place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The place Miller departed from in 1974 after an arduous summer."</data>
