    <node id="&quot;N. E. MILLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A beekeeper described as an obsessive type and the ancestor of John Miller."&lt;SEP&gt;"An apiarist who maintained detailed records of bee-yard success, although his tendency to remove failing yards created a lack of control groups for scientists."&lt;SEP&gt;"N. E. Miller is a beekeeper who first wintered his bees in the California citrus belt."&lt;SEP&gt;"N. E. Miller is a seasoned beekeeper and businessman who manages a California operation and is known for his wit and enthusiasm for agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"N. E. Miller was a pioneer in industrial migratory beekeeping who managed thousands of hives and developed large-scale interstate movement of bees via rail."&lt;SEP&gt;"N. E. Miller, also referred to as Nephi, is John Miller's great-grandfather who ushered in the industrial revolution of beekeeping."</data>
