      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A U.S. state containing the Olympic National Park and the Upper Elwa River Valley."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state home to a massive Armillaria ostoyae colony and the Snoqualmie Forest."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where municipal compost was found to be widely contaminated by the herbicide clopyralid."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where mushroom analyses were conducted, including the Olympic Peninsula."&lt;SEP&gt;"A U.S. state where northwestern fireweed honey is highly coveted."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state used by migratory beekeepers for hive placement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state where a colony of Honey mushrooms is cited for destroying thousands of acres of conifers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state where apples are grown optimally for efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"A US state where the parasitic phorid fly was observed parasitizing honey bees in 2012."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where Miller sent bees for apple pollination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in the western United States where the Black Morel (Morchella angusticeps) is endemic."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state in North America where the Red alder tree is common and used for mushroom cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A state in the US mentioned as a location where Douglas fir forests provide a natural example of mushroom polyculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington State is a U.S. state located across the border from British Columbia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington State is a U.S. state where the narrator conducted a seminar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington State is a location in the US where the author searched for mushrooms and where Paul Stamets collected new strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington state is a location where bees are sent to pollinate apple orchards."</data>
