    <node id="&quot;HOOPHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hoophouse is a farming structure used to extend the growing season by protecting plants from cold weather."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hoophouse is a modern eco-techno architectural design consisting of bent pipes acting as arches covered in plastic to trap heat."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hoophouse is a structure used for hardening off plants, providing a transitional environment with roll-up sides to expose plants to sunlight and wind."&lt;SEP&gt;"A low inner tunnel of wire hoops and row cover used to protect cold-tolerant crops, increase yield and quality, and extend the growing season."&lt;SEP&gt;"A simple greenhouse structure used to extend the growing season and improve crop yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"A simple, low-cost structure made of hoops and plastic used to house kitchens or plants without requiring building permits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structure consisting of arches covered with a skin, used for housing animals or growing plants; can be referred to as tall tunnels or greenhouses depending on heating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as a high tunnel, this is an unheated structure erected in the field to extend the growing season and protect crops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5399890419cd7e402f5e411514ee3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dce82d196594b7d4ed0c72afe727f4be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5077481d5cb91c7d0b17451ff87c351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679416bb166ca53a86b2b2f4dbcf7deb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e929a727edf557065879c8f5b9dc9020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-356cb9d53fad80b6e9eefed8d2216eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ea57df04e61e758719d06787adec63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8f79af241970eb67f1ac2fa37905aae</data>
