    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC MOVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A social and agricultural movement based on Howard's thought, aiming to improve crop health and oppose industrial gigantism."&lt;SEP&gt;"A socio-economic shift emphasizing quality over quantity and alternative business models to conventional mass-market practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The organic movement is a social and philosophical approach to agriculture and living that emphasizes respect for nature's biological processes."</data>
