    <node id="&quot;PUSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A center located in Bihar and Orissa used for agricultural experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where outdoor tomato growing was carried out."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where the author conducted studies on fruit crops and tobacco between 1905 and 1923."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where the author managed a large fruit plantation for nineteen years and conducted research on peaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neighborhood in North Bihar where specific soil conditions and vegetation lead to alkali patches."&lt;SEP&gt;"A place where the author farmed land for twenty years and observed the early stages of alkali production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location characterized by intermingled wheat and rice tracts and damp soil and atmospheric conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location in Bengal, India, where the Agricultural Research Institute was established."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location in India where agricultural research on wheat was conducted and where the Agricultural Research Institute is based."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location where agricultural research on soil conditions and crop diseases, specifically regarding vetch, was conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location where the author conducted experiments with working oxen, featuring common pastures and a cattle estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a location, likely an agricultural research station, where studies on peaches, guavas, and bananas were conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is a research institute organized into specialized compartments like plant breeding and agricultural chemistry, characterized by a rigid administrative structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pusa is the location of a small farmyard and a larger estate where the author observed the effects of foot-and-mouth disease on oxen."</data>
