    <node id="&quot;INDORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A city and region in Central India where the author managed land and oxen and where an Institute is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"A city in Central India where the Institute of Plant Industry is located and where significant cotton research was conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"A city in Central India, home to the Institute of Plant Industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location in India where efforts to accelerate the manufacture of humus were taken and where the Indore Process was developed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location in India where the author grew excellent crops of cane and converted them into crude sugar using specific soil methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where the author conducted work on leguminous crops and soil conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is a location in Central India where the author repeated experiments on disease resistance in oxen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is a location where the Shahjahanpur cultivation results were repeated and tested on black soils."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is a location where the author moved to and conducted further experiments on soil fertility and animal health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is a location where various agricultural observations on gram and san hemp were made regarding soil and disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is the location of the Institute of Plant Industry where the author managed 300 acres of land for agricultural experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indore is the location where the original experiments regarding the composting process were conducted."</data>
