    <node id="&quot;NATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scientific journal that published a 2015 paper estimating the impact of fossil fuel reserves on the world's climate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scientific journal that published records of the mycorrhizal relationship in Egypt."&lt;SEP&gt;"A weekly international scientific journal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is a prestigious international scientific journal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is a scientific journal that published a 2014 paper/meta-analysis on conservation agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is a scientific journal that published a 2015 paper estimating the fossil fuel reserves that must remain unused to limit climate change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is described as a systemic force characterized by stability, precise timing, and the maintenance of enormous reserves to ensure the continuity of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is personified as a farmer who arranges the creation of humus and manages the 'Law of Return' to maintain soil fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is personified as the 'supreme farmer' and the manager of the universe, responsible for balancing growth and decay through agricultural operations and the Wheel of Life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is personified as the system responsible for maintaining the earth's surface fertility through natural regeneration and mineral circulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature is portrayed as the supreme farmer and the source of natural laws and cycles that govern growth and decay, which human agricultural practices must respect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personified as 'the supreme farmer' who manages the kingdom of life and conducts agricultural operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The natural world and its inherent biological processes and cycles of growth and decay."&lt;SEP&gt;"The physical world and its biological processes, described as the force that initiates the creation of humus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The physical world and its biological processes, viewed as the provider of surpluses and the entity that imposes laws and limits on farming."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a50a07328bb0a1a78dc4b1422311f893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff493a2aa6061d02c444386e37f3a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b6f8bdb7d910bab994c57a8e47dd2c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f583a53a338f37e2fd8d21aeb1478f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78cd230da4011941db03f3bf1f0a18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6795ac13deea0240f9376837154726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad44bd47e01a1d6bfb342156af1965f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550966fca0f2f090187553fe9bc99e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff6fbf3f5ff09df476cd44ec19e3d67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcd140f4d99d1b2503c614d0206518dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5753cf47228cedb4b58dfbff8318e398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cbbf08936e127d696a15794ccea1707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-571b3fa101d4bb8e213e6691eda956ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe735eff1ddb5f51823657c9cb6e03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d184d39c4fc61b176c219e8852dce</data>
