    <node id="&quot;NPK MENTALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scientific approach to agriculture focused on the three primary nutrients: Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NPK mentality refers to a specific mindset or attitude in agriculture that prioritizes the use of nitrogen, potassium, and phosphorus artificials over other soil considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NPK mentality refers to a traditional chemical approach to fertilization focusing on Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium, which Dymond seeks to move beyond in favor of biological methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NPK mentality refers to the mindset centered on the use of Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium chemical fertilizers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f54ae758c012dc186d43caf6a059360a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bde3a9925e013ce4a55dadba03682d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ac72dfa70392b35da5b9538cf9d2202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6308a55dba63b8652c56c1424f2ab3b6</data>
