    <node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL MANURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical fertilizers used in farming practices which, according to the text, can lead to the destruction of humic cement and soil degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical fertilizers used in farming, noted for reducing the lifespan of wheat straw thatch compared to organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical fertilizers used to stimulate crop growth, which the author claims lead to long-term soil degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemical-based fertilizers used as substitutes for organic manurial rights, described by the author as ephemeral and harmful."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inorganic fertilizers used to supplement soil nutrients, the use of which is the central subject of the debate in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Man-made fertilizers used in modern agriculture, associated by the author with a phenomenon of declining agricultural health."</data>
