    <node id="&quot;MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A government agency that provides guidelines and recipes for making manure and bokashi for farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government body involved in agricultural oversight and discussion on plant diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government body involved in agricultural policy and associated with the disciples of Rothamsted."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government body responsible for overseeing agricultural practices and providing support to farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government body where Felicia Echeverría led the organic program from 1999 to 2006."&lt;SEP&gt;"A government department that generally promotes conventional chemical farming methods to farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ministry of Agriculture is the government body responsible for agricultural policy, including the grow-more-food campaign."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ministry of Agriculture is the government body that inaugurated the first Accredited Milk Scheme to improve the nation's milk supply."&lt;SEP&gt;"The government body responsible for directing war farming and promoting the use of artificial fertilizers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The government department responsible for agricultural policy in Great Britain, advocating for the use of artificial manures."</data>
