    <node id="&quot;AFRICANIZED HONEY BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bee characterized by aggressive defensive behavior, originating from African bees brought to Brazil in the 1950s and spreading through Central America to the southern United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hybrid honey bee known for a higher tendency to swarm and a degree of resistance to varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hybrid honey bee known for being more aggressive, making the low-disturbance design of the top bar hive particularly advantageous."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hybrid honey bee known for natural genetic resistance to mites and a more aggressive nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"A subspecies of honey bee (Apis scutellata) characterized as a warm-weather cousin to the European honey bee, lacking the same cold-weather survival mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as A. mellifera scutellata, a bee species that combats varroa mites through biting and shortened pupation periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as AHB or 'killer bee,' this is a strain of honey bee known for its aggressive defensive nature, originating from African queens imported to Brazil."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fcbe54cf1d72b0c107b42a5d283af2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e31a42be32b10fec891321276eff3bb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6246333458a48f952d940bddf47976a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b9c3131c2e6763d0e21d39ae068acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35f6eef0d2ff08b3a3b7b2c2e942edde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-027615784640b56f822e7f3e6ed8eb5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13bef129d93b5a27e008dbee0931310</data>
