    <node id="&quot;TOP BAR HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hive that uses top bars instead of full frames, allowing bees to build comb naturally."&lt;SEP&gt;"A horizontal hive design where bees build comb freely from top bars, popular among backyard beekeepers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of beehive design characterized by horizontal bars that encourage bees to build natural comb."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific type of beehive design that helps city beekeepers reduce visibility and protect the colony from vandals and thieves."&lt;SEP&gt;"A style of beehive that uses horizontal bars for bees to build combs, rather than rectangular frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of beehive that utilizes top bars instead of frames to support the comb."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also referred to as TBH or KTBH, it is a horizontal beehive design characterized by removable top bars, requiring minimal materials and tools, and widely used in rural Africa and urban settings."</data>
