    <node id="&quot;VARROA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A parasitic mite from Asia that attacks European honey bee colonies and transmits viruses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A parasitic mite that affects honey bee colonies, mentioned as a factor in the evolution of hive management programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A parasitic mite that attacks honey bees and causes significant colony stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"A parasitic mite that has overshadowed American foulbrood in recent years."&lt;SEP&gt;"A parasitic mite that infests honey bee colonies, whose population growth is linked to the developmental time of bee larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of parasitic mite that affects honey bee colonies, which the sticky trap is designed to control."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of parasitic mite that infests honey bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a type of mite that causes damage to bee hives and is the target of various treatments described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa mites are parasitic mites that infest honey bee colonies and can lead to hive collapse if not managed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa refers to the parasitic mites that infest honey bee colonies, which the text describes methods for monitoring and counting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086256446757da0fffa536b4247d998d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29145fee1938f274aaef2d5bd61453f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-528607c392c3ac867f863732d8ba5821&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4675cad2098c6c5be67a3bdcf6e32e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b9c3131c2e6763d0e21d39ae068acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8953187d0b7dfcfd8123496f550e9191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad59b3ec786d96ceb0cf84e4d5b8446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39baafb5b073ac43e9932248ea8ca932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58512ee8d1c43dccf19e6d73e944fd38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1514064bbd0a8e145cda20ebb9ecab</data>
