    <node id="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cultivation medium where fungi are grown on grains to be used as an inoculum for substrates, providing a nutritional base that improves yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fungal culture grown on grain, used as the inoculant to seed sawdust bags for mushroom cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medium, typically cereal grains, inoculated with mushroom mycelium used to expand the culture for larger substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medium-priority stage of mycelial expansion, organized by generation and incubated in jars."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method of mushroom cultivation where grains serve as the vehicle for mycelium, used for direct inoculation or as a precursor to sawdust spawn."&lt;SEP&gt;"A substrate consisting of sterilized grains inoculated with mycelium, used to expand the fungal culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grain spawn is a method of using grain as a carrier medium for mycelium to be transplanted into substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sterilized grain inoculated with mycelium, used to expand cultures and inoculate substrates like straw or sawdust."&lt;SEP&gt;"The fungal starter used to inoculate the pasteurized straw substrate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c8c8ff82911884af1d7f6dd1d5a5310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1ef2ff91f86f93c8d85ce6a2b3161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d8ffd59b496178c8be531ac64f1a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a15c712ab4cd262f392a9cd9ec6621d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99b3c5799adf4153f31a635e31e46c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee67735ee2d22fc01623c11e43940a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e12830990f7ea8d716253d971a2d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
