      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A researcher who conducted a study in 1976 regarding the liberation of carbon dioxide during the decomposition of wheat straw by Oyster mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who demonstrated in 1976 that a significant portion of wheat straw mass evolves into carbon dioxide during Oyster mushroom production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who noted that mycelial growth of P. ostreatus peaks at specific CO2 levels in 1974."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who noted the ability of certain mushrooms to render straw into nutritious feed for ruminants in 1979."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual who references Vasilkov's naming of a specific mushroom."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual whose 1976 work provided data on the by-products generated by Oyster mycelium's decomposition of wheat straw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zadrazil is a researcher cited in the context of checking the synonymy of Pleurotus eous and P. djamor in 1993."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zadrazil is a researcher who, in 1974, demonstrated that mycelial growth peaks at specific carbon dioxide levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zadrazil is an author/researcher cited for providing more information on cultivation and contamination."</data>
