      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound used as a disinfectant for washing hands in a laboratory setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical compound used as a disinfectant to wipe the hands of the inoculator to maintain sterility."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemical solution used as a disinfectant in aerosol sprays to maintain laboratory cleanliness."&lt;SEP&gt;"A disinfectant used by the inoculator to wipe their hands frequently to maintain sterility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as 80% rubbing alcohol, used as a sterilizing agent for hands and equipment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as isopropyl alcohol, a chemical compound used as a disinfectant to clean tabletops before pouring agar media."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as rubbing alcohol, it is used for disinfecting hands and surfaces in the laboratory to maintain sterility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as rubbing alcohol, it is used for wiping countertops, hands, and sterilizing tools."&lt;SEP&gt;"Isopropanol, or rubbing alcohol, is used as a cleaning agent to sterilize glass surfaces for spore collection."</data>
