    <node id="&quot;MAITAKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gourmet and medicinal mushroom, also known as Grifola frondosa, sold as fresh mushrooms, dried mushrooms, tablets, and teas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mushroom also known as the 'Dancing Mushroom', synonymous with Grifola frondosa, associated with a fable about inducing frenzied dancing in nuns and woodcutters."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom cultivated using specific inoculation paths involving sawdust and grain spawn."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom grown in production blocks that can be implanted outdoors for additional fruitings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom that consumes supplemented sawdust, triggering exothermic reactions during incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom used in cultivation and production."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of edible mushroom cultivated using resterilized Shiitake substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of medicinal mushroom known for antiviral and immunopotentiating properties, typically fruiting in the fall and cultivated on hardwood substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom (Grifola frondosa) that requires specific environmental controls, attention to detail, and a unique growing room for successful cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom cultivated using various hardwoods, including oak."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom noted for having numerous studies on its medicinal properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of polypore mushroom known scientifically as Grifola frondosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"A wood-loving mushroom species (Grifola frondosa) cultivated using a specific sawdust/bran formula."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as Grifola frondosa, a fleshy polypore mushroom used as a comparison for cultivation methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as Grifola frondosa, a mushroom whose mycelium on grain smells like day-old, cold corn tortillas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as Grifola frondosa, a mushroom with similar growth parameters to Sparassis crispa that can be co-cultivated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grifola frondosa, a gourmet and medicinal mushroom grown on wood substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake (Grifola frondosa&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake (Grifola frondosa) is a medicinal and edible mushroom known for its polysaccharides, specifically the D-fraction, and its various health benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a type of gourmet or medicinal mushroom."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Japanese name for Grifola frondosa, recognized for its gourmet and medicinal properties."</data>
