    <node id="&quot;LAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A principal investigator and president of the International Union of Soil Sciences who conducts research on soil carbon sequestration and no-till farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"A researcher who provides conservative estimates of soil carbon sequestration potential based on the assumption that levels cannot exceed native ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is a scientist and researcher who conducted extensive experiments on soil erosion and conservation agriculture in Africa and other tropical regions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is a soil scientist who discovered that no-till farming and the use of mulch prevent soil erosion and maintain soil fertility in the tropics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is an expert whose message emphasizes that farming practices and soil quality are as important as agricultural technology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is an expert/researcher who advocates for conservation agriculture and discusses soil degradation and sustainable soil management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is an individual accompanying the narrator who visits Brandt's farm to observe his agricultural practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lal is an individual who accompanies the narrator and asks Brandt questions about his farming practices."</data>
