    <node id="&quot;BECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Ph.D. researcher and research manager at Dakota Lakes Research Farm who developed and promoted no-till farming systems to improve soil biology and economic viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agricultural researcher and farm manager who prioritizes farmer-benefitting research and advocates for no-till farming and soil health."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual associated with the principles of conservation agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual mentioned by the author as having a similar 'farmer to farmer' approach to agricultural education."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is a Ph.D. researcher and farmer who advocates for and implements no-till farming systems and zero-net-energy infrastructure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an agricultural expert and farmer who advocates for crop rotation and cover crops to manage weeds and soil health, and conducted field trials to prove herbicide resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an agricultural expert or farmer who advocates for complex crop rotations and biological pest control over the use of pesticides."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an agricultural expert or farmer who advocates for complex crop rotations and no-till farming to increase yields and reduce environmental damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an expert or advocate for no-till farming and soil conservation who influenced Mike and Monty Cronin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an expert or educator on sustainable farming practices who demonstrates the benefits of no-till agriculture and nitrogen management to students."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beck is an individual who advocates for and practices conservation agriculture, specifically no-till farming, cover crops, and crop rotations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dwayne Beck is a farmer whose approach to no-till, cover crops, and diverse rotations serves as a model and point of comparison for Boa's methods."</data>
