    <node id="&quot;BOA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Also referred to as Kofi Boa, he is a proponent and 'prophet' of no-till farming in Ghana, advocating for conservation agriculture to combat hunger and poverty."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual associated with the principles of conservation agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa is a farmer and educator who promotes low-input, nature-based agricultural practices, focusing on cover crops and minimal soil disturbance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa is a naturally gifted teacher and farmer who advocates for low-input, nature-based agriculture and instructs others on weed control and crop rotation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa is a practitioner and educator who promotes no-till farming and organic soil management to improve soil organic matter and reduce fertilizer use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa is an expert and advocate for no-till farming who guides the narrator through various fields and runs the No-Till Center."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa is an expert or educator who instructs students on conservation agriculture, emphasizing sustainable farming techniques and the restoration of soil organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boa, also known as 'Mr. Mulch', is a farmer and educator who established the No-till Center to promote conservation agriculture, soil health, and food security in Africa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77cfc24323ad9f95c28062b00cb60101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e21be11265296d18e2a7632e5e359e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ff78a393ff1a0888c9e615bbd889db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5244a72295d4f84fc85246a4eb4df315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d827b4b169dc20f345800758c486eb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6999c1ead4c12e4056d420abe0a419bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6c7b5a78bab1ad1dda59f93699b5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9aa3a35ab2b80b18d7eb59a93eb1c07</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 546}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1795}, {"level": 4, "cluster": 2096}]</data>
    </node>
