    <node id="&quot;FOOD POLICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A colloquial term used by the author to describe government regulatory agencies responsible for food safety and enforcement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A metaphorical term used by the author to describe government regulators and inspectors who enforce food safety laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"A term used by Joel Salatin to describe government inspectors who harass small-scale food producers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'food police' is the narrator's term for health department officials and government inspectors who enforce food safety regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The food police refers to the government regulatory agencies tasked with enforcing food safety and production laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"The food police refers to the regulatory agencies and inspectors responsible for enforcing food safety protocols."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-151e12b25a4e3b90360a667161585b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7479ce6c439a8dad27fa65453b6fb717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c91bc35d36c8498b9d61a9d491bf15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65953ac0df3c024d00056d147d289531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eabfcf3f16934075b028cdd31a4a8e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d628ebc9fbc7db25894f19c606113e6</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 150}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 803}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL FOOD SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The industrial food system is a large-scale, commercialized method of food production characterized by factory farms, vaccinations, and centralized distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is characterized by large-scale food production that relies on sterilization and zero-tolerance policies to manage bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is described as an energy-hogging network where food travels long distances, which the author advocates replacing with local gardening."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is the large-scale commercial infrastructure of food production, characterized by the author as opposing small-scale, local food initiatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is the large-scale, conventional method of food production characterized by confinement, chemical use, and centralized distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is the large-scale, corporate-driven method of food production that often separates the consumer from the farmer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industrial food system is the large-scale, factory-based method of food production characterized by sterilization and standardized protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large-scale infrastructure and network of companies that produce, process, and distribute food, often using unnatural substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large-scale, complex network of production and distribution that drives food availability, characterized by economies of scale and sophisticated networking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-151e12b25a4e3b90360a667161585b36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b092b362831dceef318ecd8875fd262d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22f3967d311f087b86fc91bd0708142c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4941781303f19e745042aad2237f81ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c9172daf9801bd62c5822cc8c36ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919f42e3dd377019c4cd2c5bd0dc31ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659bb35c94ac64eb362d6537bc347e37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ee13c5b268bc457eb5f60d71cda15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1c7e1b601a6b8a0deb46da88c1a33b6</data>
