    <node id="&quot;ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Asia is a continent characterized by a diverse ecological and agricultural landscape, though it faces significant environmental challenges, including forests experiencing ecological decline and immense plains with lakes that are dying due to intense oxygen starvation. In terms of agriculture, Asia has a long-standing tradition of returning manure and night soil to fields, though the adoption of conservation agriculture—which accounts for only a few percent of cropland—is often hampered by the use of animal dung for fuel and the removal of crop residues. The region is also noted for its use of low-input, resource-conserving practices, crop rotations, and nutrient recycling of organic matter.

The continent has a rich history of mycology and mushroom cultivation. Asia is home to mycophilic societies and a long tradition of marketing gourmet mushrooms. Specific species such as the Paddy Straw Mushroom, the Golden Oyster mushroom (discovered by Singer), and *Pleurotus abalonus* are commercially cultivated or highly popular. Shiitake mushrooms have been grown on logs in temperate mountainous regions for over a thousand years, and dried Shiitake are highly valued. Additionally, *A. auricula* (Wood Ears) is collected from the wild and grown using various cultivation techniques, while *G. lucidum* and *G. japonicum* are valued and cultivated using methods such as cylindrical bags. The region's subtropical areas are particularly well-suited for open-air, netted growing rooms. Other notable fungi include *H. tessulatus*, distributed throughout temperate hardwood forests, *H. sublateritium* (found in temperate regions including Japan and Korea), and the use of Krestin as an approved anticancer drug.

In the realm of apiculture, Asia is a region where honey bees spread naturally and migrated, and where the descendants of honey hunters maintain their traditions. However, beekeepers face challenges from birds such as bee-eaters and honeyguides. Asia is also the region where Varroa mites were endemic and coevolved with Asian honey bees, and it served as the location where Anderson collected mite samples.

Beyond agriculture and biology, Asia is noted for the long-standing use of mushrooms as medicine and is a region where culture banks utilize specific methods of preserving cultures in straight test tubes. Historically, the continent was also the site of food riots in 2008.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ad03c75085e62d4cf641ff00f56a870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01d793c2dc61cc5608f3044cefea7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920c2b8a5eaf89205bbce9d1db91bfac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817bac06738b1392b1904426ad3a9798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf19c04e874b6deb92ca7f0145054be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d184d39c4fc61b176c219e8852dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aa9e3a4728dc666c9af9ca8874591f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1308290a383b7cf6cad5084748151135&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf6ea422300d7cce3d594e740c6f1f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503fd9df081d23d8ec7105a0dfdec72c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33ea2f9846e58f5947feff6e3a84d189&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5711a5f5dfd11e4a830061fafb1909d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f7e3ba7786fba28e5d662f74af986c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8f4ced19f39489760889dcf78f83b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00ca524316427ad52b01cb6871e49060&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cf015c914ceeb12acc1a5f9c6773a85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da657fc11e9f746515ea884faf190105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5222544fbac611153c3910b7a49b1632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a11bfe1dc62c3ee867b5e29138914b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb886065fde7376bc6f30e23079e875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dce32ddceff9da5a8dff8d861090706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a529b2a82aeedaec884d490e181507e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9373ee84b3a77eb37578d5b0a36a9135&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74cd72bbc78235ee2cc27e78214fb076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7b50e88ceffec311ad8345ea78ee7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800e0b66b56649c0bb08b5036495f580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc2a2ad2b38fdda540087364d1c8ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54338209a610084057de4fde840e5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e69dee1c96e41bfd054cbe43266a769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4455bd7c30235e62c66747849070cfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89313a604603d854506a3dd824a4a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e823f4271cc674d258a850b82bd8b70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5753cf47228cedb4b58dfbff8318e398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-096e2f877b1d380c9b6ee623940df75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74c9c00fc19895ed849661987adee4cb</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1087}]</data>
