    <node id="&quot;MILLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">John Miller is a professional commercial beekeeper and business owner who manages a large-scale honey-producing operation, overseeing thousands of hives across North Dakota and Idaho. A descendant of Nephi Ephraim Miller, John Miller is a central figure in the provided text, serving as both a protagonist and a primary subject of study. His operation is highly migratory; he coordinates the transport of bees via various railcar methods and trucks—surviving a major truck accident in the process—to move hives to California for almond pollination. He manages the complexities of the almond boom's economics and employs crews, including South African workers such as Wessel and Jaco, to maintain hives and operate his honey house.

As an expert in his field, Miller is deeply knowledgeable about honey varietals, moisture content, and taste profiles, and he maintains a strong commitment to honey purity, expressing frustration over the presence of adulterated honey in bargain stores. Beyond production, he is a dedicated researcher and experimenter. He utilizes a "Frankenstein yard" to test miticides and treatments, having employed Apistan strips and extreme vigilance to combat varroa mites. He has faced significant challenges, including the loss of hives to Nosema ceranae in 2008 and the effects of IAPV. Miller is a proponent of the "death-by-a-thousand-paper-cuts theory," suggesting that Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) is caused by an accumulation of multiple stressors.

In his business practices, Miller focuses on genetic continuity by purchasing thousands of queen cells annually from Heitkam to mate with his own drones. He also implements security measures, such as branding, to protect his equipment and has a personal history of recovering stolen hives with his father in California. Despite his professional success and pride in managing ten thousand hives, he has experienced periods of restlessness in his youth and currently balances the financial struggles of the industry with a romantic passion for beekeeping. While he oversees a sophisticated operation and a "man cave" at his unpretentious home, he remains a mentor who observes new beekeepers to assess their temperament for the work.

Additionally, the name Miller is associated with other distinct roles: a researcher involved in naming the species *P. populinus* and substrate buffer research, an author of a 1969 publication on mushroom cultivation, and a chef who collaborated with Molovinsky to reengineer a menu using local meats.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3ab2196ed3cfc357ea2968eacf70e5cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67da272e0cf77b7a72954b23074375bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911d39a734ce63729ca31ddecfbbdb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2f9bf7db953b160f0ff4e9bdf3bd0c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47bc4d6bb9b54f7a4498039a09e27192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdea054bc69c6e9c8b52cea9b454cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-688342abe8464e36fad009bdc5a7a22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e6144bc70a4f4cbdf43cfe854a269e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7acff18895bfa08e6388fc660689bad7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6b42805d670ff5f1b75194ea815c5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dac5e0fc4b3efb7d62d286bfe82fe84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f2377f0cd08c77c000df20f4ac40c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-280e4eba2d5b92ebc5f548d23b3591b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75673023cb192cee1fbe66473e0ff86d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b198fa71b44d8dd33dcfc2eb267be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-875244dbf5b92a0cbabb5deff3c5629e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b0512dda0784c4b872422e6d8bd9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a019e529b263129037d3a41686a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e3bb2a40d743661733d6555e921ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b1d9cb4feb594eafc5f44559345e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5711a5f5dfd11e4a830061fafb1909d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ca6ad40e2f56cfc0ab67f96d1552b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53dab54c5e432f26775d35bbbc12efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e647f4fae9bf23b96a7c260839df22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-944c5b4df7883966aee796898bc6c38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5886c64a8eabfd9136afefc941f06b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52fd5c92980e8846f221b5900200a76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d84e8388b1b3835cf15d2729a7bded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6595de7e08679e25db37588321f5c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb886065fde7376bc6f30e23079e875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1f94cc5f14959e322093167c5b5ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24285ce060eba50dee0f1aeb98d3fb26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85eaeec0849996dd41a39cefe3eb69e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936929886afd4a64ba379fe6ac052a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d288912e79b43bbf8f55e37e96c89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceb6afb7b86fd8dee5d1ffc49066a3be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69a6f293580aa424d04ad67558a1427b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d8286e6a8f25ded00034a7a287f09cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b59d57778c2109af21150bee2b7208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0702b35ab5da980ccafcd8b491aa1562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd6250bf9119073ff90517ec6a09534&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13d75b31628c95bce2d1de33c7d05683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8422f27b6e2f7c49af2d7c0895af1179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464158e8ae6f11d3eade0bd5a72fca55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcdd66d1199b5aa96f04600977274c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9eafb5519ae847ebc95f1b6bd7a3901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788901d0b4d29c039e6a86eed1ac4b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1bab4a72f46eead5c78b6d5b292d2ef</data>
