    <node id="&quot;AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">America, primarily referring to the United States, is presented as a complex geographic and political entity defined by a historical tension between an egalitarian agrarian vision and an industrial economy. Historically characterized as a land of opportunity for immigrants, artisans, and farmers, the nation was shaped by fertile lands and foundational events such as the Boston Tea Party and the Homestead Act. However, the text notes a significant cultural shift around 1910 from an agrarian society to an industrial one, moving toward a commodified twenty-first-century world where the landscape is increasingly defined by fast food and a "playground" mentality focused on recreation, lawns, and horse facilities.

In terms of agriculture and environment, America is a location where European drainage mentalities were applied to diverse environments and where sustainable farmers currently employ multiyear rotations and rotational grazing, drawing on the work of Voisin. While the country has a history of widespread backyard gardening—notably in 1946—the current food system is criticized for the vast distances food travels from farm to consumer, a lack of food choice, and the prevalence of manure as a top pollutant. Despite this, a grassroots local food revolution is spreading, supported by initiatives like FoodCorps and individuals like Allison Sosna, who seek to integrate socially responsible work with food production.

The nation's regulatory and social environment is described as litigious, characterized by legal blackmail, government manipulation of the marketplace, and restrictive food safety regulations. The author highlights issues regarding taxation, government control, and the social axioms of corporate ladders and family sacrifice. Furthermore, America's global influence is noted through its food and agriculture aid policies affecting African food systems, as well as its military actions and energy policies aimed at securing oil.

Ecologically, America (and the broader North American continent) faces significant challenges. The honey bee species *Apis mellifera*, introduced in the 1620s, currently faces unprecedented threats, including colony stress and Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD), with climate patterns in the Northeast specifically affecting winter survival. Additionally, the region is noted for its forests and ecological resources, as well as historical events such as the Spanish flu following World War I. Ultimately, the text explores the potential for a "New America" that returns to sustainable land management, such as implementing perennial grain crops and utilizing lawns and paddocks for produce.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-910a5a0e2e0272eebc02ca3ea30cdeb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2f3cf7878919c86769d45741d13fa4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebf6866ed6ad144c3c4b844913be03e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c46a7f814f9b988da76a9ac71bdab30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ffdb0c84602631ea1239c5c98fe486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9b2fa060b49dfcd9523440966c974ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5f192ebac2944968cd0ca9275cc34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0707af73cf1b7f988c4cf8ff24fb2972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099841c9e59bebef5ddbb5acdb1e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7ee13c5b268bc457eb5f60d71cda15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cee44e954d1abb009f061fd993b844c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79fcf59d7b63a10ed28124a2923fc0f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a140060d3e3d6e8b8621035f57c83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ba9b55dcb2de76a73fed895734246f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d86135a3ecce951cb211b81554dd41c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36349dc9e2604b53b31c0c3d9931128e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419e80efe9993622fcb085a34f66a623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1c7e1b601a6b8a0deb46da88c1a33b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd14f53a18e1bfed4254e942f345269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd762b4d6c9647db05924d3e745a6991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41976a69de893e06188aa8717a3c4235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe8a4b8462310a0c1d2d68cbd07f35b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa91d64a86fa58173080c8817943c1c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8609577658e45ab0e2c17bf451f3b33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76c2057d5c276cb6c59fa1880287fda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4387433fb465c65791d73fe4c7fb964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6b9a8adfd5878890c3765c2eae35c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3e7055c35d73ed38d71048f4698efe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a222f4d2ebac0805d7a35f6ea2281563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b547b6cef0753ad76c2ec6637caea67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-240dc87c75a401ddeacc3f1a641ed3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5399890419cd7e402f5e411514ee3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04d5012cc1525877c7e032e6701e281&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cd73657f68ecf71018d63e394162ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4941781303f19e745042aad2237f81ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08a903bcc29ba54a545f0fbfc922a7b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9da95d303f996398774af59a2327d539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650e78b8096f9f7cece370950962f3c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de4b66d69047666bdb2ab47a03828fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-880c95881d83db855d75eadf8297358a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2431b3b4552aa63a72178a202c92bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d55b538adad3c639b729e3377b78a20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58df44cda05927cd903adbe63f48641c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7ff846be03f8677673730625ad6e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fee18f76430d121ab613984069f209e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b56d1daf41a7135af792e5f17f10061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614e33f39295a7909ffb544894f8dbcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac85fc649d6253fd56f0c0e65b99ddfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4953d5aa366add6d40468e1643931eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6f8753099a6779fea902d00492c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010d59f53c353a09e626f3656e43f25f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4cb059595fad783966d73f011af493a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9eafb5519ae847ebc95f1b6bd7a3901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28d8a78f075f0eccbcec19198a69d0c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4642364014d20a8527d9fb4ec06bdb04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97df03a76764ebe5533b42a54e7596c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68449f9db8a1088d8cfd218d490323d</data>
