    <node id="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Sir Albert Howard (born 1873) was an influential English agronomist, government scientist, and agricultural expert who is widely regarded as the godfather of scientific aerobic composting and a pioneer of organic agriculture. He developed the scientific foundations of organic farming, most notably through the creation of the Indore Process for converting animal and vegetable wastes into compost or humus. Central to his philosophy was the "Law of Return," which emphasized the necessity of returning organic matter to the soil to maintain health and fertility.

A prolific author, Sir Albert Howard wrote foundational works including *An Agricultural Testament*, *The Soil and Health*, and the pamphlet *The Manufacture of Humus from the Wastes of the Town and the Village*. In these works and his research, he emphasized the critical role of mycorrhizal fungi, soil life, and humus—defining fertile soil as one rich in humus—and argued that improving soil quality and plant food directly increases the quality of human food. He viewed health as "the one great subject" and spent years observing how soil management could prevent disease.

Beyond his technical contributions, Sir Albert Howard was a visionary who designed "diamond cities" to integrate food production with waste management, referring to compost sites and refuse-dump screenings as "humus mines." He advocated for agricultural practices that worked within the technological and economic limits of local farmers and envisioned a return to cultivating the highlands of the English chalk country. His insights into using compost as both a source of humus and an inoculant to increase seed yields in legume crops, as well as his overall philosophy on soil and human health, served as a major inspiration for Jerome Rodale.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1fbfc96142fb2e1554de743e1067f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49fe442094e7ea7c8e57a86dad17be24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ef084330f6f60c511ebb2e8e657b3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11905a2957c65e69706bb6f3ff65226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c90f74f233ea23d233d1c4023e91f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30b96f19db572c69aecf37c0f0b030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951a7735e0ed92839673ec30c6f5ee8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6308a55dba63b8652c56c1424f2ab3b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9be35452a55159cea361655ca53487b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28ab0744bd2c8644bdc99e6c30ae80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2473f4dcebdbdd42ecfa05be804a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85f843ce4c9e414f5a474793768109cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6acd1bd95566acfb8cf6c422a4a4f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3b1063c1d500ceacda94be5c1a920e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f01a9018938914804f49a80182b2f205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1932cb031e5713bde84668b6254f5c5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6795ac13deea0240f9376837154726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3781f0cc9a2995419d1d77092b5b7e7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4475a7350a431c2a4e38619dc9e13e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e075666adecb76602095c816ea6583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0745126232bd711152a0184bdc10060&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7e8b4bde4465470684d8ec0af5b158a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b5d1c530308e0e7a1ed5639a5d2b60</data>
