    <node id="&quot;NEW ZEALAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">New Zealand is a country characterized by its history of settlement by Westerners who arrived by boat to exploit natural wealth and establish extensive farming practices on virgin soil. While the region possesses large tracts of fertile land, it has also faced significant environmental challenges, including brittle environments, soil erosion, and soil exhaustion resulting from the systematic burning of forests for pasture. These soil exploitation issues were linked to a deterioration in population health, leading Dr. Chapman to conduct feeding experiments in the country. To address soil fertility, New Zealand utilizes the Indore Process, and the Humic Compost Club operates there; additionally, the country is the origin of a specific compost box design.

In the realm of agriculture and research, New Zealand is home to the Ruakura Animal Research Station, where grazing studies were performed, and it is the location where John Hancock conducted research on dairy cows. The country is noted for its integration of Voisin's work into pasture management practices, the use of management-intensive grazing systems to produce high yields of beef per acre, and studies conducted by agricultural workers on the grazing qualities of cows and their hereditary capacity to harvest grass. Furthermore, New Zealand is recognized as a successful example of eliminating agricultural subsidies to drive productivity and innovation. Other agricultural notes include the introduction of earthworms to increase pasture production, the use of formic acid for mite control, the existence of a specific clover strain that can cause bloat in livestock, and the presence of scientists providing expertise on grass proteins.

Biologically and geographically, New Zealand is a location where mushrooms such as *Stropharia rugosoannulata* are found. In its history, the country was involved in trading Wood Ears to China and Hong Kong during the late 1800s. New Zealand is also the site of the Mount Albert School, the origin of researcher A. T. Johns, and the place where the horse Solicitor General became one of the elite sires. Finally, New Zealand is mentioned as a potential source for lamb served on flights and was the destination of a one-month speaking tour undertaken by the author.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7029b183fa2cc4e652b9cb3d96c587ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a9a34a8a3dcef6c536d20a4d9cd4f9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445fbff3137d26bce84d879934fb156e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52de62eaf5c15e94a0f74fc247e02ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11b76d3a5c1bcd15187db94fe0f1ae9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cee44e954d1abb009f061fd993b844c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5010f12c1a9feda14321ff2156104eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6286cb14eb10acae02073bf5ac246ef1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3039a688aa2e6b47b0ab1e9e0729fc47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64f9f1d0ae53b516c4de411cdfbaec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09b0b6a4dfc3db42d923d3575dbf8ee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77998f10068e98f374d36ce3925f2d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c9875544dc79e979dbf41d0591d793b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-629af50f18d6312eb4d088cb93078b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cf015c914ceeb12acc1a5f9c6773a85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f327dcda762579e3e8ff20376026fc06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1609048eb7cbdd2e53212288aa2d0e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc52f86574e1bfc1754f84c90ed93d24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de4b66d69047666bdb2ab47a03828fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6960fa545678f7ef098947fd99e7d73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54170b5634f9fcf277523f76e163840f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b5917356402ab1051d609ddf238bd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87fba51a43132c1fcb0a51e42da41fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d719ed515957569d5a5c0e944e89a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f116a0e83303d4ebb8971bd977ade7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe627e052810ef46f019731a7bb9fda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064729886f339ac8895e2f324d6dd47e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7877eecb47b8c4e31e1be8eeeb5ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38b5915dc248e6ded7d55b74f484cddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2c449f01571421e5d465367c2416a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5641a9faf3471844174eec5d62e7b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68449f9db8a1088d8cfd218d490323d</data>
