    <node id="&quot;CHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">China is a country in Asia and the Far East with a profound agricultural history and a significant impact on global trade. It is characterized by an intensive agricultural system that has maintained soil fertility for over 4,000 years through the use of compost and age-long practices of utilizing farm wastes to create humus, including the historical use of soybeans as a cover crop. However, the region has also faced challenges with soil degradation and severe erosion due to failures in managing drainage areas as single units. The country is an example of an ancient civilization that employed top-down, large-scale irrigated agriculture and slave labor, and is geographically supported by the Himalayas.

In the realm of mycology, China is a global leader and a pioneer in mushroom cultivation. It is the native home of Shiitake mushrooms (the origin of the Stamets CS-2 strain) and P. citrinopileatus, and it holds the first written records of Shiitake cultivation. China is a primary source for various fungi cultures and stock culture libraries, and its scientists were the first to develop industrial-level spore-mass inoculation techniques. The country utilizes diverse cultivation methods, including the traditional practice of burying logs in sandy ground for Ling Chi and G. lucidum, as well as the submerged fermentation of Ganoderma lucidum mycelium. A wide variety of mushrooms are native to, cultivated in, or sold in Chinese markets, including Tremella fuciformis, Zhu Ling, Paddy Straw mushrooms, Wood Ears (cultivated since circa A.D. 600), G. frondosa (found in temperate hardwood regions), Pholiota nameko (common in cool temperate highlands), and P. cystidiosus. Additionally, Agaricus blazei strains are refined in Chinese laboratories, and Hericium erinaceus is distributed there. Despite this productivity, some analyses of mushrooms in China have revealed high concentrations of lead, mercury, and aluminum.

China plays a critical role in global commodity production and trade. It is a purported birthplace of the almond, with a history of dispersing the nut via the Silk Road and a current state-led expansion of almond planting (where it is called xingren). The country accounts for nearly half of the world's phosphorus production and is a primary source of imported softneck garlic. In the livestock and textile sectors, China is now the primary location for the tanning of hides, which has contributed to the decline of domestic hide markets in America. China is also</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ad03c75085e62d4cf641ff00f56a870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab2196ed3cfc357ea2968eacf70e5cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67da272e0cf77b7a72954b23074375bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cdcda2273c4d3e807e607b85d38791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f80535289583d0b174a792dec934f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-187f47c8b8e6814f319c165475064ae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1101930a67ed83a3fac551ddd493eeef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d488e4cd2bbc4b091273904e594e2cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01d793c2dc61cc5608f3044cefea7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d1aec09332ff6a142a5567b1afdc379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd01bcf1e428ba50030230c77f03910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99a4f6bfcac3f89a5e412fbeeb432e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25cec84d3faefdd8e04042d49203e0e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41976a69de893e06188aa8717a3c4235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc84578a2a9965cca7bdee803ba8f735&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe8a4b8462310a0c1d2d68cbd07f35b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b994c4aaecb06bda273f0e09161deddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3d2608ec774e94ae3556c5b7d8cd1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d467caefee31df754438e71491848a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a37142150e6090a50d92e1d1dabef730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363259c41f29f455370656b3d04be170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb648e07d9441fbfe3bcee4498fbad8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9869e53adcb9d90fe040e3a2bec26a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eba1d230844cb33e45b56b8cfd620d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3e7055c35d73ed38d71048f4698efe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162427b12ed8d1e50c5d8b055e2cd5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52fd5c92980e8846f221b5900200a76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65176548bde10cfe17c293a533bace23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d1c5c9d85a28b024fb5b126803180d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb886065fde7376bc6f30e23079e875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22f3967d311f087b86fc91bd0708142c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04f10386c4a39e5f50574580ea2171d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b6b727989514aa1ed7c4b5cf4c60484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74cd72bbc78235ee2cc27e78214fb076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de4b66d69047666bdb2ab47a03828fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec816632b945dc5236be5a3d82d9ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86fe558f51b1271d8f00b8534ee37050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b5917356402ab1051d609ddf238bd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87fba51a43132c1fcb0a51e42da41fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422fbd40d9eaa3fb837b775984c912c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc2a2ad2b38fdda540087364d1c8ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f716dbb539b9e685559a05a8f9f5d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6710a74adf9d60f7c9121567c01098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89fcb74fe3e0427762ee636b97ac891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63283b5b0d7af44d93e355da3bac994e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a03386c8fdad1c49ade13815bc6b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82bc20afcc996297375967f9d759b0ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4b544ed75741294a829a0b07b3bdf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8422f27b6e2f7c49af2d7c0895af1179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c412d7b08105fd05e24e46b46f204fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba34a2616df408aea43de3a851323499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bece2f190b302e65065ab1536812a7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64c2af8229ae517acd685a5341a4b3ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65edb41384e08b49b56188bbf153099d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3780f8195f7b351d288fda3cba325c0</data>
