    <node id="&quot;GREAT BRITAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Great Britain is a sovereign island nation and geographic region characterized by a moist, temperate climate that prevented the total soil sterility seen in Mesopotamia or North Africa. Historically, the nation's farming evolved from Saxon times to the present, though it has faced significant challenges, including a history of commerce that contributed to the spread of the bubonic plague and food security threats caused by submarine warfare in 1939, which necessitated an intensive "grow-more-food" policy.

In the realm of agriculture, Great Britain is depicted as a place of both innovation and systemic failure. While it is home to agricultural colleges, research institutes, the Ministry of Agriculture, and the Agricultural Research Council, the author observes a decline in farming standards and claims that fatal blunders regarding chemical versus organic farming are being repeated. Specific agricultural issues include the inefficient "bit by bit" filling of silos, concerns regarding eelworm diseases in potato and sugar beet crops, and the rapid development of grass tetany following the wartime policy of ploughing up old pastures. The nation is also noted for its methods of dealing with foot-and-mouth disease via slaughter and the practice of ley farming.

To combat these issues and the inertia of local governments, the author suggests implementing municipal composting and a regular subsoiling campaign. Great Britain is identified as a region where large-scale compost work is particularly relevant, with pioneers in farming, gardening, and nutrition currently breaking new ground in composting. The author analyzes the maintenance of soil fertility within the region, contrasting the alarming state of modern potato growing and soil health with the relative health of roadside hedges.

Additionally, Great Britain is the location of the Buckfast abbey, where the Buckfast hybrid was developed, and it serves as the sovereign state where the discussed medical, legal, and War Agricultural Executive Committees operate. Finally, Great Britain is used as a point of comparison to the United States, specifically regarding its historical response to epidemics and its current approach to farming.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9bde3a9925e013ce4a55dadba03682d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e187da58191464d057a3f1d2d09c423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282a09c67a0423a68ef7aac02a1b4779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb58cc843f6cfcf0ee4d5ba223c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963bd6f10eb2a3f0abb4b8280b4ac94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d276eaffd9fb05c963e568744d4574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de45d40ec65e6186764314ff7c6c5c95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c36ef4876a049c252a61a7110833f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e82a4a6907b17bf68833a636bd6ad5ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d49f5bc82b76d8f4146b18f3c7076cc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-993680272f3e5678f61ebce7fc3d0706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a20dca5473a46eeac4310d35a490fdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af625be74f2abb3e1944efcdd2748f34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f685240aeecfc4a0556f03c0af930046&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-240dc87c75a401ddeacc3f1a641ed3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05374d444d89278cd804bde3807b7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218f65ec9b659cddff295e2ed6826cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc52f86574e1bfc1754f84c90ed93d24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a7f4aa7178f919427c0954ff8040e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d719ed515957569d5a5c0e944e89a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2431b3b4552aa63a72178a202c92bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad44bd47e01a1d6bfb342156af1965f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15abe44b0e95afa45dd19faa53ac41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d4663e2e3eeb5466a2592bc8824b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e54f756180fea1648a4f8a1c56a989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b117c84af6b43cb698d268784eb7234e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6930a29b100d665f24c78c209eccf850</data>
