    <node id="&quot;ENGLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">England is a country located in Western Europe within the British Isles, characterized by a damp ecology and a history of land drainage. Historically, it was the European power from which the American colonies separated, and its political structures—specifically the House of Lords and House of Commons—influenced the political frameworks of the Federalists in the United States. England is the site of significant historical events, including the English Civil War, the occurrence of the Black Death, the Industrial Revolution, and the emergence of eighteenth-century utilitarian philosophy used to combat conservatism. It is also the location where Thomas Hobbes developed his political theories.

Agriculturally, England has a complex history transitioning from an open-field system and the use of the heavy mould board plough to enclosed farming. The country faced the challenge of expanding farming beyond its best land and experienced the tragedy of destroying permanent pastures. While England benefited from cheap goods produced through the exploitation of soil fertility elsewhere, it also dealt with the prevention of famine during the Napoleonic Wars. The nation is home to various agricultural landmarks and institutions, including the Royal Agricultural College, Nottingham University, and the Weybridge Veterinary Research Laboratory. Specific regions such as Berkshire, Devon, Leicestershire, Norfolk (including the Elveden Estate), and Holbeach Marsh are noted for their roles in grass growth data, soil recreation, and general farming.

England has been a hub for scientific research and agricultural innovation. It is the place where Nicolas Lampkin's original rotation designs were formulated, where pasture experiments at Jealott's Hill were conducted, and where the Indore Process is known. The country has seen research on soil fertility and nutrition by figures such as Liebig (who visited in 1865) and Dr. Scharff. More recent activities include a 2011 study on annual phosphorus budgets, ongoing research into the medicinal properties of Maitake with human subjects, and the establishment of producer-only farmers markets by Nina Planck.

From a biological and veterinary perspective, England is the location where tracheal mites were first identified in 1921 and where *P. euosmus* has been found. Additionally, the country is characterized by a mix of industrial phenomena and agricultural struggles, ranging from the professional land survey activities and hop-growing research conducted by the author to the observation of cows in May 1949 and the implementation of mechanized tethering apparatuses. Despite these advancements, some notes indicate a criminal neglect of organic waste along country roads and</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3b08c5812a78d79a773ecd56c3c1e084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c1e39a2b39311bfd6f1c3c05dab313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-591de784bfb5c3376bd8c1f7c511d0e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7029b183fa2cc4e652b9cb3d96c587ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e328d3b527b1888b7f5192459a3b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc828547e31ad0722ddb6c9ae3f92d30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5264961d05f0c7fcacb7d71cf57283a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10c2b55c35f65d6b5ffdc8c603ef37f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb58cc843f6cfcf0ee4d5ba223c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0707af73cf1b7f988c4cf8ff24fb2972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30aca7d7248a398bf698c2f58e21181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7501c88b4753d0e36195cd4c777c004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efe185a1df447e99af70cc3756a14187&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-993680272f3e5678f61ebce7fc3d0706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-613368bdb7745a7ad903ee709c39868e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84729b070482e322c7c832ced520e10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b994c4aaecb06bda273f0e09161deddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec66802bc43867cee6b1280e5876d8d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a20dca5473a46eeac4310d35a490fdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f820b4fd30fc97f0083ef9327fa9ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc5200861bfbf924cb02074bbc681c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6acd1bd95566acfb8cf6c422a4a4f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a12e811ea06c5bd6638d7a05b6486e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cf7746378c6e8d2b371fa8b0e35955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c70a5acc631338be6403992b6cfc4d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b22c7f65c401c0b783c864349640f372&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23fed92ffe59e67730588150c2a1cbf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-240dc87c75a401ddeacc3f1a641ed3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b320d4bf5bae3f28f4bca97246cd735&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec72301cd65d24bcaa0b9ddc0bf03d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b97dd6d6b95eae2e9e3d26bad764c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf76857d444c3de7b2d30bb6186a08a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87aef9adbbf32f7b8ba9d9db34d927a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d719ed515957569d5a5c0e944e89a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a60d6af54cb19714a27e9fba5484f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-243f1254a7c052194d69406b86376d18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7877eecb47b8c4e31e1be8eeeb5ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ed11907814c6b8e3996d688398501e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7d1f6e890206946300a3591e785ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e15abe44b0e95afa45dd19faa53ac41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c4f4d996e9e97716cae8883c368d24c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d4663e2e3eeb5466a2592bc8824b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2c449f01571421e5d465367c2416a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4cb059595fad783966d73f011af493a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1868297eecd6bcd734ccfccf0f46633a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5641a9faf3471844174eec5d62e7b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4be7aab5835b5557dffc1a1c85fd336d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68449f9db8a1088d8cfd218d490323d</data>
