    <node id="&quot;CANADA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Canada is a North American country characterized by a variety of economic, agricultural, and environmental contexts. In terms of agriculture and industry, Canada shares similar economic patterns with the United States, particularly regarding owner-operators, farmland under conservation agriculture, and the percentage of food produced via sustainable methods. While Canada has a property culture similar to that of the U.S., it is described as being less intense. The country’s agricultural landscape includes community and family-based farming (though this is on the wane), the use of the Indore Process, and a system where animal production is made cheaper through taxpayer-supported subsidies. Canada is also a source of imported lumber for home construction and exports wild picked mushrooms to Europe, maintaining a higher per capita mushroom consumption than the United States and prioritizing the fresh mushroom market over the dried market.

Environmentally and biologically, Canada is a habitat for *G. frondosa* in its eastern regions, but it also faces challenges such as the spread of the garlic bloat nematode pest and the potential movement of Africanized bees. In the realm of apiculture, Canadian honey bees have adapted to foreign ecosystems, and beekeepers—including those operating migratory hives—extensively use formic acid for mite control, adapting dosages to prevent queen failure. Apiculturists in Canada must also contend with poisonous plants like poison ivy and poison sumac. Additionally, mature wheat in Canada serves as a source of rust spores that can be transported by wind to other regions, and the country returns approximately a fifth of its sewage to the land.

Historically and socially, Canada is noted as a place where European farming practices once displaced indigenous cultures and served as a refuge for Tory manufacturers during the American Revolution. It is the home of the University of British Columbia, the companies Heilyser Technology Ltd. and F. W. Jones and Sons, and a regional office for HarperCollins. Individual accounts link Canada to specific events, such as a farmer raising chickens for fly-tying feathers, a location where Woodrow served on a Mormon mission, and the origin of an apprentice's fiancée. Furthermore, the author of the provided text gave a speech in Ontario, Canada, and conducted interviews with Canadian growers to assess the potential success of "pick-your-own" farming. Finally, Canada is recognized as a source for stock culture libraries and a place where the health- and risk-based critiques of industrial farming have had a significant influence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49fe442094e7ea7c8e57a86dad17be24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c1e39a2b39311bfd6f1c3c05dab313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbc1c2ec064a792c47e97c74d0a8614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48779ccefd65e29504648e87fe948afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54c5f82f0f44cdd87998f2211f5330e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ac3062e2f983be26233b2d2aaf916a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01d793c2dc61cc5608f3044cefea7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a81a83856d7b7ec39448bc80f43b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc43a3f1c081aba3e143c209e36aef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69d184d39c4fc61b176c219e8852dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85284a23be3f49e6f94cd4e536e396a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99a4f6bfcac3f89a5e412fbeeb432e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5780ec82bf5f9eace3f594f7e7368b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff2a1270133813dbf92927fcbf14a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a20f78a3d55496e66f77ebe53b96a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c3e9b22256bd1fdb52e241a416095ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150b6a45026cb8f7ac1617459ec54b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8609577658e45ab0e2c17bf451f3b33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f631071313bdef0aeb10a5956616bd17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a222f4d2ebac0805d7a35f6ea2281563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99e4abb0de7b0941ca1fc87ecc8fb4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a529b2a82aeedaec884d490e181507e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ae2b642515d199b40d344346490776&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30f323d641a1c5f22026b8b0bab6b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25521141823b7becef820b71d7dbda0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b97dd6d6b95eae2e9e3d26bad764c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc2a2ad2b38fdda540087364d1c8ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408f6f0784b8ad7de477241c6ca88e5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ba06576d3e50eb6533780747a29cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4455bd7c30235e62c66747849070cfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f716dbb539b9e685559a05a8f9f5d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38b5915dc248e6ded7d55b74f484cddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6f8753099a6779fea902d00492c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2c449f01571421e5d465367c2416a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbe3628e117427ed1c35a791b026e9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc219a87c7ecb22911c9b9083bd392f</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1035}]</data>
