    <node id="&quot;WASHINGTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">Washington refers to both the U.S. state in the Pacific Northwest and the capital of the United States.

As a U.S. state, Washington is home to cities such as Seattle, Olympia, Port Townsend, and Sequim, as well as institutions like Evergreen College and the Janus Youth Programs. The region is characterized by diverse geography and agriculture, including the Olympic Peninsula, the production of regional apples—where bees are sent to pollinate Pink Lady varieties—and lavender production in Sequim. The state is a hub for various farming initiatives, including conservation agriculture and locations such as Finnriver Farm, Chimacum Corner Farmstand, and the Bear Tribe's teaching center. Additionally, Washington is noted for its fungal diversity, with wild Shiitake sightings, Oyster mushrooms from river-valley habitats, and common coastal mushrooms in November. The state's forestlands have been used for studies on biosolid applications, which has occasionally caused concern among hikers, and a specific pulp company's sludge flood triggered a massive Morel fruiting. Geologically, its calcareous soils are suggested as ideal sites for truffle orchards. Furthermore, Washington is a destination for the shipment of mated queens and was the origin of stolen beehives.

As the capital of the United States, Washington serves as the seat of government and the center of political authority where legislators and officials are located. It is the destination of Khrushchev's flight and the site where congressional hearings on soil conservation were held following dust storms. While it is the center of political power where agricultural policies are made, it has been suggested that this political center is less effective at driving change than consumer demand.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f4f83b407929c9c73f6150edfd6dc214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aaeba6a87de6589129068300a4f26db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f99aab1cb82082ba3da1ae7b1c873ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ad84f4512a86bce4785f65f78b9c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-923ecd82dafb6f5a01be8c322b21fe79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ac3062e2f983be26233b2d2aaf916a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679416bb166ca53a86b2b2f4dbcf7deb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8c87a64c0ba531f4c75b187a357ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21be92c21b7215c9e86b338cd15d5f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2476a09713ca3285f8982dbedd3d0db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa6369dd0584465f07387131c6d28e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64f9f1d0ae53b516c4de411cdfbaec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75673023cb192cee1fbe66473e0ff86d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a0e526319f92312412e2845aee3568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-485a6a1d47c4c9bf2bf563c9e11d4af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a019e529b263129037d3a41686a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46b743897ae935dc3e642a4af1293bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a37142150e6090a50d92e1d1dabef730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-606bb2ef5a69bfd9d5624ad8d5f3f93d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a472c8ad6a1e1fdcb7328f429ac1ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e0be7f0a6204d59bd58a3fab64b0fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf21622f766ab205d57f7915f9105bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6db795582f52e35a0bb9aea86e66f7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e410bfae74fb6896e8e0079e060cf83d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9373ee84b3a77eb37578d5b0a36a9135&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ebf23631547617747b7c2b24e2249cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a1f23ac039aa3ef70ba8ce3a43a9117&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc622c3b7686d0920d6c36b83dafaaf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d628ebc9fbc7db25894f19c606113e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e65d0c627c6c1fa008b88b36a9097158&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbfbbce7bbb2b1195a5322a8057953dc</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 266}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1227}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALIFORNIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">California is a populous, agriculturally rich state on the West Coast of the United States, encompassing regions such as the Central Valley, Placer, Merced, and Tuolumne counties, as well as cities like Sacramento, San Rafael, and Santa Cruz. Known for its superlative climate and soil, it is a global agricultural powerhouse, dominating the world's almond market with a share of 70 to 80 percent. This dominance creates a massive annual demand for honeybee colonies, making California a primary destination for millions of hives—including those operated by beekeepers like John Miller, Brandi, and Pat Heitkam—to pollinate almond and apricot blossoms every January. The state is also a center for citrus production, specifically mandarins, and is a top honey producer.

The state's agricultural landscape is characterized by large-scale industrial monoculture, featuring massive lettuce and spinach production for distant urban markets, and megadairies that have impacted local communities. This industrialization is mirrored in its labor politics and history; California is the setting for *The Grapes of Wrath*, where the Joad family and other Depression-era refugees migrated in search of work only to face a flooded labor market and farm evictions. In more recent times, the state has served as a hub for hippie organic farming and is viewed as a litmus test for the viability of bioregional food systems.

California's diverse ecology and geography include hardiness Zone 9, western coastal areas where *Agaricus brunnescens* and wild Shiitake mushrooms are found, and the western edge of the habitat for Africanized honey bees. However, the state faces significant environmental and agricultural challenges, including droughts, soil alkalinity caused by modern irrigation, and the presence of heavy metals in some mushrooms. It has also dealt with bee-related crises, including hive collapses, the parasitic phorid fly, and strict policies involving border closures and hive destruction to prevent the spread of varroa mites.

Beyond agriculture, California is home to institutions such as Pomona College and California State University at Chico, and is the location of businesses like "Outstanding In The Field," Gourmet Mushrooms, and the manufacturer of the Valley Oak Wheel Hoe. The state's legal and social landscape includes voter-passed initiatives on livestock production and zoning restrictions that have impacted family ranches. In the context of beekeeping, it is a key region for queen-rearing and the development of innovative pest-control methods</data>
