      <data key="d6">chunk-2a7084302d57591ff02e89969b4c3abd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;VERMONT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In the context of beekeeping in Vermont, honey supers are used to harvest honey while allowing for ongoing mite control."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4f0965a7f888753898bdb3624830c9fd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;GOLDENROD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The timing of removing honey supers in Vermont affects whether the late-season goldenrod honey flow is harvested."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4f0965a7f888753898bdb3624830c9fd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMB HONEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey supers are used in the production of comb honey, with specific placement strategies to improve harvest appearance."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85263881590bbad34c8bcb9551c9a883</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen may lay eggs in honey supers if the brood nest is congested, though beekeepers often try to discourage this."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85263881590bbad34c8bcb9551c9a883</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;BEKEEPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper adds honey supers to the hive to provide additional space for honey storage and prevent swarming."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey bees fill honey supers with nectar and honey, and the lack of these supers can lead to the colony becoming honey bound."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">61.5</data>
      <data key="d5">"A smoker is a basic tool used by beekeepers during the process of opening and inspecting a hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"A smoker is a piece of essential equipment used in the profession of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"A smoker is a tool used by beekeepers to aid in managing bees and handling hive components."&lt;SEP&gt;"A smoker is a tool used by beekeepers to calm bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker is described as one of the essential tools of beekeeping used to calm and soothe bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker is listed as necessary additional equipment for the practice of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker is listed as necessary equipment for the practice of beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f928b6b6595520556e61b690ad234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91fddbed5da654e2156cc50a2222b4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788901d0b4d29c039e6a86eed1ac4b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c85b379d83c9f869435c42e6568dee9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The smoker is mentioned as an essential piece of equipment that a beekeeper needs to have available at the site of the hives, such as a beeyard."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-048ad5fead1e52a66cfd2e40b5467d7b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper uses the smoker to calm upset bees or move them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper uses the smoker to distract, calm, and herd bees in a desired direction."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A smoker is used to blow smoke into the hive entrances and between boxes to manage bees during inspections or reversing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker is used to puff smoke into the hive entrance and under the cover to calm the bees before inspection."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c516e184f72cae24cee188c702d41f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SUIT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">12.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A smoker is used as a tool to mask pheromones and reduce bee defensiveness, serving as an alternative or supplement to defensive clothing like bee suits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The author mentions that using a well-lit smoker and a calm demeanor often makes the use of a bee suit unnecessary."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-abf15980aea2d79d85e102a8e8c947bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288ac639645002f12344e2dbb4b38cb6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;SMOKE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The smoker is the tool used to create and apply the smoke to the hives."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIC STANDARDS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The type of fuel used in a smoker is regulated by organic standards to ensure only natural sources are used."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">13.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool is used to create a gap in the hive so that the nose of the smoker can be inserted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker and hive tool are both described as basic necessities and tools of the beekeeping trade."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c516e184f72cae24cee188c702d41f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;VEIL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">11.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author mentions that using a well-lit smoker and a calm demeanor often makes the use of a veil unnecessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker and veil are both basic necessities for beekeeping; additionally, the flame from a smoker can melt the screening on a veil."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-abf15980aea2d79d85e102a8e8c947bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;BELLOWS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bellows are part of the smoker, used to provide air to the fuel to keep it burning."&lt;SEP&gt;"The smoker utilizes bellows to provide air blasts that light and rekindle the fuel fire within its chamber."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;ARMY SURPLUS AMMUNITION BOX&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"An army surplus ammunition box serves as a safe, fireproof container for storing the smoker."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SMOKER&quot;" target="&quot;VERMONT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author lives in Vermont and uses smokers as part of their beekeeping practice."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-abf15980aea2d79d85e102a8e8c947bc</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
