      <data key="d6">chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool is used for manipulating parts of a beehive."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hive tool is listed as necessary additional equipment for the practice of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hive tool is used for prying hive sections apart and is a common tool used in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f928b6b6595520556e61b690ad234</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BEEYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool is mentioned as an essential piece of equipment that a beekeeper needs to have available at the site of the hives, such as a beeyard."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-048ad5fead1e52a66cfd2e40b5467d7b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;THE HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool is used to manipulate the hive and can potentially break plastic frames within it."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91fddbed5da654e2156cc50a2222b4ed</data>
