    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BEEHIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool is a steel implement used by beekeepers to open the top of a beehive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27c4a101237a6eb4eff648c0b0b5a16d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;PACKAGE OF BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool is used to pry open the package and remove the feed can during the transfer of bees into a hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e9de2778ec077dc2aae514901168a89</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SUIT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool (specifically its flat edge) can be used to remove stingers that penetrate the skin, complementing the protection of a bee suit."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-288ac639645002f12344e2dbb4b38cb6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;VEIL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool and veil are both identified as basic necessities for beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c6739d4c7c92b4bbf50b18187fe06b72</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;EUROPEAN HONEY BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool is used by the beekeeper when interacting with and manipulating honey bee hives."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e4c100bb043929fe5d53e4af2e279dfb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool is used to pry up the corners of hive bodies or supers to separate them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hive tool is used for prying, scraping, and manipulating the parts of a hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c516e184f72cae24cee188c702d41f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67600081c317292f8ef362e2f5621f34</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BEESWAX&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hive tool is used to scrape burr comb (beeswax) off the frames for collection and rendering."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85263881590bbad34c8bcb9551c9a883</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;BILL MRAZ&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bill Mraz taught a system for finding the queen that involves the use of a hive tool as a lever to remove frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-813ff1de343023e85ba7e541c258f8f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE TOOL&quot;" target="&quot;PROPOLIS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A hive tool is used to slide along propolis-filled openings to dislodge buildup and clean the trap."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5cdc449839e793310ef8f89b87479c09</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VEIL&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">27.5</data>
      <data key="d5">"A veil is essential beekeeping equipment used to protect the beekeeper from stings during work."&lt;SEP&gt;"A veil is protective equipment worn by beekeepers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The veil is an essential part of beekeeping attire to protect the face and head from stings."</data>
      <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f928b6b6595520556e61b690ad234</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VEIL&quot;" target="&quot;BEEYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The veil is worn by the beekeeper while working in the beeyard to protect against bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VEIL&quot;" target="&quot;HELMET&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
