      <data key="d6" />
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEYARD&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeeping activities and the associated discomforts and pleasures take place within the beeyard."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEYARD&quot;" target="&quot;PACKAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Packages are often made up in a southern beeyard using bees from colonies in that yard."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEE STING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees perform stinging as a defensive behavior to protect themselves and their colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers work with bees and manage their colonies, often facing the risk of being stung."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper monitors bee activity, weather patterns, and colony health to determine if the bees need help or feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper works with, manages, and monitors the behavior and health of the bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;SWARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Swarming is described as nature's solution for bees to perpetuate their species and replace colonies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers manage bees and monitor them for signs of swarming to maintain colony strength and honey production."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">40.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bees live and work within the hive, and their activities are observed by inspecting the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bees live in the hive, forming a cluster and utilizing frames within it to store honey and pollen."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hive is the dwelling where bees store food, rear brood, and are managed by the beekeeper."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hive serves as the house and permanent location for the bee colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees are fed sugar syrup (including in candy form), but burned sugar can be lethal to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees consume sugar syrup provided by the beekeeper, though their ability to access it depends on the temperature and cluster size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees feed on sugar syrup, especially during installation and the first month."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;PACKAGE OF BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A package of bees is a commercially available unit containing workers, drones, and a queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;NUC&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A nuc is an alternative option to a package for installing a new bee colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen is the egg-layer of the bee colony; she takes a break in early winter and resumes laying during colder periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen is the member of the bee colony responsible for laying the brood pattern."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BROOD NEST&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees occupy and use frame space to expand the brood nest."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees collect and store pollen in cells within the hive frames."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees store pollen in frames within the hive as a necessary food reserve."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees draw out the foundation to create comb, stimulated by the presence of incoming nectar."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bees are responsible for drawing out the foundation steadily."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;NECTAR FLOW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees depend on the nectar flow to produce wax and draw out foundation comb."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bees take advantage of the nectar flow to build up population and produce honey."&lt;SEP&gt;"The start of the nectar flow indicates that the bees no longer need supplemental feeding."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;SUPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees move into the super to store surplus honey, provided there is a nectar flow and no undrawn frames below."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Supering is the process of providing bees with superstructure space to store surplus honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;FALL MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Fall management consists of tasks performed to prepare the bees for the challenges of winter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;WINTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees survive winter by forming a cluster for mutual warmth and remaining confined to the hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;COLONY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees form the cluster that constitutes the population and activity of the colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colony is described as a superorganism composed of bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d689db19e9533ba99ddacc008292886b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees consume honey as their primary winter food store and move upward through the hive as they consume it."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;CANDY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees are fed candy as a sugar source, though burned sugar in the candy can be lethal to them."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;DRY GRANULATED SUGAR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees use dry granulated sugar as an emergency subsistence food source when other reserves are low."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN SUBSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees are fed pollen substitute when they are short on pollen, either in patty form or dry."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN PATTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees consume pollen patties placed on frame tops near the brood nest."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;VIRGIL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Virgil described an ancient belief that bees were born from the putrid blood of a slaughtered bullock."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;CHARLES BUTLER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Charles Butler concluded that the bee controlling the hive was a female."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;JAN SWAMMERDAM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Jan Swammerdam determined that the queen bee laid all the eggs in the hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;FRANÇOIS HUBER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"François Huber discovered that queens are fertilized on the wing during a virgin flight."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;INDIGENOUS CULTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Indigenous cultures are mentioned as having had a natural connection to the land, plants, and animals, serving as a contrast to the effort modern humans must put in to connect with bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d689db19e9533ba99ddacc008292886b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;OBSERVATION HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"An observation hive is described as a useful tool for the process of closely observing bees to enhance the connection between the human and the bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d689db19e9533ba99ddacc008292886b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEE VENOM THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees produce bee venom which is used for therapy; the author discusses taking bees from the colony for this specific purpose."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d689db19e9533ba99ddacc008292886b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;BEE STING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers are frequently stung, but often build a physical and psychological tolerance to the stings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper studies and observes the activities and behavior of honey bees to improve their skill."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text discusses the interaction between bees and beekeepers, noting that bees react to the beekeeper's odor and behavior rather than 'knowing' them personally."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;LEARNING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text suggests that a beekeeper's success depends on their own learning and understanding of why bees behave the way they do."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;COLONY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper manages and observes the behavior of the entire colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper monitors the population growth and health of the colony to ensure its progress."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper can collect pure pollen at the hive entrance and feed it back to the bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;THE DANCE LANGUAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The effectiveness of the dance language contributes to the success of the colony, which in turn benefits the beekeeper."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">34.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper manages the size of the hive and uses strong hives to prevent infestations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper performs inspections by opening the hive to check on the queen and the colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper prepares, sets up, and manages the hive to house the bee colony."&lt;SEP&gt;"The beekeeper routinely checks the hive for blockages, inspects the internal cluster, and checks the hive's weight to assess food stores."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0f4bb80b935e118383082352a101ac3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;PROTECTIVE GEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper wears protective gear, such as a veil, for safety while working with bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;JACKKNIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper uses a jackknife to puncture the plug of sugar candy in the queen cage."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;PLIERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper uses pliers to remove the syrup can from the package."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;FEEDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper prepares and uses a feeder to provide syrup to the bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;PACKAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper monitors the progress of the package and provides assistance to ensure its survival."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper evaluates the queen's performance and may perform requeening to improve colony strength."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper prepares and feeds sugar syrup to the bees using frames or feeders when honey stores are low."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;CANDY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper can make and provide candy (made from sugar and water) as an alternative method of feeding the bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;FIRE EXTINGUISHER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A fire extinguisher should be kept handy by the beekeeper in vehicles or buildings used for beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;SUGAR WATER SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A beekeeper may use a sugar water solution as an alternative to smoke to manage bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dee772a46eb60a47d303c4f69578a182</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;WAX MOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers must manage and control wax moth infestations using sunlight, ventilation, and hive management."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0f4bb80b935e118383082352a101ac3c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper manipulates supers to manage space and store honey, affecting wax moth prevention."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0f4bb80b935e118383082352a101ac3c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;APIARY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The beekeeper manages the location of supers relative to the apiary to prevent feeding frenzies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0f4bb80b935e118383082352a101ac3c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPER&quot;" target="&quot;APICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.5</data>
      <data key="d5">"A BEEKEEPER is an individual who practices apiculture."</data>
      <data key="d6" />
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE STING&quot;" target="&quot;ANAPHYLACTIC SHOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A severe level of reaction to a bee sting can lead to anaphylactic shock, which is a life-threatening situation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ANAPHYLACTIC SHOCK&quot;" target="&quot;STING KIT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"People prone to anaphylactic shock from stings are advised to carry a physician-prescribed sting kit."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a4a1a431b94a27a92d263b7dde5aa5a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;APIARY INSPECTION PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers are regulated by apiary inspection programs, and budget cuts to these programs have shifted more responsibility onto individual beekeepers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;PARASITIC MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers are increasingly pressured to recognize, control, or eliminate parasitic mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers must deal with the threat and spread of the Africanized bee."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;SWARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers generally view swarming as a highly undesirable occurrence due to loss of population and honey production."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;SWARM CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers are the practitioners who implement swarm control and prevention techniques."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;THE COLONY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers evaluate the health, queen performance, and food stores of the colony to ensure winter survival."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers determine the requisite amount of honey stores needed for a colony to survive winter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers feed sugar syrup (two parts sugar to one part water) to the colony if honey stores are insufficient."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers inspect the hive for minimum pollen levels and may provide pollen in early spring."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;POLLEN SUBSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers provide pollen substitute in early spring if natural pollen is lacking."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE BODIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers use hive bodies (specifically two deeps) to store the necessary amount of honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;BULK FEEDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers use a bulk feeder on top of the hive to provide supplemental food."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;MOUSE GUARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers place mouse guards across the hive entrance to prevent mice from nesting."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;INSULATION BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers use insulation boards to keep the hive warm and dry and provide an upper entrance."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text describes the collective practices of beekeeping, such as fall requeening and winter preparation, performed by beekeepers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERSEDURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers may choose to intervene in the natural process of supersedure by introducing ripe queen cells to help the hive raise a replacement queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bed6fe8d6b1e0689fd3080d94a55bcac</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers focus on the queen as one of the primary bees responsible for the production of comb, honey, and brood."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b481828497c05f9df552dd81b644f543</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers focus on the workers for their role in hive production and may cull drone brood to protect them."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b481828497c05f9df552dd81b644f543</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;DRONES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers often overlook drones or treat them as an inconvenience, but holistically oriented beekeepers recognize their sacrificial role."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b481828497c05f9df552dd81b644f543</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers may cull drone brood specifically to suppress the population of varroa mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b481828497c05f9df552dd81b644f543</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEEKEEPERS&quot;" target="&quot;BLACK BEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bears cause more fear and trepidation among beekeepers than any other wild animal."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7efd4ef14d88b08f2fac0f36e6180fa3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;APIARY INSPECTION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Apiary inspection programs are concerned with controlling the spread of the Africanized bee."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;APIARY INSPECTION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;PARASITIC MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Apiary inspection programs are concerned with controlling the spread of parasitic mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;APIARY INSPECTION PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"These programs regulate beekeeping and monitor hive health."</data>
      <data key="d6" />
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The spread of Africanized bees leads to a need for further beekeeping regulations and can cause public perception issues affecting the craft."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96f78f364d74eca8b91a5a10f5f9de4b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;SWARM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The introduction of Africanized bees makes capturing swarms riskier in some areas."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;POLICE DEPARTMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text mentions that state/province regulations may require authorized personnel (like police/fire) to pick up swarms to prevent the spread of Africanized bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;FIRE DEPARTMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text mentions that state/province regulations may require authorized personnel (like police/fire) to pick up swarms to prevent the spread of Africanized bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;BRAZIL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee resulted from African bees escaping and interbreeding with existing stock in Brazil."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;SOUTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Offspring of the original African swarms spread and interbred through South America."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;CENTRAL AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee spread from South America into Central America."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee spread into the United States in 1991."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;ITALIANS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee is a crossbreed of the African bee and European races like the Italians."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;CAUCASIANA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee is a crossbreed of the African bee and European races like the Caucasiana."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AFRICANIZED BEE&quot;" target="&quot;CARNIOLANS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Africanized bee is a crossbreed of the African bee and European races like the Carniolans."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PARASITIC MITES&quot;" target="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Parasitic mites have been present in North America since the mid-1980s."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PARASITIC MITES&quot;" target="&quot;WESTERN HEMISPHERE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
