      <data key="d5">"The author proposes using plastic film for greenhouses in the East to reduce reliance on California's exports."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e0411bd672adabdde5a4bdf77ebe2d43</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EAST COAST&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The East Coast is a region of the United States."</data>
      <data key="d6" />
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WEST COAST&quot;" target="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey bees reached the West Coast of North America by 1850."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORENZO L. LANGSTROTH&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Lorenzo L. Langstroth discovered or realized the concept of bee space in 1850."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORENZO L. LANGSTROTH&quot;" target="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Langstroth's discovery of bee space resulted in the creation of the Langstroth hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Langstroth hive design and dimensions are based on the concept of bee space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Langstroth hive is a standard style of hive used for housing and caring for honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Langstroth hive is the standard housing system used for managing honey bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e06b0074dff6e9083043d922831e71f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;LANGSTROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Langstroth invented and patented the Langstroth hive in 1852."&lt;SEP&gt;"Langstroth invented and patented the Langstroth hive, featuring suspended movable frames based on bee space."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lorenzo L. Langstroth is the namesake and developer of the Langstroth hive system."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;WAX-COMB FOUNDATION SHEETS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wax-comb foundation sheets were designed to attach to the movable frames used in the Langstroth hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;MOSES QUINBY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Quinby developed his own variation on the Langstroth hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;LORENZO LANGSTROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Lorenzo Langstroth invented the Langstroth hive, which revolutionized beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0984220078ce71973ba3b0fa10b37a2e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;JOHN MILLER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"John Miller's profession was made possible by the invention of the Langstroth hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0984220078ce71973ba3b0fa10b37a2e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers evolved to use the Langstroth hive as a standard, simple, and elegant system."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5b6278bcba2e2dfe6f1202b147f87019</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;TOP BAR HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are types of beehives mentioned as options for adding expansion room (supers or top bars)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the two designs in terms of orientation, cost, ease of construction, and impact on bee stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"The top bar hive is compared and contrasted with the Langstroth hive regarding design, orientation, and perceived impact on bee health."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-141bd4f59be1ccee796abafaf0658f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13bef129d93b5a27e008dbee0931310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9b2fa060b49dfcd9523440966c974ac</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;KENYAN TOP BAR HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The KTBH was developed to help transition traditional Kenyan hollow log hives to Langstroth-style hives."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e9b2fa060b49dfcd9523440966c974ac</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;EUROPEAN HONEY BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The vertical orientation of the Langstroth hive mimics the natural cavities used by feral European honey bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b13bef129d93b5a27e008dbee0931310</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;TBH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text compares the construction, dimensions, and management benefits of the Top Bar Hive (TBH) against the Langstroth hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the two types of hives, discussing inspection time, standardization of frame widths, and their relative effectiveness for beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e06b0074dff6e9083043d922831e71f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;BEESWAX FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Langstroth hives typically use full sheets of beeswax foundation or starter strips to guide comb building."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions that using beeswax foundation in a Langstroth hive results in less drone comb compared to natural building."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;WAX MOTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"If a Langstroth hive is supered too early without enough worker bees to patrol the space, it can lead to problems from wax moths."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84b0074137dce67380e1f3b23f86de2b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LANGSTROTH HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;SMALL HIVE BEETLES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"If a Langstroth hive is supered too early without enough worker bees to patrol the space, it can lead to problems from small hive beetles."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84b0074137dce67380e1f3b23f86de2b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;REMOVABLE FRAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bee space allowed for the free use of movable/removable frames that were not fastened to the hive walls."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;BEESWAX FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The development of beeswax foundation was a result of the understanding of bee space and its application to frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The development of the honey extractor was enabled by the discovery of bee space and the subsequent use of movable frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN EXCLUDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The development of the queen excluder is linked to the understanding of bee space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93fd599c3721904b0c0c72f8f1f0969f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The installation of the queen cage can violate bee space, leading bees to build wild comb in that area."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bee space is the critical gap between frames in the hive that must be maintained to prevent the build-up of wild comb."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;LANGSTROTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Langstroth identified and named the 'bee space' (three-eighths of an inch) as the key to designing a hive with movable frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPOLIS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees fill gaps narrower than a fifth of an inch with propolis, which informed Langstroth's definition of bee space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEESWAX FOUNDATION&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bees in a hive are often hived on beeswax foundation, where they must build comb."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEESWAX FOUNDATION&quot;" target="&quot;TBH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"TBH beekeepers often limit or avoid the use of beeswax foundation to allow bees to build combs naturally."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;FRANCESCO DE HRUSCHKA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Francesco de Hruschka invented the honey extractor in 1865."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6099b8ab1322280eb9653d60e287b9d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;PLASTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Plastic combs are more rugged than wax, resulting in fewer lost frames when spinning in a honey extractor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0bfa52bca196a2a92c24daffb2347956</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNCAPPING MACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The uncapping machine is used to prepare frames before they are placed into the honey extractor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SUPPLY COMPANIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bee supply companies promote and sell various equipment, including smaller boxes that affect how honey is collected and extracted."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN EXCLUDER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen excluder is a piece of equipment used by beekeepers to manage bee movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The queen excluder is listed as optional equipment for beekeeping."</data>
