      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A nucleus hive is a small colony drawn from an established hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUCLEUS HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A nucleus hive contains a new, young laying queen who is an accepted member of that colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUCLEUS HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A nucleus hive is a smaller colony that is transferred into a permanent hive setup."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUCLEUS HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"If the queen of a nucleus hive is not already free on the frames, she may be delivered in a separate queen cage."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE BEES&quot;" target="&quot;MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Mites are noted as a potential problem when using package bees, requiring precautions."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE BEES&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen is introduced to the package bees under traumatic conditions and may not always be accepted by the colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE BEES&quot;" target="&quot;SWARM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Once captured, a swarm can be treated similarly to package bees with similar results."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING EQUIPMENT SUPPLIER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeeping equipment dealers often have package bees or arrange for truckload shipments of them."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE BEES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING PUBLICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Package bees are advertised extensively in beekeeping publications."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
