      <data key="d5">"Tartaric acid is added to syrup to invert the sugar."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6bb5ed2e7521db41a82dfc5b79b8b701</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;INVERTED SUGAR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The addition of tartaric acid to sugar syrup creates inverted sugar."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6bb5ed2e7521db41a82dfc5b79b8b701</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;BEE FEED&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sugar syrup is a common component or type of bee feed mentioned in the context of bulk feeding."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6bb5ed2e7521db41a82dfc5b79b8b701</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sugar syrup is used by beekeepers as a food source for hives that are low on honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-693ffb57dfcac7260fd0345d7e791e21</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;BEKEEPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Many beekeepers use sugar syrup to feed bees to ensure that foundation is drawn out into comb."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f2e066e2a68f225f5ecf3fa2f5d02bd8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;BEE TEA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned as types of feed beekeepers use to ensure comb is drawn out or to replace harvested honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-afb545522a163c5982461b497e852ea7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;CORN SYRUP&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are described as feeds used to replace honey, which the author argues is unsustainable and not in the bees' best interest."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-afb545522a163c5982461b497e852ea7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUGAR SYRUP&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIC STANDARDS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Organic standards discourage the practice of harvesting all honey and replacing it with feeds like sugar syrup."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-afb545522a163c5982461b497e852ea7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUC&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers handle nucs (nucleus colonies) as part of colony management."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUC&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Creating a nuc (nucleus colony) reduces the number of mites and interrupts their reproductive cycle by breaking the brood cycle."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-35f6eef0d2ff08b3a3b7b2c2e942edde</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NUC&quot;" target="&quot;KIRK WEBSTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Kirk Webster uses nucs to attempt to develop mite-resistant bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-35f6eef0d2ff08b3a3b7b2c2e942edde</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKER BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen cage contains a half-dozen worker bees who serve as attendants to the queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN CAGE CANDY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Queen cage candy is located at one end of the queen cage to serve as food and a plug for delayed release."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;CANDY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The candy is located inside the queen cage and is eaten by bees to release the queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen cage is located within the hive body to introduce the queen to the colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;NUCLEUS COLONIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Queen cages are used during the process of establishing colonies, including nucleus colonies, to safely introduce the queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bdb2c38da2254d735c78b22dae9b2c6c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;NUCLEUS COLONY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen cage is used as the primary method to introduce a new queen into a nucleus colony (nuc) to ensure the bees accept her."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78c200287e609c62f98d61c6a969e444</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;SWISS ARMY KNIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A Swiss Army knife (specifically its reamer/threading tool) can be used to poke a hole in the candy of a queen cage to encourage bees to release the queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78c200287e609c62f98d61c6a969e444</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;BEE YARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen cage is used to introduce specific genetic traits into the bee yard by facilitating the introduction of a new queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78c200287e609c62f98d61c6a969e444</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN CAGE&quot;" target="&quot;PUSH-IN CAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A push-in cage is a specific type of queen cage made of hardware cloth."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9654edf0284987ba4f0c8bde4acffe9b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WORKER BEES&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN CAGE CANDY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The worker bees eat the queen cage candy, which can eventually lead to the release of the queen."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PACKAGE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The original package consists of worker bees with varying ages and life spans."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIVE BODY&quot;" target="&quot;HIVE BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A second hive body is placed directly on top of the first hive body to expand the colony's space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;NECTAR FLOW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The timing and presence of a nectar flow determine when a beekeeper should place a super."&lt;SEP&gt;"The timing of the nectar flow is a primary consideration for when to add a honey super."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Supering is defined as the act of placing supers (superstructure) on the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supering is the act of adding supers (the boxes) to a hive to provide honey storage space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39baafb5b073ac43e9932248ea8ca932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;BEE BRUSH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bee brush is used to brush live bees from frames within the super during the harvest process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;BEE ESCAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bee escape is one of several methods used for clearing bees from supers to remove the crop."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;ESCAPE BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The escape board is one of several methods used for clearing bees from supers to remove the crop."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;FUME BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The fume board is one of several methods used for clearing bees from supers to remove the crop."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;BLOWER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A blower is used as an effective way to remove bees from the super."&lt;SEP&gt;"The blower is one of several methods used for clearing bees from supers to remove the crop."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;SHOP VACUUM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Some shop vacuums operated in reverse may work to remove bees from the super."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;BRUSH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A brush may be used to remove the last few bees from the super if other methods fail."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;DEHUMIDIFIER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A dehumidifier helps maintain or lower moisture content in the room where supers are stored."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"An extractor is used to remove honey from the frames within the supers using centrifugal force."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;MESH BAG&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A mesh bag is an alternative method for extracting honey by crushing the honey-laden comb removed from the super frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;STRAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A strainer is an alternative to an extractor for removing honey from the comb taken from the super."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeepers use supers to provide additional space for bees to store honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-caeb5d2bd49a72e7116025708c05e9f6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPER&quot;" target="&quot;TOP BAR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The ends of the top bar rest in the rabbets of the supers to suspend the frame."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39baafb5b073ac43e9932248ea8ca932</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NECTAR FLOW&quot;" target="&quot;DANDELIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The appearance of blooming dandelions often signals the start of the first meaningful nectar flow of the season."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FALL MANAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WINTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Fall management is explicitly described as the process of preparation for winter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOSEMA DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Nosema disease is described as being widespread and serious within North America."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOSEMA DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;FUMAGILLIN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Fumagillin is the medication used to treat Nosema disease."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOSEMA DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both Nosema disease and tracheal mites have similar debilitating effects on colonies; their combined presence is devastating."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOSEMA DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;DYSENTERY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Nosema disease and dysentery are both listed as probable causes for similar symptoms of brown spotting/staining on frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27c4227735c6f952b192f6d769deb712</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites arrived in and became widespread across North America."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;ACARAPIS WOODII&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Acarapis woodii is the scientific name for the honey bee tracheal mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">24.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites have caused the loss of thousands of colonies in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracheal mites were found for the first time in the United States along the Mexican border in 1984."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracheal mites were imported or migrated into the United States between 1984 and 1997."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbe3628e117427ed1c35a791b026e9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;ENGLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites were first identified in England in 1921."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;MEXICO&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites that entered the US apparently came from sources in Mexico."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;MENTHOL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Menthol is used as a treatment to kill adult tracheal mites and control their winter buildup."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;MITICUR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Miticur is a contact miticide used to protect colonies by killing tracheal mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Miticur is used as a treatment for tracheal mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940d85de3b7092a6c76b3ef360a50ea0</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;K-WING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"K-wing is a specific symptom that suggests the presence of a tracheal mite infestation in the hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;RUBBING ALCOHOL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Rubbing alcohol is used to immerse bee samples for the diagnosis of mites, including tracheal mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are types of mites that infest honey bee hives and can be treated with the same medication (Miticur)."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-940d85de3b7092a6c76b3ef360a50ea0</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;CALIFORNIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"California embarked on a campaign to destroy outfits where tracheal mites were detected and closed borders to prevent their spread."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;FLORIDA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text mentions Florida beekeepers were aware of the spread of tracheal mites to other states like North Dakota."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;NORTH DAKOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites spread to North Dakota, leading California to close its borders to bees from that state."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;MILLER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Miller moved his operation to Idaho specifically to avoid tracheal mite infestation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites wreaked havoc on the interstate beekeeping industry and caused genuine panic in the mid-1980s."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dff8f6d16d91f6c080ca2e3b7cb50555</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;ROSS CONRAD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Ross Conrad addresses the issue of tracheal mites as a parasitic threat to honey bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4642364014d20a8527d9fb4ec06bdb04</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites are mentioned as a potential problem inherited when purchasing established bee colonies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0c85b379d83c9f869435c42e6568dee9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;ACARAPIS WOODI&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Acarapis woodi is the scientific name for Tracheal mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27c4227735c6f952b192f6d769deb712</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;HONEYBEE ACT OF 1922&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The discovery of tracheal mites spurred the creation of the Honeybee Act of 1922."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;MEXICAN BORDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites were first discovered in the US along the Mexican border."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;US BEEKEEPING INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The industry focused on breeding strains of bees resistant to tracheal mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;ROGER MORSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Roger Morse led efforts to breed bees resistant to tracheal mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA DESTRUCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The experience with tracheal mites is seen as a foreshadowing of what to expect from Varroa destructor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRACHEAL MITES&quot;" target="&quot;EUROPEAN HONEY BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tracheal mites are identified as pests of the European honey bee."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5fbe3628e117427ed1c35a791b026e9a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INSULATION BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The use of an insulation board is a specific technique in beekeeping for winter hive management."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INSULATION BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;FIBERGLASS-TYPE INSULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Fiberglass-type insulation is mentioned as an alternative material that beekeepers use in place of an insulation board."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INSULATION BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;TAR PAPER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wrapping with tar paper is described as a different method of hive insulation compared to using an insulation board."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FIBERGLASS-TYPE INSULATION&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Fiberglass-type insulation is used by some beekeepers to insulate the hive during winter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TAR PAPER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tar paper is used in the practice of wrapping hives, a method of insulation employed by beekeepers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-27f6271ed08f494278ee4aa9601556c4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUEEN EXCLUDERS&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Queen excluders are mentioned as a specific equipment/aspect of beekeeping that a practitioner must learn to use."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE BRUSH&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">19.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bee brush is described as a basic piece of beekeeping equipment."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE ESCAPE&quot;" target="&quot;ESCAPE BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both the bee escape and the escape board work on the same principle of providing a one-way door for bees to exit honey supers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-749c6fdbfff886885761e25892c820c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEE ESCAPE&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The bee escape is a tool used in beekeeping to remove bees from honey supers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-749c6fdbfff886885761e25892c820c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ESCAPE BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The escape board is a tool used in beekeeping to remove bees from honey supers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The escape board is used as a method to empty bees from a super in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-749c6fdbfff886885761e25892c820c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ESCAPE BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;PORTER BEE ESCAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The escape board works on the same principle as the Porter bee escape, allowing one-way passage for bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ESCAPE BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;BEE SUPPLY COMPANIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The escape board is listed as a tool for removing bees, and such specialized equipment is typically sourced from bee supply companies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-afb545522a163c5982461b497e852ea7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FUME BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The fume board is used to drive bees out of a super in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FUME BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;CARBOLIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Carbolic acid was commonly used with the fume board as the foul-smelling liquid to drive bees away."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FUME BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;MILLER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Miller uses a fume board while prying open a hive for harvest."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7acff18895bfa08e6388fc660689bad7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BLOWER&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A blower is used as an effective way to remove bees from supers in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LITTLE RED WAGON&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A little red wagon is suggested as a cart to hold spare supers during the beekeeping process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PORTER BEE ESCAPE&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Porter bee escape is used as a tool for emptying bees from supers in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-92090c6a7f40e420c9b8e4d961a9a21b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING EQUIPMENT SUPPLIERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Beekeeping equipment suppliers often have rental units of extractors available for beekeepers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNCAPPING KNIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"An uncapping knife is used to remove wax cappings from the comb before the honey can be extracted using an extractor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;STRAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The strainer is used to filter honey as it comes out of the extractor to remove wax and debris."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY GATE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Most extractors have a honey gate used to drain the reservoir where honey accumulates during extraction."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;TANGENTIAL EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A tangential extractor is a specific style of extractor where honey is spun from one side of the frame at a time."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;RADIAL EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A radial extractor is a specific style of extractor where honey is spun from both sides of the frames at once."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;BOTTLING TANK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey is moved from the extractor into the bottling tank after being strained and settled."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Extractors are tools used within the process of beekeeping to remove honey from frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;TBH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Some beekeepers are developing a specific extractor for TBH combs to preserve the comb for reuse through horizontal spinning."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5250b34c6030902898b14ec6202d48c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MESH BAG&quot;" target="&quot;STRAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A mesh bag can be used in conjunction with a strainer if the strainer's holes are too large."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-539e9876329b00dde77700328dfd38d1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STRAINER&quot;" target="&quot;MESH MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Mesh material is used in conjunction with a strainer to prevent wax particles and debris from remaining in the honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STRAINER&quot;" target="&quot;CAPPINGS CONTAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The cappings container should ideally have a strainer near the bottom for the cappings to rest on."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STRAINER&quot;" target="&quot;FILTER CLOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey may be strained through a filter cloth after an initial coarse straining to remove very fine particles."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNCAPPING KNIFE&quot;" target="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are manual tools used for uncapping, with the scratcher used for areas the knife cannot reach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The capping scratcher is used to break up cappings that the uncapping knife may have missed."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNCAPPING KNIFE&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRIC KNIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The electric knife is a more sophisticated version of an uncapping knife used for removing wax cappings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNCAPPING KNIFE&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIC PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The uncapping knife is an approved manual method for removing cappings in organic production since it does not require heat."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNCAPPING KNIFE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCAPPING MACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are tools used for the same purpose of removing wax cappings from honey frames."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A capping scratcher is used to remove drone brood to make Varroa mites on their bodies easily visible."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;" target="&quot;VARROA DESTRUCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A capping scratcher is used to remove drone pupae from cells to inspect for the presence of varroa mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2691225b766f240d4e630fa426b6e435</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;" target="&quot;HILDE WHALLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Hilde Whalley provided a photo demonstrating the use of a capping scratcher (uncapping fork) to check for varroa infestation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2691225b766f240d4e630fa426b6e435</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CAPPING SCRATCHER&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIC PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The capping scratcher is an approved manual method for removing cappings in organic production since it does not require heat."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3e5e906cf4b7199dbae90ca40e51e65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLASTIC PAILS&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY GATES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A plastic honey gate can be threaded into a plastic pail to create a bottling tank."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLASTIC PAILS&quot;" target="&quot;BOTTLING TANK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A bottling tank can be constructed using a 5- or 6-gallon plastic pail."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY GATES&quot;" target="&quot;BOTTLING TANK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A honey gate is the valve used in a bottling tank to control the flow of honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BOTTLING TANK&quot;" target="&quot;HONEY GATE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A honey gate is an essential component of a bottling tank, used to cut off the flow of honey sharply for bottling."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BOTTLING TANK&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bottling tanks are used in beekeeping to prepare honey for bottling by allowing bubbles to rise and be skimmed."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HONEY GATE&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Honey gates are used in beekeeping equipment to manage the flow of honey during processing."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TANGENTIAL EXTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;RADIAL EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"These are the two primary styles of extractors used in beekeeping, differing in how frames are positioned and spun."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc4c6eeeb090dac26dee2e9e9154d95f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRANULATION&quot;" target="&quot;DOUBLE BOILER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A double boiler is the recommended tool to reliquify honey that has undergone granulation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-da9216023ced68a9aa545d43ca1d419f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COMB HONEY&quot;" target="&quot;BEEKEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Comb honey is a product obtained through the practice of beekeeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Producing comb honey is a specialized operation within beekeeping, often discussed as an alternative or supplement to extracted honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b652e467f32b1db6fbb1cf5b9315586e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da9216023ced68a9aa545d43ca1d419f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COMB HONEY&quot;" target="&quot;WIRED FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wired foundation is used in the same super as comb honey frames to balance the production of extracted and comb honey."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-da9216023ced68a9aa545d43ca1d419f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
