    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;AUSTRALIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Varroa mite is found on every continent except Australia."&lt;SEP&gt;"There is a high risk and anticipation that varroa mites will eventually arrive on Australian shores."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001b3ca70f42e9cc2ce8671a72009988</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;AFRICAN BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The African bee (a race of A. mellifera) has a shorter development time, which allows fewer Varroa mites to mature."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;CAPE BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Cape bee (a race of A. mellifera) has a shorter development time, which allows fewer Varroa mites to mature."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;ETHER ROLL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The ether roll is a method used to detect the presence of Varroa mites on adult bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;SHAKING METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The shaking method is a technique used to remove and detect Varroa mites from adult bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;DRONE FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Drone foundation is used to concentrate drone brood in one place to aid in the detection of Varroa mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;BOTTOM BOARD INSERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bottom board inserts are used to collect Varroa mites that are killed or stunned by hive treatments."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
