      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Varroa mites carry the deformed wing virus into the bee hive."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-13d75b31628c95bce2d1de33c7d05683</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;ASIAN BEES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Asian bees developed grooming and hygienic behaviors to detect and expel varroa mites."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e9eafb5519ae847ebc95f1b6bd7a3901</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;EUROPEAN HONEY BEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The varroa mite has devastated European honey bee populations, making them almost entirely dependent on human domestication for survival."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e9eafb5519ae847ebc95f1b6bd7a3901</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
