    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;CALIFORNIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Standardized bees from California may be especially vulnerable to the varroa mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;FLORIDA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Standardized bees from Florida may be especially vulnerable to the varroa mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;CCD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are described as destructive scourges that threaten bee populations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;QUEEN-REARING INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The queen-rearing industry contributes to a lack of genetic diversity, making bees more susceptible to the varroa mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;PAT HEITKAM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pat Heitkam is a breeder whose impact on genetic diversity is less damaging than that of the varroa mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VARROA MITE&quot;" target="&quot;THE KOEHNENS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Koehnens are breeders whose impact on genetic diversity is less damaging than that of the varroa mite."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-880657fcead983c1ada31e3024872a79</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
