      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"If a top bar hive is supered too early without enough worker bees to patrol the space, it can lead to problems from wax moths."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84b0074137dce67380e1f3b23f86de2b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;RATIONAL GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">33.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Electric fences are mentioned as a tool used by farmers implementing rational grazing plans to reduce the work required for shifting fences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electric fences are mentioned as a tool used within rational grazing systems to divide pastures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electric fencing has aided the development of rational grazing by allowing for cheap and flexible division of paddocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text clarifies that rational grazing is a comprehensive system and does not result simply from the use of an electric fence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text warns against the misconception that simply shifting an electric fence thrice daily constitutes a greatly improved rational grazing system."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0bee7d5fac9dd017be636b45597ba373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7266683ce075bd299f9731e6b76917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5de83212539cb3933ac7783d0ed745be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b8b8502370c6624f8c498266b33fb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f09c1defaf6c7013ba4ecd1cac40b5a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;RATIONED GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Some claim that the electric fence is the primary tool used in rationed grazing compared to fixed fences in rotation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The electric fence is the tool used to implement the rationed grazing system by moving the stock and controlling access to grass portions."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-583d1c446eecee65cf5a758322efee03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-527055291c96f565ab1e262a61faefd9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;STRIP GRAZING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Strip grazing is a system intended to imitate tethering by shifting electric fences several times a day."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f35c3962af55711c0635829973feaae5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ROTATIONAL SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Electric fences are used in rotational systems to divide pastures into smaller sections and manage animal access to water."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f35c3962af55711c0635829973feaae5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;HOHENHEIM SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Hohenheim system's attempts to re-divide paddocks were greatly facilitated by the advent of the electric fence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The advent of the electric fence facilitated the re-division of paddocks to address failures experienced in the Hohenheim system."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c7501c88b4753d0e36195cd4c777c004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35c3962af55711c0635829973feaae5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;THE FARMERS WEEKLY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Farmers Weekly provides photographic evidence of rationed grazing using a single electric wire in front."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f35c3962af55711c0635829973feaae5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELECTRIC FENCE&quot;" target="&quot;FRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Trials in France utilized electric fences that were shifted forward twice daily for rationed grazing."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c7501c88b4753d0e36195cd4c777c004</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
