      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Dutch study is mentioned in the context of evaluating production systems and selecting indicators like mortality and air quality, which relates to the broader discussion of sustainability and functional integrity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c1c64b52d1680cf9b8c87710eaab068d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURAL ETHICS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text argues that integrating animal welfare into the conceptualization of sustainability is a task for agricultural ethics."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c1c64b52d1680cf9b8c87710eaab068d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;HUMAN RIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author suggests that basic human rights and well-being are first ethical priorities, and sustainability is then considered as a way to make a society satisfying those priorities more sustainable."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c1c64b52d1680cf9b8c87710eaab068d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;TARLA RAE PETERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Tarla Rae Peterson argues that sustainability has become a substitute for ideals of progress in the postmodern era."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fa6c175f37ce7089fa657f33595c666c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;EGYPTIAN SLAVE AGRICULTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text discusses Egyptian slave agricultures to argue that long-term endurance does not equate to true sustainability."</data>
