    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;AGRARIAN PHILOSOPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry is described as the most articulate advocate of agrarian philosophy in our own time."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-44b869f980d6664b6e8d9930d9e12a16</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;THE UNSETTLING OF AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Unsettling of America is a work written by Wendell Berry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wendell Berry expresses his interpretation of Jefferson's agrarian ideals in his work 'The Unsettling of America'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wendell Berry is the author of 'The Unsettling of America', where he confronts the claims of specialization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0b8e1c006d239029795854fde00ebba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc543c8a30e99c725b127846caddef9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b869f980d6664b6e8d9930d9e12a16</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;GREAT AGRARIAN GOAL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry is identified as the main contemporary advocate of the Great Agrarian Goal."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2b561afe8a3fd467795e6d58a0118448</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;AMERICAN TRANSCENDENTALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry's arguments regarding the Great Agrarian Goal have precedents in the philosophy of the American transcendentalists."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2b561afe8a3fd467795e6d58a0118448</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry's work serves as a clear critique of industrial agriculture and its negative impact on the farmer and family."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3330698527e14dc575dc6a2e0e2a7c9d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;THE TRANSCENDENTALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry used similar arguments to those made by the transcendentalists regarding the role of the independent family farm."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3330698527e14dc575dc6a2e0e2a7c9d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;BORGMANN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">13.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Borgmann's concept of deictic discourse is exemplified by Wendell Berry's writing on farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borgmann's early work cites Wendell Berry, and both are grouped together as thinkers urging a specific perspective on focal practices."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-81158f16b3cf87e12a53465738040b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;DAVID STRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Strong cites Berry's discussion of plow horses to illustrate the concept of focal things."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry's vision of family-based farming still exists in many parts of the United States."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;CANADA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry's vision of family-based farming still exists in many parts of Canada."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry emphasizes the seductive nature of industrial technology and how it offers relief from toil but detaches the farmer from the land."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;MODERN FARM TRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry laments the loss of contact with the land caused by farming behind the windshield of the modern farm tractor."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75d231af67d93bdb8bdb190752047b68</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry advocates for an agrarian ideal and a specific vision of farming and stewardship."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7ec816632b945dc5236be5a3d82d9ce6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;AGRARIANISM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry is a contemporary touchstone for the articulation of agriculture's moral value, which is central to agrarianism."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cd1c1d4f15102d0ce3bf4f9a157c71f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;THE SPIRIT OF THE SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Spirit of the Soil contains a discussion of Berry's work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Spirit of the Soil is a book by the author that discusses Wendell Berry's ideas."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bc543c8a30e99c725b127846caddef9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1c1d4f15102d0ce3bf4f9a157c71f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;THOMAS JEFFERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry provides an interpretation of Jefferson's views, linking farming to the protection of democratic liberty."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0b8e1c006d239029795854fde00ebba1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;MODERN AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Wendell Berry provides a critique of modern agriculture, specifically focusing on the negative impact of specialization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cd6cef65b73cbf090d0f46d890908a11</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;ALBERT BORGMANN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Berry's argument against specialization aligns with Albert Borgmann's view of the device paradigm regarding the loss of diverse skills."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cd6cef65b73cbf090d0f46d890908a11</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WENDELL BERRY&quot;" target="&quot;BIODYNAMIC FARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both Wendell Berry and biodynamic farming are cited as accessible resources for those interested in agrarian ideals and sustainable living."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e4e99eda5a55a138ef0183fda88c31a5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
