      <data key="d4">40.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Continuous grazing is presented as the ordinary system that contrasts with the structured approach of rational grazing/rotation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the amount of grass a cow harvests under rational grazing (maximum 100 lb) versus continuous grazing (88 lb)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the efficiency and productivity of cows under rational grazing versus continuous grazing, noting that rational grazing increases efficiency through better sward management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the two methods, stating that rational grazing triples the yield compared to continuous grazing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text compares the two, stating that rational grazing is superior in productivity compared to continuous grazing."</data>
