      <data key="d6">chunk-3a9d0dea50021742bc52cffc66eae1b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DESCARTES&quot;" target="&quot;MODERN PHYSICS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"John Dewey notes that Descartes' notion of space was essential to the development of modern physics."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a9d0dea50021742bc52cffc66eae1b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DESCARTES&quot;" target="&quot;GILBERT RYLE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Gilbert Ryle's concept of 'the ghost in the machine' is a critique of the dualistic model of mind and body established by Descartes."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a9d0dea50021742bc52cffc66eae1b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DESCARTES&quot;" target="&quot;JOHN DEWEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"John Dewey analyzed and critiqued Descartes' notion of space, viewing it as an abstraction compared to the concept of place."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a9d0dea50021742bc52cffc66eae1b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DESCARTES&quot;" target="&quot;THOMAS HOBBES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text suggests that Hobbes's notion of self-interest, when combined with Descartes' dualism, creates a pervasive feature of subjectivity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4be7aab5835b5557dffc1a1c85fd336d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DESCARTES&quot;" target="&quot;ECONOMIC THEORY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Descartes' dualism, alongside Hobbesian self-interest, informs the subjectivity that underpins economic theory."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4be7aab5835b5557dffc1a1c85fd336d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
