      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HERMAN DALY&quot;" target="&quot;FOR THE COMMON GOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Herman Daly is the co-author of the book 'For the Common Good'."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-21251d93da08e46a2457c1d8ac3cc530</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROBERT SOLOW&quot;" target="&quot;RESOURCES FOR THE FUTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Robert Solow delivered a lecture commemorating the fortieth anniversary of Resources for the Future."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ae29b94ecffe086781947e2fdbfad895</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROBERT SOLOW&quot;" target="&quot;BRUNDTLAND CRITERION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Solow's approach suggests that by reinvesting wealth in productive capability, the Brundtland criterion can be met."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ae29b94ecffe086781947e2fdbfad895</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROBERT SOLOW&quot;" target="&quot;SOLOW SUSTAINABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The general approach to sustainability developed by Robert Solow is referred to as Solow sustainability."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ae29b94ecffe086781947e2fdbfad895</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROBERT SOLOW&quot;" target="&quot;JULIAN SIMON&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned as thinkers whose work relates to sustainability and the potential for technology to compensate for declining resources."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b35bf5371164b92c6f94b6b1edaf6f2a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GORDON K. DOUGLASS&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURAL SUSTAINABILITY IN A CHANGING WORLD ORDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Douglass is the editor/organizer of the book titled 'Agricultural Sustainability in a Changing World Order'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gordon K. Douglass is the author of the collection of essays titled Agricultural Sustainability in a Changing World Order."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d2e7bd65679a478d0454882e6ccaa48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c852a940991461ca29b76becfe24a7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GORDON K. DOUGLASS&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURAL SUSTAINABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Gordon K. Douglass collected authors to write about agricultural sustainability in 1984."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-11c852a940991461ca29b76becfe24a7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHEMICAL FERTILIZERS&quot;" target="&quot;HUMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text argues that chemical fertilizers are ineffective or lead to disappointing crops if the soil lacks a supply of available humus."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c1fbfc96142fb2e1554de743e1067f65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DOUGLASS&quot;" target="&quot;WALTER GOLDSCHMIDT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Douglass's paradigm of social sustainability relies heavily on the research conducted by Walter Goldschmidt."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WALTER GOLDSCHMIDT&quot;" target="&quot;CALIFORNIA'S SAN JOAQUIN VALLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Goldschmidt studied two towns in California's San Joaquin Valley to analyze the impact of farm size on community infrastructure."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WALTER GOLDSCHMIDT&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Goldschmidt's study contrasted small family farms with large monoculture operations typical of industrial agriculture."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WALTER GOLDSCHMIDT&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIOLOGY OF AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Walter Goldschmidt conducted a landmark study that is central to the sociology of agriculture."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a488dc13c8287677db8f5b116ebb1a1b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA&quot;" target="&quot;MECHANICAL TOMATO HARVESTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The University of California was involved in the development of the mechanical tomato harvester, which led to a lawsuit."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA&quot;" target="&quot;GROWING DEGREE-DAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Information on GDD is available at the University of California's IPM website."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6c5f50eb1805931ea6eef1cf9700c46b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA&quot;" target="&quot;COLLEGE OF BIOLOGICAL SCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The College of Biological Science is a part of the University of California."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-33dbbf90fb02e64b31433c46153fb293</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MECHANICAL TOMATO HARVESTER&quot;" target="&quot;CALIFORNIA'S TOMATO INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The availability of the mechanical tomato harvester precipitated the rapid concentration and consolidation of California's tomato industry."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;OLIVER GOLDSMITH&quot;" target="&quot;ENCLOSURE METHODS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Oliver Goldsmith lamented the decline of rural villages following the adoption of enclosure methods in English farming."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-93cf1c2c8715fe3d60a2173d08025f78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRUNDTLAND&quot;" target="&quot;PEARCE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Brundtland commitment to future needs is contrasted with the development vector defined by Pearce, Barbier, and Markandya."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ddd79b341dfcb637bbc86f0265484513</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRUNDTLAND&quot;" target="&quot;BARBIER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Brundtland commitment to future needs is contrasted with the development vector defined by Pearce, Barbier, and Markandya."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ddd79b341dfcb637bbc86f0265484513</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRUNDTLAND&quot;" target="&quot;MARKANDYA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Brundtland commitment to future needs is contrasted with the development vector defined by Pearce, Barbier, and Markandya."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ddd79b341dfcb637bbc86f0265484513</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;BROMFIELD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both referenced soil and earth as a living system, though largely as a metaphor, and both were conservationists."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bennett's work lacked the disdain for chemical amendments found in Howard's writings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;BALFOUR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bennett's work lacked the disdain for chemical amendments found in Balfour's writings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;WASHINGTON&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bennett strategically timed his activities and testimonies in Washington to coincide with dust storms."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f8a0e526319f92312412e2845aee3568</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;SENATE PUBLIC LANDS COMMITTEE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bennett testified before the Senate Public Lands Committee to call for the saving of America's soil."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f8a0e526319f92312412e2845aee3568</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BENNETT&quot;" target="&quot;SOIL CONSERVATION SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bennett was appointed as the chief of the newly established Soil Conservation Service."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f8a0e526319f92312412e2845aee3568</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EARLY AUTUMN&quot;" target="&quot;PULITZER PRIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The book Early Autumn won the Pulitzer Prize in 1926."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-95f1a55e5dae098bc247517e22a19be3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard's views on soil health were seen as reminiscent of the 'life force' concepts that Liebig targeted in the nineteenth century."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;MCDONAGH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard relied on McDonagh's work, which contributed to the lack of acceptance of organic farming in scientific societies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH ORGANIC MOVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard's ideas regarding systemic and holistic health were the driving value in the British organic movement."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;J. I. RODALE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard's ideas were brought to the United States by J. I. Rodale."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-760ee66daea81221ff77e23a75a9dedd</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;STEINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both developed specific techniques for improving soil fertility and were associated with ideas rejected by the scientific establishment."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;BAILEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both advocated for an environmentally sound approach to farming and viewed soil as a living thing."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ECONOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard was fundamentally at odds with the industrial economy, which views humans and agriculture as analogues of industrial systems."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PHYSICS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard viewed biology as being 'poles asunder' from physics, criticizing the reductionist approach often associated with the latter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard formulated and advocated for the 'law of return,' where what is taken from the soil is returned to it to ensure sustainability."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;WHEEL OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard related the cycle of birth, growth, death, and decay in agriculture to the eastern religious concept of the Wheel of Life."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;MYCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard began his professional career as a specialist mycologist before moving toward a more integral approach to science."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-59f100ffb03d2213b475479279d60e37</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;INDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard conducted his research on scientific aerobic compost in India during the 1920s and 1930s due to the availability of cheap labor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Howard took up land in India and learned agriculture from the local people and peasant farmers there."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-145b265b8d53df8f70babd69fc84ec3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ROTHAMSTED&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard received preliminary training from professors at Rothamsted."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;GABRIELLE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Gabrielle was Howard's first wife, and they worked together to solve the problem of indigo wilt."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard dedicated his life and work to studying and practicing agriculture through an integrated, holistic approach."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard's realizations about ecological and economic sustainability preceded the failures of industrial agriculture by half a century."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;J. P. J. VAN VUREN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"J. P. J. Van Vuren studied the results obtained by Howard regarding the conversion of urban wastes."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-79a1a0cb0810e8c4db52132d6d4c6596</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ACTINOMYCETES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Howard is cited as stating that soil microbes like actinomycetes will look for non-artificial nutrition."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f41a230435631a03248889184c93b965</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;STEINER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Steiner's intellectual circle rejected the biological views held by Liebig."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb65f1a45d35048b00a53d3e4f8fe7fe</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH FARMING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig's essay in 1843 influenced British farming by drawing attention to the importance of fertilizers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b117c84af6b43cb698d268784eb7234e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH ASSOCIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig contributed his work 'Chemistry in Its Application to Agriculture' to the British Association in 1840."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75cc73a73aa1db4b46b480931b5836ef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;HUMUS THEORY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig vigorously combated the humus theory, disproving its premises regarding dead matter."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-75cc73a73aa1db4b46b480931b5836ef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;ARTIFICIAL FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Artificial fertilizers were born out of the abuse of Liebig's discoveries regarding the chemical properties of the soil, and Liebig himself manufactured artificial manures."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f54ae758c012dc186d43caf6a059360a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;LABORATORY HERMIT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The laboratory hermit represents a divorce between theory and practice that would have been deprecated by Liebig."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f54ae758c012dc186d43caf6a059360a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;CHINESE AND JAPANESE AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig pointed to Chinese and Japanese agriculture as examples of success due to their practice of returning waste to the land."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;BAVARIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig described the Bavarian experience with poudrette, a fertilizer made from night soil."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;RADSTADT FORTRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig related how troops at the Radstadt fortress used a system to collect excrement for use as fertilizer in surrounding fields."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;PARLIAMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Parliament invited Liebig to visit England to advise on returning town sewage to farmers' fields."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;ENGLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig visited England at the invitation of Parliament to provide advice on sewage utilization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;GREAT STINK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Great Stink in London spurred the government action that led to Liebig's invitation to advise on sewage."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;RIVER THAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig's visit was prompted by the pollution of the River Thames, which caused the Great Stink."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LIEBIG&quot;" target="&quot;CLASSICAL GREECE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liebig's ideas on returning nutrients to the land had precedents extending back to Classical Greece."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fc063bcbb000e43f7427394a529bddaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
