      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text suggests avoiding chemically laden products derived from petroleum in favor of foods grown with biodynamic methods."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ba112c4310be31fc99e92db5c7bc7f59</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;PERMACULTURE METHODS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text suggests avoiding chemically laden products derived from petroleum in favor of foods grown with permaculture methods."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ba112c4310be31fc99e92db5c7bc7f59</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;COAL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text describes a chronological energy progression where the coal boom preceded and set the stage for the petroleum boom."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-da2ed8a27091d9b374270e513324aa63</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSCONTINENTAL RAILROAD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The railroad boom followed the coal boom and preceded the petroleum boom."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-da2ed8a27091d9b374270e513324aa63</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;ECONOMIC APARTHEID&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The availability of cheap energy (petroleum) broke down community boundaries and led to a stratified society described as economic apartheid."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-da2ed8a27091d9b374270e513324aa63</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;COTTAGE INDUSTRIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">4.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author contrasts the 'petroleum blip' (cheap energy anomaly) with a return to participatory energy and the patronage of local cottage industries."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f7cdcda2273c4d3e807e607b85d38791</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;MECHANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Mechanization and petroleum combined to provide the machines and cheap energy necessary to revolutionize tillage and fertilizer production."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b3fdd7b941341283d68dce92a52c682d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;CHEMICAL FERTILIZER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Petroleum provides the cheap energy required to manufacture chemical fertilizers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b3fdd7b941341283d68dce92a52c682d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PETROLEUM&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author argues that industrial agriculture (grain-fed beef/dairy) only works because petroleum is cheap."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cc84578a2a9965cca7bdee803ba8f735</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
