    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FRANÇOIS HUBER&quot;" target="&quot;FRANÇOIS BURNENS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"François Burnens was a devoted servant who helped the scientist François Huber carry out experiments on bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"François Burnens was the sighted servant who helped the blind scientist François Huber conduct research on bees."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FRANÇOIS HUBER&quot;" target="&quot;LEAF HIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"François Huber designed a 'leaf hive' in 1789, which was the first hive allowing observation of the interior without destroying the colony."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FRANÇOIS HUBER&quot;" target="&quot;ANTON JANSCHA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Anton Janscha published the same findings on queen fertilization fifteen years before Huber, though he went unnoticed."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dce07dbfe1cb37dbe56f8651f3f0f484</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LEAF HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;EDWARD BEVAN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Edward Bevan's 1827 text described a hive design related to the evolution of leaf and top-bar designs."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LEAF HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;JOHANN DZIERZON&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Johann Dzierzon's hive design, like Huber's and Bevan's, was an improvement over traditional skeps and gums."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LEAF HIVE&quot;" target="&quot;GUMS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The leaf hive was a vast improvement over the traditional gums used in beekeeping."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c29c8fc62f2aad355ff0f1407fba86a8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
