      <data key="d6">chunk-d16c2413dd929af8532f1ba9572924a1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHOLESALE PRODUCE BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;USDA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The USDA provides the grading and packaging standards used by the wholesale produce business, which chefs use as a benchmark for buying decisions."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f4f5056e367e595ba49ac25860afe112</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIGH-VOLUME RESTAURANTS&quot;" target="&quot;WHOLESALER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"High-volume restaurants often buy from wholesalers, and small growers must price their produce competitively against wholesaler prices to win these customers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f07d4af13c3a63576ce7c8e559179</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIGH-VOLUME RESTAURANTS&quot;" target="&quot;SEED CATALOGS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Growers bring seed catalogs to meetings with restaurant chefs to discuss and plan potential crop varieties to grow for them."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f07d4af13c3a63576ce7c8e559179</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIGH-VOLUME RESTAURANTS&quot;" target="&quot;AVAILABILITY SHEET&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Growers use availability sheets to communicate their current produce offerings to restaurants via fax or email to solicit orders."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f07d4af13c3a63576ce7c8e559179</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHOLESALER&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRIBUTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A distributor typically adds a markup (approximately 20 percent) to the wholesale prices."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f07d4af13c3a63576ce7c8e559179</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERMARKETS&quot;" target="&quot;ON-FARM STANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Supermarkets are contrasted with on-farm stands, which allow farmers to obtain higher prices through direct-to-consumer sales."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2dd1671b8f35843a0cf41f9b37012e5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERMARKETS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSCRIPTION PROGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Supermarkets are contrasted with subscription programs, which typically offer better pricing for the farmer than wholesale supermarket deals."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2dd1671b8f35843a0cf41f9b37012e5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERMARKETS&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD AGRICULTURAL PRACTICES (GAPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Supermarkets increasingly require third-party GAPs certification from their suppliers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2dd1671b8f35843a0cf41f9b37012e5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERMARKETS&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFIED-ORGANIC PRODUCE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The prices of certified-organic produce are compared to supermarket prices to determine competitiveness and value."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-69367273cfc9c0877f276be544f8188d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERMARKETS&quot;" target="&quot;ENTERPRISE BUDGETS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Enterprise budgets help growers determine costs of production, which informs how they price their goods relative to the 'loss leader' pricing strategies used by supermarkets."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-69367273cfc9c0877f276be544f8188d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ON-FARM STANDS&quot;" target="&quot;NATURAL FOODS STORES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The expansion of natural foods stores potentially affects the customer base of growers selling at farm stands."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2dd1671b8f35843a0cf41f9b37012e5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUBSCRIPTION PROGRAMS&quot;" target="&quot;NATURAL FOODS STORES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The proliferation of natural foods stores may impact small growers who utilize subscription programs."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2dd1671b8f35843a0cf41f9b37012e5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
