      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The method of charging pits used by van Vuren follows the guidelines set out in An Agricultural Testament."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5e1e151c82b3fc06c79b833667c8828b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AN AGRICULTURAL TESTAMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DR. REID&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Dr. Reid worked to make the ideas in 'An Agricultural Testament' known to the planting community."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5332439349dbc980b17ca1f0c9044b2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AN AGRICULTURAL TESTAMENT&quot;" target="&quot;J. M. MOUBRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"J. M. Moubray previously wrote notes for the publication 'An Agricultural Testament' in 1939."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c1fbfc96142fb2e1554de743e1067f65</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE SOIL AND HEALTH&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sir Albert Howard wrote and published the book The Soil and Health in 1947."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1932cb031e5713bde84668b6254f5c5d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE SOIL AND HEALTH&quot;" target="&quot;INDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The book was a product of Howard's years of work as a government scientist in India."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1932cb031e5713bde84668b6254f5c5d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ORGANIC MOVEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The organic movement is the manifestation of Sir Albert Howard's thought and agricultural philosophy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1932cb031e5713bde84668b6254f5c5d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ORGANIC MOVEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTIONAL MASS-MARKET BUSINESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The organic movement began as an alternative to conventional business; conventional businesses now seek to profit from organic success or exploit regulatory confusion."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-00846d8ceb93399d6fd4ec6dd83fac36</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ECONOMY&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sir Albert Howard's premise that the economy should be an analogue of the organic world put him fundamentally at odds with the industrial economy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1932cb031e5713bde84668b6254f5c5d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;NATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Law of Return is the phrase used to sum up the intricate arrangements of Nature's farming, specifically the processes of destruction and storage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The law of return is the mechanism by which humans fulfill their duty to restore the natural cycle and maintain the earth's reserves."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2b6f8bdb7d910bab994c57a8e47dd2c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550966fca0f2f090187553fe9bc99e80</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;MOTHER EARTH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Law of Return is described as the great principle underlying Nature's (Mother Earth's) farming."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18b8ee2e72fa6f47d60cc453b7711fdc</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;HOMO SAPIENS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Homo sapiens have flouted the Law of Return in favor of cheaper methods of transferring humus reserves for profit."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-18b8ee2e72fa6f47d60cc453b7711fdc</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The duties of the agriculturist to the land are summed up in the law of return, emphasizing the need to maintain soil reserves."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-550966fca0f2f090187553fe9bc99e80</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sir Albert Howard is the individual who first proposed the Law of Return regarding the role of soil organic matter in fertility."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85f843ce4c9e414f5a474793768109cf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAW OF RETURN&quot;" target="&quot;SYNTHETIC FERTILIZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Law of Return emphasizes the biological basis of soil organic matter, contrasting with the use of synthetic fertilizers which can degrade long-term soil health."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85f843ce4c9e414f5a474793768109cf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHEEL OF LIFE&quot;" target="&quot;NATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Nature's farming processes, specifically the balanced manufacture and use of humus, are described as the even turning of the Wheel of Life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nature's stability is secured by the even balancing of the Wheel of Life, which consists of the cycle of birth, growth, death, and decay."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Wheel of Life represents the continuous natural cycle of growth and decay governed by Nature."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-aff6fbf3f5ff09df476cd44ec19e3d67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b6f8bdb7d910bab994c57a8e47dd2c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550966fca0f2f090187553fe9bc99e80</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHEEL OF LIFE&quot;" target="&quot;ZOOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Zoology is criticized for focusing only on living things and ignoring the death and decay phase of the Wheel of Life."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-aff6fbf3f5ff09df476cd44ec19e3d67</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHEEL OF LIFE&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Agriculture's interventions are seen as moments that stop the Wheel of Life, which must then be set spinning again through restoration."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-550966fca0f2f090187553fe9bc99e80</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GABRIELLE&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Gabrielle worked with Howard to solve agricultural problems, specifically the indigo wilt."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IMPERIAL ENTOMOLOGIST&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Imperial Entomologist was tasked with finding an insect cause for the indigo wilt plague in an agricultural context."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IMPERIAL MYCOLOGIST&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Imperial Mycologist was tasked with finding a fungus cause for the indigo wilt plague in an agricultural context."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IMPERIAL BACTERIOLOGIST&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Imperial Bacteriologist was tasked with finding a virus cause for the indigo wilt plague in an agricultural context."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROMAN EMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The agricultural history of the Roman Empire is cited as a failure due to the conflict between soil fertility/population needs and capitalist operations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROMAN EMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The failure of the Roman Empire's agriculture is presented as a historical parallel to the failures of industrial agriculture."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f10e286b0ce488adcc83133b6ebb3a9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROMAN EMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;DIRT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Roman Empire is cited as a civilization that sank into poverty and demise after destroying its topsoil."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cf82877961e08200011936c26d80e1bb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROMAN EMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;THE PLOW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Roman Empire developed the iron plow, which served as the forerunner to the modern plow."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-df17faa8ab3183c29a4b66fae2714601</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LOUISE E. HOWARD&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Louise E. Howard wrote about Sir Albert Howard in the book 'Sir Albert Howard in India'."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c28ab0744bd2c8644bdc99e6c30ae80a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DR. LIONEL J. PICTON&quot;" target="&quot;SIR ALBERT HOWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sir Albert Howard acknowledges Dr. Lionel J. Picton for recording evidence of organic farming in the News-Letter on Compost."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f01a9018938914804f49a80182b2f205</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
