      <data key="d5">"Latex paints are used to paint supers to help bees identify their colony and protect the wood."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-58530be97ce8bec48257c2ee46f928b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUPERS&quot;" target="&quot;OIL-BASED PAINT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Oil-based paint is discouraged for painting supers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-58530be97ce8bec48257c2ee46f928b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LINSEED OIL&quot;" target="&quot;TURPENTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Linseed oil can be mixed with natural turpentine to help it dry faster and soak deeper into the wood of bee equipment."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-58530be97ce8bec48257c2ee46f928b4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROGER MORSE&quot;" target="&quot;WILLIAM COGGSHALL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Roger Morse and William Coggshall co-authored the seminal book titled 'Beeswax'."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0bfa52bca196a2a92c24daffb2347956</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROGER MORSE&quot;" target="&quot;US BEEKEEPING INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Roger Morse led the US beekeeping industry's efforts in the late 80s and early 90s."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c5e37349454eb3591b4615887c1807b8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AMERICAN FOULBROOD DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;BEE TEA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"If honey is added to bee tea, the honey source must be free from American foulbrood disease."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d23e81de581a25fd88f0445b106d4f9f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STYROFOAM&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Styrofoam is a foamed or expanded form of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0bfa52bca196a2a92c24daffb2347956</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STYROFOAM&quot;" target="&quot;TEXAS-SIZED ISLAND OF PLASTIC FLOTSAM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Styrofoam and other non-biodegradable plastics contribute to the formation of the Texas-sized island of plastic flotsam in the ocean."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7743420fb913bc6919678a336fad7bdb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STYROFOAM&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Styrofoam is a form of polystyrene foam; both are discussed as materials used in beekeeping and food packaging."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7743420fb913bc6919678a336fad7bdb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;" target="&quot;GREEN PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both polystyrene and green plastics break down into smaller pieces in the environment without fully biodegrading."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0bfa52bca196a2a92c24daffb2347956</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;POLYSTYRENE FOAM&quot;" target="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ORGANIZATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Environmental organizations prioritize restricting the use of foamed polystyrene take-out food packaging."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7743420fb913bc6919678a336fad7bdb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLASTIC FOUNDATION&quot;" target="&quot;WOODEN SUPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Plastic components are compared to natural wood counterparts in terms of cost and bee preference."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7743420fb913bc6919678a336fad7bdb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHRIS HARP&quot;" target="&quot;NEW YORK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
