    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GM CORN&quot;" target="&quot;BRANDT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Brandt is experimenting with GM corn to see if the higher seed cost and associated herbicide use are necessary for productivity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eea73e36d5dc1a7d6617766c0a980521</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GM CORN&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIC CORN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"These two types of corn are being compared by Brandt in side-by-side strips to evaluate cost versus productivity."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eea73e36d5dc1a7d6617766c0a980521</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GM CORN&quot;" target="&quot;ROUNDUP&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text associates the use of GM corn with a higher reliance on herbicides like Roundup."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eea73e36d5dc1a7d6617766c0a980521</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GMO&quot;" target="&quot;GENETICALLY MODIFIED (GM) CROPS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"GMO is the abbreviation for genetically modified organisms, and the text describes GM crops as incorporating genes from different species."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d8e8d4cc911657d6fdf8ff1c7e34b598</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
