    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE STAMETS \&quot;P\&quot; VALUE SYSTEM&quot;" target="&quot;AGAR MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Stamets 'P' Value System is used to categorize mushroom mycelium types, some of which are observed as volunteer primordia on nutrified agar media."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-43a1ef2ff91f86f93c8d85ce6a2b3161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is prepared using autoclavable spawn bags, requiring sterilization via an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-43a1ef2ff91f86f93c8d85ce6a2b3161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SAWDUST SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The creation and sterilization of sawdust substrates for spawn involve the use of a retort or autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-43a1ef2ff91f86f93c8d85ce6a2b3161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SAWDUST/BRAN BAGS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The autoclave is used to sterilize bags of supplemented sawdust."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;STERILIZATION INDICATOR STRIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sterilization indicator strips are placed throughout bags inside the autoclave to outline a profile of sterilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sterilization indicator strips are placed within the mass of bags inside an autoclave to verify the profile of sterilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sterilization indicator strips are used in the autoclave to confirm that sterilization has actually occurred."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7465ed3b02e2efa8c7b1c2c113bd9f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUID MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liquid media are sterilized using pressure and heat (typically 15 psi) in an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MALT EXTRACT AGARS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Malt extract agars require a recommended sterilization time of 40 minutes at 15 psi in an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;POTATO DEXTROSE AGARS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Potato dextrose agars require a recommended sterilization time of 40 minutes at 15 psi in an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SOIL EXTRACTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Soil extracts must be subjected to a minimum of 2 hours of sterilization in an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0844446be98c91a11acfc07bb4139aa8</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;DR. STOLLER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Dr. Stoller invented a specialized collar/lid system for bags that are subsequently sterilized in an autoclave."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3f7c54ea888763f1d03f685097757427</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;PRESSURE COOKER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">22.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A pressure cooker is used as a separate autoclave for towels, water, and other equipment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both are listed as equivalent pressure vessels used to sterilize sawdust bags for 2 to 3 hours at 15 psi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pressure cookers are mentioned as smaller vessels used for sterilizing substrates, contrasting with larger autoclaves used for higher volumes."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7c54ea888763f1d03f685097757427</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;LAMINAR FLOW HOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bags are removed from the autoclave and placed in the windstream of a laminar flow hood to cool."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laminar flow hoods (and walls) are used to rapidly cool sterilized mass coming from an autoclave prior to inoculation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7c54ea888763f1d03f685097757427</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;RED ALDER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Substrates containing red alder are loaded into the autoclave for sterilization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-71d4b92006db2e1bfffb89c800fc0a3d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;RICE BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Substrates containing rice bran are loaded into the autoclave for sterilization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-71d4b92006db2e1bfffb89c800fc0a3d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;HOSPITAL AUTOCLAVES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Hospital autoclaves are a specific type of autoclave, though often deemed unsuitable for commercial mushroom growers due to size and pressure ratings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;CANNING INDUSTRIES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The text identifies vessels developed for canning industries as the most cost-effective autoclaves for spawn producers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;RETORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Retorts are the common name for the cost-effective autoclaves developed for the canning industries."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MUSHROOM CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The autoclave is described as the centerpiece of the production process in mushroom culture, essential for sterilizing substrates."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-74e08f9019a6721b44f903e073f95b43</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MUSHROOM MYCELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Oversterilization in the autoclave can render the substrate inhospitable to mushroom mycelium."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7465ed3b02e2efa8c7b1c2c113bd9f9d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;BOYLE'S LAW&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Boyle's Law explains the arithmetic relationship between temperature and pressure within the autoclave once thermal inertia is overcome."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7465ed3b02e2efa8c7b1c2c113bd9f9d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MICROPOROUS FILTER CANISTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A microporous filter canister can be attached to the autoclave's pressure/vacuum gauge pipe to ensure air entering the autoclave is contaminant-free."&lt;SEP&gt;"A microporous filter canister is connected to the autoclave to allow pressure equalization without introducing contaminants."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7465ed3b02e2efa8c7b1c2c113bd9f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;CLEAN-ROOM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Autoclaves are typically opened into the clean-room air to prevent contamination upon reaching atmospheric pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The autoclave is designed to be opened into clean-room air or uses a filter canister located on the clean-room side to prevent contamination."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7465ed3b02e2efa8c7b1c2c113bd9f9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;STEAM BOX&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned as devices used for sterilization that may or may not have a tight seal to form a vacuum."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;LAMINAR FLOW WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Laminar flow walls are used to provide a sterile environment for substrate that has just been autoclaved."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7a3fb337bf89926a26a3b13ae25b3cc4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SHIITAKE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Autoclaves are used to sterilize the sawdust substrates used for growing Shiitake."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91456f98a926e6abc80385dc245cc777</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;THE LAB&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The autoclave is used in the lab for sterilization, and the lab must be cleaned after it is emptied."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91456f98a926e6abc80385dc245cc777</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;GANODERMA LUCIDUM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"An autoclave is used to sterilize spawn plastic bags used in the cultivation of Ganoderma lucidum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cultivators may use an autoclave to short-cycle sterilize Ganoderma lucidum mushrooms to prevent insect larvae."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5222544fbac611153c3910b7a49b1632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a03386c8fdad1c49ade13815bc6b2f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;DXN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The autoclave is part of the cultivation process used by production crews like DXN for Reishi."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5222544fbac611153c3910b7a49b1632</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLEMENTED SAWDUST CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Checking autoclave seals is a solution for contamination occurring during the cooldown of supplemented sawdust cultures."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a99b3c5799adf4153f31a635e31e46c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AUTOCLAVE&quot;" target="&quot;HEPA FILTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned as tools or components used to maintain sterile technique and prevent contamination in mushroom cultivation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2b55e55c8fb7ad2fc82b21eddc75408b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;SINDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Sinden revolutionized spawn technology in 1933 by discovering grain as a spawn carrier medium."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a15c712ab4cd262f392a9cd9ec6621d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;WOOD-BASED SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are commercial forms of spawn, with wood-based spawn being preferred over grain spawn for outdoor, unpasteurized substrates."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a15c712ab4cd262f392a9cd9ec6621d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;MUSHROOM CULTIVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn serves as a carrier medium used in the process of mushroom cultivation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a15c712ab4cd262f392a9cd9ec6621d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;NUTRIFIED AGAR MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Mycelium grown on nutrified agar media is used to inoculate and produce grain spawn."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-69e12830990f7ea8d716253d971a2d83</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;SAWDUST SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">19.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is used to inoculate the substrate to produce sawdust spawn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sawdust spawn is created from grain spawn."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-69e12830990f7ea8d716253d971a2d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d8ffd59b496178c8be531ac64f1a01</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUID-INOCULUM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Liquid-inoculum is used as a precursor to generate grain spawn in the cultivation process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee67735ee2d22fc01623c11e43940a78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is the recommended inoculation method for growing Oyster mushrooms on straw to improve yields."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee67735ee2d22fc01623c11e43940a78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;PLUG SPAWN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is the starting point used to create plug spawn via sterilized sawdust."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ee67735ee2d22fc01623c11e43940a78</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOM&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is preferred over sawdust spawn for the cultivation of Oyster mushrooms on cereal straws to improve yields."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;VOLVARIELLA VOLVACEA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"As a tropical species, Volvariella volvacea may die if its spawn is exposed to cold storage temperatures."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pleurotus ostreatus is a cold-weather Oyster strain that can be shocked into fruiting when spawn is placed in a cold room."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;HEPA FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A HEPA filter is suggested for installation in refrigeration rooms to prevent contamination of stored spawn."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;AGARICUS INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Agaricus industry widely utilizes cold storage for spawn to manage overproduction and inventory."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e449960bc2a0309e5e78859fdb6bcdef</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;SAWDUST SPAWN BAGS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is inoculated into sawdust spawn bags to initiate the growth process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2c8c8ff82911884af1d7f6dd1d5a5310</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;LABORATORY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is incubated in jars and stored in racks within the laboratory."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a4d8ffd59b496178c8be531ac64f1a01</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;PETRI DISH CULTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is developed downstream from the petri dish cultures."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a4d8ffd59b496178c8be531ac64f1a01</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;PHASE II&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Grain spawn is fed or broadcast onto the straw as it is off-loaded from the Phase II box."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;ARCHIMEDES SCREWS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Archimedes screws are used as a means to mix grain spawn into the pasteurized straw to ensure even colonization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GRAIN SPAWN&quot;" target="&quot;MICRON FILTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Installing micron filters is a solution to prevent airborne contamination of grain spawn."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a99b3c5799adf4153f31a635e31e46c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
