      <data key="d4">30.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned as mushrooms that give rise to faster fruitings on alder and cottonwood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both demonstrate strong photosensitivity, requiring light for proper primordia development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both species are listed as types of mushrooms where sawdust-to-sawdust transfers are common."&lt;SEP&gt;"Expired Shiitake substrate can be resterilized for the sequential cultivation of Reishi mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cultivation of polypores like Reishi can follow tracks similar to the cultivation of Shiitake."</data>
