    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;PLEUROTUS EUOSMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pleurotus euosmus is described as being closely related to, and potentially a variety of, Pleurotus ostreatus."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ec72301cd65d24bcaa0b9ddc0bf03d77</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;P. EUOSMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"P. euosmus is closely related to P. ostreatus, resembling it in biology, appearance, and cultivation, and is a possible future synonym."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3e7dec6ab9d7f3f4eda38f7bb986ce91</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;P. PULMONARIUS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"P. ostreatus is so similar to P. pulmonarius that strains of the two are often mislabeled as one another."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3e7dec6ab9d7f3f4eda38f7bb986ce91</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;SALVATORE TERRACINA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Salvatore Terracina, a farmer, collected a massive P. ostreatus specimen in Sicily."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3e7dec6ab9d7f3f4eda38f7bb986ce91</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;EGER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Eger (1980) provided evidence regarding the sensitivity of P. ostreatus to light levels."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8d01f4ab0b6edb6aedfd23fcfda61b39</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS OSTREATUS&quot;" target="&quot;THORN&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Thorn and Barron (1984) noted that P. ostreatus exudes a metabolite toxic to nematodes."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8d01f4ab0b6edb6aedfd23fcfda61b39</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
