    <edge source="&quot;MYCOSPHERE&quot;" target="&quot;INITIATION STRATEGY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The careful management of the mycosphere through environmental stimuli is collectively referred to as the initiation strategy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-168cc3fa8dca26838fa71068b19dc0e4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INITIATION STRATEGY&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The initiation strategy is the process used to trigger the formation of mushrooms, including Oyster mushrooms, via environmental shifts."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1634ffc0bb5eabb2ca88a56400372467</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INITIATION STRATEGY&quot;" target="&quot;PRIMORDIA FORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Primordia formation is explicitly defined as the initiation strategy, involving shifts in moisture, air exchange, temperature, and light."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1634ffc0bb5eabb2ca88a56400372467</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BADHAM&quot;" target="&quot;PSILOCYBE CUBENSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Badham conducted a study in 1985 focusing on species such as Psilocybe cubensis to determine factors affecting cap orientation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-168cc3fa8dca26838fa71068b19dc0e4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
