      <data key="d6">chunk-91456f98a926e6abc80385dc245cc777</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BADHAM&quot;" target="&quot;SUPER-PASTEURIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Badham (1988) is cited as a source for information regarding substrates, which includes the context of super-pasteurized sawdust."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6595de7e08679e25db37588321f5c89</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PSILOCYBE CUBENSIS&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Money (1998) studied the force of spore ejection from basidia, which are the spore-producing cells found in mushrooms like Psilocybe cubensis."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-168cc3fa8dca26838fa71068b19dc0e4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KARYOGAMY&quot;" target="&quot;MEIOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Karyogamy is the process where nuclei fuse to form a diploid nucleus, which is immediately followed by meiosis (reduction division)."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-168cc3fa8dca26838fa71068b19dc0e4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KARYOGAMY&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Money studied the final stage of the basidia process (spore ejection) that follows the biological stages of karyogamy and meiosis."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-168cc3fa8dca26838fa71068b19dc0e4</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MEIOSIS&quot;" target="&quot;MITOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are processes of nuclear division within cells, contrasted here as reduction division (meiosis) versus nonsexual replication (mitosis)."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7293fc01c557821f6218df5f9fa300ad</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STROPHARIA&quot;" target="&quot;BASIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
