    <edge source="&quot;BASIDIA&quot;" target="&quot;PLEUROCYSTIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pleurocystidia project beyond the surface plane of basidia to keep gills from contacting one another."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CYSTIDIA&quot;" target="&quot;CHEILOCYSTIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Cheilocystidia are a specific type of cystidia located on the edge of the gills."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CYSTIDIA&quot;" target="&quot;PLEUROCYSTIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pleurocystidia are a specific type of cystidia located on the interior surface of the gills."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS CYSTIDIOSUS&quot;" target="&quot;CONIDIOPHORES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Pleurotus cystidiosus and its allies utilize asexual life cycles where spores can be produced on conidiophores."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS CYSTIDIOSUS&quot;" target="&quot;OIDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Oidia are listed as an example of asexual reproduction, and Pleurotus cystidiosus is cited as an excellent example of a mushroom with such alternative cycles."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS CYSTIDIOSUS&quot;" target="&quot;CHLAMYDOSPORES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Chlamydospores are listed as an example of asexual reproduction, and Pleurotus cystidiosus is cited as an excellent example of a mushroom with such alternative cycles."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PLEUROTUS CYSTIDIOSUS&quot;" target="&quot;COREMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Coremia are listed as an example of asexual reproduction, and Pleurotus cystidiosus is cited as an excellent example of a mushroom with such alternative cycles."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e200ba0bf931b71bc51f4a652dcb336</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
