      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Leon-Chocoo reported high biological efficiency yields of Oyster mushrooms grown on coffee pulp."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-25db8095ea0b0d4b55ab42331903d3f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COFFEE PLANTATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOM FARMS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Coffee plantations and Oyster mushroom farms are described as complementary industries, with coffee pulp serving as an ideal substrate."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-25db8095ea0b0d4b55ab42331903d3f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PASTEURIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;HOT WATER BATH METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The hot water bath is presented as a simple and easy method for pasteurizing straw."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-25db8095ea0b0d4b55ab42331903d3f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PASTEURIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;STEAM PASTEURIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Steam pasteurization is identified as a second method for pasteurizing straw."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-25db8095ea0b0d4b55ab42331903d3f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STEAM PASTEURIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The 'Phase II' Chamber is the specific equipment/setup used for steam pasteurization."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-25db8095ea0b0d4b55ab42331903d3f3</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;SHIPPING CONTAINERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Many growers convert shipping containers into Phase II chambers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;GATE VALVE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Phase II chamber features a floor drain fitted with a gate valve to prevent contamination."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;BOILERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Boilers provide the live steam that is dispersed into the straw within the Phase II chamber."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH-PRESSURE BLOWERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"High-pressure blowers are used to enhance heat penetration within the Phase II chamber."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPERATURE PROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Temperature probes are inserted at various locations in the Phase II chamber to monitor the pasteurization profile."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II CHAMBER&quot;" target="&quot;CONVEYORS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"After pasteurization in the chamber, the steamed mass is thrown onto conveyors for further processing."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-db332f84616a8c651529c78841e8e9d9</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHASE II&quot;" target="&quot;BLEACH BOMBING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Bleach bombing is the industry term for the intensive cleaning of the inoculation area associated with the Phase II process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE HYDRATED LIME BATH METHOD&quot;" target="&quot;HYDRATED LIME&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Hydrated Lime Bath Method utilizes hydrated lime to create a highly alkaline environment that inactivates competitor fungi and bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;THE HYDRATED LIME BATH METHOD&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOM MYCELIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Oyster mushroom mycelia are noted for their ability to tolerate the alkaline environment created by the Hydrated Lime Bath Method better than competitors."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HYDRATED LIME&quot;" target="&quot;OYSTER MUSHROOM MYCELIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The alkaline pH resulting from hydrated lime is tolerated by oyster mushroom mycelia during the colonization process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cbc4a286310a7bafa84441b67de3d71e</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
