    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAND PRESERVATION GROUPS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSERVATION EASEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Land preservation groups utilize conservation easements as instruments to try and ameliorate farm succession and land loss issues."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAND PRESERVATION GROUPS&quot;" target="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The narrator argues that land preservation groups should focus their efforts on eliminating inheritance taxes rather than relying on easements."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAND PRESERVATION GROUPS&quot;" target="&quot;AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author argues that land preservation groups in America often ignore the successional issues of farming and can be overly restrictive with private land."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LAND PRESERVATION GROUPS&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Land preservation groups are urged to focus on solving the impediments to profitable farm businesses (agriculture)."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-32dccbe80c5a2907ae81c8b0b4b49792</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FERRIS WHEEL SPROUTER&quot;" target="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The narrator's desire to build a Ferris wheel sprouter is hindered by the time and creative energy spent trying to escape the inheritance tax policy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROTARY CYLINDRICAL RABBITMOBILE&quot;" target="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The development of the rotary cylindrical rabbitmobile is presented as a productive alternative that is sidelined by the need to deal with inheritance tax."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VERMICOMPOSTING&quot;" target="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The narrator views vermicomposting as a way to heal the land, which is prioritized lower than the legal struggle against the inheritance tax policy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MOLDERING TOILET&quot;" target="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The creation of a moldering toilet is another innovation the narrator would pursue if not burdened by the government's inheritance tax policy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INHERITANCE TAX POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;CONSERVATION EASEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Both are discussed as mechanisms affecting the preservation of farmland, with the narrator contrasting the efficacy of easements against the burden of the tax policy."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-326af0d2f4f5cb2e60b5f3dc889133d2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GREENIES&quot;" target="&quot;CALIFORNIA&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In California, 'greenies' pushed through legislation that prevented a young couple from building a second home on their own family ranch."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INVESTMENT PORTFOLIO&quot;" target="&quot;LAND USE PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The author uses the concept of an investment portfolio as an analogy to highlight the unfairness of external control exerted by land use planning."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FARMLAND PRESERVATIONISTS&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURAL ZONE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Farmland preservationists set rules within agricultural zones that decree houses and farmland do not go together, limiting development."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FARMLAND PRESERVATIONISTS&quot;" target="&quot;LAND USE PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Farmland preservationists utilize land use planning to stop random development, though the author suggests this often leads to arbitrary and unfair results."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a5ec62399679b6e30a34af778780d6d6</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
